{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01STUpKA53Y5Bz4iaYb1PvWy","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-i\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\n....\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n780:- `map.floorMat` †: a material (E.MATERIALS id or '#hex pattern') for every floor cell\n796:- `E.MATERIALS: brick, stone, rock, plank, timber, plaster, hedge, speckle, plain, tiles, slab, leaves, grass, flagstone, ... (61)`: the materials by id: { color, pattern, ...its numbers, ramp, glow } or a painter of a surface (face, roof, floor, tile); add your own: E.MATERIALS.oak = { color: '\n797:- `E.PATTERNS`: the patterns, by name: (s, m) => a tone step (-1 .. +2) at a point s of a surface, for a material m's numbers. Add your own: E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0\n798:- `E.PATTERNS.bark(s)` †: fissures running up a trunk; a cut end shows its rings\n799:- `E.PATTERNS.bricks(s, m)` †: running bond, bw x bh (6 x 3), mortar a step darker (mortar: its step)\n800:- `E.PATTERNS.cloth(s, m)` †: a fine weave and soft folds (fold .9)\n801:- `E.PATTERNS.crate(s, m)` †: a framed and braced crate side (frame 2 wide, a diagonal brace, boards bw 3 inside); lids are planks\n802:- `E.PATTERNS.foliage(s, m)` †: leaf clumps (size 3.5), each lit at its top and dark at its foot, a few bright leaves\n803:- `E.PATTERNS.glaze(s)` †: a glossy shine where the light is strongest, a few specks\n804:- `E.PATTERNS.metal(s, m)` †: hard light (a shine where lit, darker in shade); rivet: a rivet every rivet units\n805:- `E.PATTERNS.noise(s, m)` †: soft patches (scale 4)\n806:- `E.PATTERNS.none()` †: the light's bands alone\n807:- `E.PATTERNS.planks(s, m)` †: boards bw wide (3) with joints and butt ends every len (14); along u on lids and flat sides, along v (staves) on turned surfaces; dir: 'v' turns them on flat faces\n808:- `E.PATTERNS.shingles(s, m)` †: staggered rows of roof tiles (course 2.5, bw 4)\n809:- `E.PATTERNS.speck(s, m)` †: dark and light specks (amount .08)\n810:- `E.PATTERNS.stones(s, m)` †: irregular stones (Voronoi cells about size across, 5) with dark joints and a lit rim\n811:- `E.PATTERNS.thatch(s, m)` †: straw in overlapping courses (course 3)\n812:- `E.PATTERNS.tiles(s, m)` †: square tiles size (4) with grout\n813:- `E.material(id, local, kind = 'material', depth = 0)`: a material ready to draw: { q (its entry), ramp (five [r, g, b], dark to light), hexes (the same as '#rrggbb'), pat (its pattern), glow }. id: an id (looked up in local first, a set's own, then E.MATERIALS), a shorthand string or an entry;\n1096:- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turne\n1101:- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and b\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"943e74c0-5066-4011-b89a-f41c97d93843","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:59:41.033Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-i\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\n....\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n780:- `map.floorMat` †: a material (E.MATERIALS id or '#hex pattern') for every floor cell\n796:- `E.MATERIALS: brick, stone, rock, plank, timber, plaster, hedge, speckle, plain, tiles, slab, leaves, grass, flagstone, ... (61)`: the materials by id: { color, pattern, ...its numbers, ramp, glow } or a painter of a surface (face, roof, floor, tile); add your own: E.MATERIALS.oak = { color: '\n797:- `E.PATTERNS`: the patterns, by name: (s, m) => a tone step (-1 .. +2) at a point s of a surface, for a material m's numbers. Add your own: E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0\n798:- `E.PATTERNS.bark(s)` †: fissures running up a trunk; a cut end shows its rings\n799:- `E.PATTERNS.bricks(s, m)` †: running bond, bw x bh (6 x 3), mortar a step darker (mortar: its step)\n800:- `E.PATTERNS.cloth(s, m)` †: a fine weave and soft folds (fold .9)\n801:- `E.PATTERNS.crate(s, m)` †: a framed and braced crate side (frame 2 wide, a diagonal brace, boards bw 3 inside); lids are planks\n802:- `E.PATTERNS.foliage(s, m)` †: leaf clumps (size 3.5), each lit at its top and dark at its foot, a few bright leaves\n803:- `E.PATTERNS.glaze(s)` †: a glossy shine where the light is strongest, a few specks\n804:- `E.PATTERNS.metal(s, m)` †: hard light (a shine where lit, darker in shade); rivet: a rivet every rivet units\n805:- `E.PATTERNS.noise(s, m)` †: soft patches (scale 4)\n806:- `E.PATTERNS.none()` †: the light's bands alone\n807:- `E.PATTERNS.planks(s, m)` †: boards bw wide (3) with joints and butt ends every len (14); along u on lids and flat sides, along v (staves) on turned surfaces; dir: 'v' turns them on flat faces\n808:- `E.PATTERNS.shingles(s, m)` †: staggered rows of roof tiles (course 2.5, bw 4)\n809:- `E.PATTERNS.speck(s, m)` †: dark and light specks (amount .08)\n810:- `E.PATTERNS.stones(s, m)` †: irregular stones (Voronoi cells about size across, 5) with dark joints and a lit rim\n811:- `E.PATTERNS.thatch(s, m)` †: straw in overlapping courses (course 3)\n812:- `E.PATTERNS.tiles(s, m)` †: square tiles size (4) with grout\n813:- `E.material(id, local, kind = 'material', depth = 0)`: a material ready to draw: { q (its entry), ramp (five [r, g, b], dark to light), hexes (the same as '#rrggbb'), pat (its pattern), glow }. id: an id (looked up in local first, a set's own, then E.MATERIALS), a shorthand string or an entry;\n1096:- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turne\n1101:- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and b","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01STUpKA53Y5Bz4iaYb1PvWy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
