{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HzfpPJsqGYVLtU7qnUZSb1","type":"tool_result","content":"785:    this._pinching = false; this._zoomAcc = 1; this._zoomNow = 1; this._zoomOn = false; this._wheelOn = false; this._fingers = new Map();\n815:    el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {\n816:      if (!this._wheelOn) return; e.preventDefault();\n817:      const d = e.deltaY * (e.deltaMode === 1 ? 33 : e.deltaMode === 2 ? 100 : 1);\n2888:    I._zoomOn = zr; I._wheelOn = zr && (this._camera() || {}).wheel !== false;\n10149:    wheel: 'deltaX deltaY deltaMode clientX clientY mods', mouse: 'button buttons clientX clientY detail mods', value: 'value checked',\n10151:  const KIND = { keydown: 'key', keyup: 'key', pointerdown: 'pointer', pointermove: 'pointer', pointerup: 'pointer', pointercancel: 'pointer', wheel: 'wheel',\n10217:    : kind === 'wheel' ? [e.deltaX, e.deltaY, e.deltaMode, e.clientX, e.clientY, mods(e)]\n10256:    const PERSON = ['key', 'pointer', 'wheel', 'mouse', 'value', 'capture'];\n10307:    else if (kind === 'wheel') t.dispatchEvent(new WheelEvent(type, Object.assign(base, { deltaX: a[0], deltaY: a[1], deltaMode: a[2], clientX: a[3], clientY: a[4] }, mm(a[5]))));\n...\n276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n277:- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n279:- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse'\n280:- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n281:- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stic\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕',\n284:- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n286:- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n288:- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }\n290:- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'),\n293:- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n294:- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and \n295:- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n298:- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n300:- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n302:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF').\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those th\n304:- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n305:- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n306:- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n307:- `input.resetBindings()` †: forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n309:- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n310:- `input.sequence(steps, o = {})` †: true on the step a sequence of inputs ends, each one after the last within window seconds (.5) of the first: input.sequence(['down', 'down+right', 'right', 'at\n311:- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n312:- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n313:- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n315:- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n316:- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it \n317:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size\n318:- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing fo\n319:- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over i\n321:- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. T\n322:- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n323:- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n324:- `input.clock = 0`: seconds of input time (the steps' dt added up)\n325:- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n327:- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n328:- `input.keysTo = null` †: the other players' inputs the keyboard's codes go to as well (players sharing it, each with half its keys: game.players)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n330:- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n331:- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bin\n333:- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n335:- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n336:- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n337:- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n338:- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n339:- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n340:- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n342:- `input.screen`: the game's screen (mouse positions are read through it)\n343:- `input.steer = 'stick'` †: 'stick' (a stick drawn under the thumb) or 'drag' (a finger anywhere on the screen but the buttons steers by drag(), with no stick drawn: a shooter's ship that follows\n344:- `input.stick = [0, 0]` †: the touch stick's direction [x, y], length <= 1\n345:- `input.stickDeadzone = .12` †: the part of that radius a thumb moves before the stick counts (0..0.5)\n346:- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n347:- `input.stickOn = false` †: a finger is on it\n348:- `input.stickRadius = 44` †: how far (CSS pixels) a finger drags for full tilt\n349:- `input.stickSide = 'left'` †: 'left' or 'right', the half of the screen the stick lives on\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n351:- `input.zones = null` †: areas of the screen a finger holds an action down in, [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }] (fractions of the canvas, 0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball'\n530:- `game.input`: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"be64a9b1-2aba-499a-85aa-c3c38e56be5a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:59:56.119Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"785:    t