 unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a collider\\\\n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (distinct), pixels, bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1], rgba }; null for an unknown shape\\\\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shape draws; null for an unknown shape\\\\n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\\\\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three corners a triangle; uv two a corner, world units across the surface)\\\\n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\\\\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\\\\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, lon\\\\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or\\\\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\\\\n321:- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\\\\n322:- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\\\\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\\\\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0\\\\n505:- `game.start({ camera })`: a scene's { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5, wheel: true }: the player zooms the camera within zoom (the wheel, - and =, a pinch, Settings, Camera zoom: theirs, kept, on top of the game's; false or none: they can't; a functi\\\\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, on top of \\\\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone'\\\\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\\\\n1089:- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydr\\\\n1253:- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01XtHhWaLikuee824mssfe9K\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"3181a7bc-6e9a-4c37-a94e-4bcdf12c2300\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":200,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":150,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"81dc681c-29c3-4ef4-89c8-33673ec6801f\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":400,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":200,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"c9856db9-a3ae-42a1-929a-22fccd77d666\\\"}\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":575,\"oldLines\":3,\"newStart\":575,\"newLines\":4,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":8850,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":100,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"638dd5a0-b9da-4e96-bad6-49ad3ffbb268\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":8950,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":100,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"36809697-4942-4ae3-893d-eb81af3c7806\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":9050,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":100,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"332a5f93-db2b-4f7a-8539-dac89c8538c7\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":9200,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":150,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"8a79626b-09c7-4c09-b325-907c35d6af13\\\"}\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":0,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01CFyyiH5J7kPUExiJHF5z53\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941\",\"uuid\":\"a73cbfa7-db83-49b8-b0d4-1695598d7d9b\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":543,"oldLines":3,"newStart":543,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":12400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944\",\"uuid\":\"d55656ee-1998-4f89-9bcb-9b97e2660cdf\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":12500,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944\",\"uuid\":\"0beec9ab-a820-440c-a5bf-554851ded6d9\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":12600,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944\",\"uuid\":\"d765e92e-e9a6-4902-ad91-870c8353cd8d\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":12750,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944\",\"uuid\":\"652b43ce-9111-414b-8d34-6d9533eb73d1\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HzfpPJsqGYVLtU7qnUZSb1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
