{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ArZBGdfNjRzVzKNg3n7ZML","type":"tool_result","content":"867 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"1f70cc8c-7364-4cb8-92a0-3afb647a1da3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:03.717Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"867 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":116,"oldLines":3,"newStart":116,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1050,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"7665c97a-d0bd-441f-b032-160c861dc666\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"7a004fcc-487d-4604-a6d0-677b98538f7e\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"8742c760-a597-4a59-a207-b5c235194fd5\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1750,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"35a2e23b-f03d-4e43-896c-e30b75360d68\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2000,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"f950bad1-0dd8-408b-81f0-dc51105d306f\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2038,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2038,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"f40db06c-a6d1-45f1-a66c-bd19165a7298\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"c4018018-1736-4757-a0d9-3ce1c99ac555\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"d6988484-765c-4773-8490-88985f6cc7a0\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"9312d9f9-9d77-4bdc-a631-43df5d43c071\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":500,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"729289e8-b8a1-4216-9557-54b1e49d8172\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":490,"oldLines":3,"newStart":490,"newLines":378,"lines":["   - **Building:** placing the right block into a ghost cell counts it, with a sparkle and a short arpeggio. Objects in ghost cells (door, lanterns) count the same way.","   - **Helpers:** residents with the `helper` job (Professor, Wren, and Mortimer by day) take the needed materials from the Town Chest. Each walks to an unbuilt ghost cell they can reach and places a block with a hammer animation and a \"tok\". Rate: `tuning.helperRate` blocks/min each (default 6). If the chest lacks materials, they say so in a balloon (\"Need Planks!\") and idle.","   - **Completion:** when every cell matches, a celebration cutscene plays (§7.10) and the reward and Cheer are granted. The structure counts as a special room (\"Quilters' Hall\") if its rules match (§7.6).","+","+### 6.10 Residents (`DQ.Residents`)","+- Each resident is a `VoxelBody` plus a `Humanoid` or `Blob` rig, with a profile from `DQ.NPCS` (§7.8): `job`, `schedule`, `needs`, `voice`, `fighter` stats, and dialog nodes.","+- **Schedule** (hours of the day clock; each block picks a target):","+","+  | Time | Activity |","+  |---|---|","+  | 06–08 | Wake, stretch (`wave` pose), go to the plaza |","+  | 08–18 | Job: see below; between tasks, wander inside the border |","+  | 18–20 | Supper: sit at a Mess Hall stool if one exists and eat (+bubble) |","+  | 20–21 | Socialise near the Banner (talk balloons `note`, `dots`) |","+  | 21–06 | Sleep in a free bed in a Bedroom (+bubble at 06:00); without one, sleep on the ground beside the Banner (mood −1, a \"No bed...\" balloon) |","+- **Jobs:**","+  - **Wren** (gatherer): each morning she puts 3 random basics (straw, branch, cotton) into the Town Chest. In sieges she uses a slingshot (4 damage, range 6 blocks, 1.2 s).","+  - **Mortimer** (guard): patrols the border at night with a lantern and fights monsters inside the border with a club (8 damage, `overhead`). In sieges he leads the defence. He needs a Guard Post to stand watch from (+bubble).","+  - **Marigold** (cook): with a Kitchen, cooks at the Hearth Pot (stirring loop) twice a day from Town Chest ingredients into the chest. At 18:00 she sets a dish on the Mess Hall table. In sieges she throws hot pies (5 damage, arc).","+  - **Professor Selvage** (helper): builds Patterns from the Town Chest at the helper rate, or reads in the Workshop. In sieges he hides in the Hall.","+  - **Lintwick** (fluff-farmer): puts 2 Lint into the Town Chest daily and dances (a Blob hop loop) when happy. In sieges he rolls into monsters (3 damage + knockback).","+- **Needs and Cheer bubbles.** At most once per day per need, each satisfied need spawns a floating pink heart bubble (+5 Cheer) over the resident, which stays until collected:","+  - sleep: slept in a bed","+  - meal: ate a dish","+  - comfort: their favourite room exists (Wren: Bedroom, Mortimer: Guard Post, Marigold: Kitchen, Professor: Workshop, Lintwick: a Bedroom with a Felt block in its walls)","+","+  Collect a bubble by walking within 2 blocks of it. Unhappy residents show a `dots` balloon and say why when you talk to them.","+- **Requests:** a resident with an available quest shows a bouncing \"!\" balloon (`story.emote`). Talking starts it, and its steps appear in the Journal and HUD. When the steps are done, a \"?\" balloon shows; talk to them to turn it in.","+- **Arrival cutscene:** the resident walks in along the east road, the camera pans to them, and they say their intro line. \"Mortimer has moved into Thimbleton!\" shows with a jingle.","+- **Navigation** (`DQ.Nav`):","+  - **Graph:** nodes are standable `(x, y, L)`. Edges:","+    - 8-neighbour moves (diagonals only if both orthogonal neighbours are open), cost 1 (diagonal 1.41)","+    - step up 1 level (a hop), cost 2","+    - drop down 1–3 levels, cost 1.5","+    - doors open for residents, closed for monsters","+  - **A\\*** with a binary heap, capped at 3,000 expanded nodes. Smooth paths by line-of-walk. Re-path when an edit touches a path cell.","+  - **Stuck rule:** if a resident has not progressed for 8 s and is off-screen, teleport them to the target. On screen, try a hop, then re-path.","+- **Talk:** dialog with a portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) and the resident's voice. Lines vary by flags, time of day, mood and town level (`E.Story` nodes with `if` conditions).","+","+### 6.11 Monsters and combat (`DQ.Monsters`, `DQ.Combat`)","+- **AI states:** `idle/wander → notice` (a \"!\" over the head plus a squeak, 0.3 s) `→ chase → windup` (telegraph: flash, crouch or squash, a sound) `→ attack → recover`. Then `→ flee` (below 20% HP for Lintlings) or `→ hurt` (stagger 0.25 s) `→ dead` (pop, particles, drops, `monsterKilled`).","+  - Aggro uses radius `tuning.aggro`, scaled by type (§7.9), plus `world.raycast` sight from eye height.","+  - Leash: return home after chasing 24 blocks away from home.","+- **Spawning:**","+  - Region tables (§7.1) by day or night. Spawn on standable cells under open sky, ≥ 10 blocks from the builder, outside the town border, never inside rooms or during cutscenes.","+  - Rate: 1 spawn per `tuning.spawnEvery` s (day 8, night 5) while the active count is below `tuning.maxMonsters` (default 10).","+  - Despawn: more than 40 blocks away for 20 s.","+- **Damage:**","+  - `dmg = max(1, round((atk − def/2) × U(0.9, 1.1)))`, where U is drawn from the combat stream.","+  - Builder crits: 5%, ×1.5 (Spin Stitch never crits).","+  - Multipliers: `tuning.monsterHp`, `tuning.monsterDmg`, `tuning.builderAtk`, and difficulty (Relaxed 0.5 damage taken, Normal 1, Hard 1.4).","+- **Hit feedback:**","+  - `game.hitFx(x,y,z,{ power, damage, angle })` (hit-stop, shake, impact star, damage number), plus `E.knockback(builder, mon, 120, 40)`.","+  - Monster hits on the builder: knockback 90, i-frames 0.8 s, a red vignette flash under `game.flash` limits.","+  - Each move has its own sound.","+- **Drops:** rolled on death from the drop table (`tuning.dropRate` multiplier on chances); items fly out.","+","+### 6.12 Siege and bosses (`DQ.Siege`, `DQ.Bosses`)","+- **Siege director** (used once in the story, M13–M14, and in the Bee round). It is a `game.script` generator:","+  1. **Prep.** Mortimer's rally line, then a 90 s countdown banner (\"The Knotted army approaches! 1:30\"). Build defences meanwhile; the music turns tense with the drum layer.","+  2. **Autosave checkpoint** `siege`.","+  3. **Waves** W1 → W2 → W3 (§7.9). Each wave spawns over 10 s from the east road (96,76), the Rift (96,80) and the north path (72,52). It ends when all of its monsters are defeated. Between waves: a 25 s breather with \"Wave cleared!\" and a repair prompt.","+  4. **Boss.** Gnarlgrim enters through the Rift (cutscene, §7.10).","+- **Monster targets in sieges:** first the Banner (HP 300; its HP bar is on the HUD during the siege), then ballistas, then the nearest town-structure block in the way (flagged `town` when placed inside the border), then residents, then the builder.","+  - Monsters path with **breaker A\\***: wall blocks count as passable at cost 8 per block, and doors at cost 4.","+  - On reaching a blocking block or door, a monster attacks it (Lintling 3, Pinhog 6, Frayed Knight 8, Knotbrute 25, Gnarlgrim 60 block damage per hit).","+- **Fail:** the Banner falls, or the builder is KO'd while Gnarlgrim is active. Then \"The Banner has fallen...\" / \"You've come undone...\", and a choice: \"Try again from the start of the siege\" (reload the checkpoint) or \"Return to title\". Waves already cleared stay cleared only within a single attempt.","+- **Sir Buttonsworth** (mini-boss, Button Quarry floor):","+  - Intro: he rises from a heap of buttons.","+  - Moves:","+    - **Slam:** wind .6 s; a shockwave ring of radius 3 blocks expands over .5 s. Jump to avoid it; it deals 12.","+    - **Button Volley:** wind .4 s; 5 buttons in a 50° spread (`E.Bullets`, 110 u/s, 8 damage).","+    - **Stomp Charge:** wind .7 s; charges 140 u/s toward the builder, breaks blocks in its path, and is dizzy for 2 s after hitting a wall. Dizzy takes double damage.","+  - Below 50% HP he summons 3 Lintlings once.","+  - The arena has 4 cobble pillars that break under charges.","+  - Defeat: he pops into buttons and drops the Golden Needle and 3 Steel Thread.","+- **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** (final boss, in and around the Thimbleton plaza), HP 600 in three phases (100–66%, 66–33%, 33–0%):","+  - **Tightly wound.** Def 25, so normal hits do about 1 damage. Mortimer and Granny hint \"Use the Ballistas!\" after 3 such hits.","+  - **Tangled.** 2 manned-ballista hits within 8 s, or 1 hit during his charge, make him Tangled for 5 s: he sits in a heap with `down: .6`, his chest **Heart Knot** glows, and his def drops to 0.","+    - Hits on the Heart Knot (front arc) with the Seam Ripper do ×4, other weapons ×2.","+    - A stagger plays at 100 damage per Tangle; leaving the Tangle triggers a roar knockback.","+  - **Phase 1:** Yarn Slam (ring, radius 3.5) and Tangle Toss (lobbed yarn ball via `E.arc`, landing in 1.1 s on a shadow telegraph; 10 damage and leaves a temporary Tangle block for 20 s).","+  - **Phase 2:** adds Charge (breaks blocks in its path and targets a ballista) and summons 4 Lintlings at the phase start.","+  - **Phase 3:** all moves 25% faster, a double Tangle Toss, and a Knotbrute summon.","+  - Phase transitions: a roar (`shout` expression) and a knockback ring; the music switches to the next layer.","+  - Defeat cutscene: he unravels into heaps of yarn (thread particles) and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner. The rift heals (§7.10).","+","+### 6.13 Day, night, lighting, weather (`DQ.Clock`)","+- One day = `tuning.dayMinutes` (12) real minutes; the story starts on Day 1 at 08:00.","+- **Phases:** dawn 05–07, day 07–17, dusk 17–19, night 19–05.","+- `game.lights.enabled = true` always. `ambient` follows the hour: night .30 with a cool blue tint, dawn and dusk .65 with a warm tint, day 1.0. Use `lights.tint`, setting `lights.dark` per phase, then `lights.refresh()`.","+- Light sources add light pools (§6.7). At night, stars twinkle in the void, Mothlets spawn and Frayed Knights roam the Rift.","+- **HUD clock:** a sun/moon dial with \"Day 3\".","+- **Weather (cosmetic, engine `game.weather`):** the Fraying always has `ash` (purple tint). The Glen rains lightly some days (Day 2 afternoon, Day 4 morning). Weather resets per region when it changes.","+- **Sleeping** is in §6.7. **Night-time Granny line:** the first night she warns \"Monsters get bolder after dark, dearie. A lit room is a safe room!\"","+","+### 6.14 Health and hunger","+- The HUD shows HP as a red patch bar with numbers (\"HP 32/40\") and Belly as a bread-loaf bar.","+- Low HP (< 25%) adds a heartbeat sfx and a red vignette (follows the reduce-flash setting).","+- Food is in §7.3. Eating restores Belly and HP; raw Thimbleberries restore Belly +5.","+- Starving: HP −1 every 4 s, with the prompt \"Your belly is empty! Eat something!\"","+","+### 6.15 Story, quests, dialog, cutscenes (`DQ.Quests`, `DQ.Cutscenes`)","+- **Engine pieces:** `E.Story` (story module) runs conversations as data nodes, with `who`, `say`, `choices`, `set`, `quest`, `done`, `emote` and `event`. One `E.Dialog` instance is skinned as a Dragon Quest-style box: a dark indigo panel with a cream stitched border (dashed 1-px line 2 px inside the edge), a name tab, a portrait at the left, typed text with Animalese blips, and a ▼ bobbing at page end.","+- **Granny Gossamer's box:** a golden stitched border with gold text and a glowing spool portrait (a custom portrait function).","+- **Text:** 3 lines per page, at most 52 characters per line, `E.font` scale 1 (≈ 31 px tall on a 1080p TV).","+- **Quest data** (§7.10): `{ id, title, giver, steps: [{ text, done: condition }], reward, next, unlock }`. Conditions are data:","+  - `{ have: {item: n} }`, `{ crafted: id }`, `{ placed: objId }`, `{ room: type }`, `{ level: n }`, `{ talk: npc }`","+  - `{ killed: {monster: n} }`, `{ at: poi, radius }`, `{ pattern: id }`, `{ flag: k }`, `{ siegeDone: true }`, `{ boss: id }`","+- **Quest director:** evaluates the current steps on relevant events (cheap) and once per second as a fallback. It advances steps and emits `questStep`/`questDone`. Rewards: `{ cheer, items, notions, flags, heartpatch }`. HUD: \"Quest complete: Wren's Bed\" with a jingle.","+- **Objective tracker** (top centre, collapsible with a long press of Create or the N key): the quest title, the current step text, and a marker. The marker is the engine's `r.marker(x,y,z,{label})`, which becomes an edge arrow off screen, with the distance in blocks. Targets: the POI, NPC or Pattern from the step, or for gather steps the nearest matching plant or block within 40 blocks (scanned once per second).","+- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens on a proxy, dialog awaits (`yield E.until(() => !talk.open)`), NPC walks (autopilot), and effects.","+  - Skip: hold ○, Esc or right click for 1 s (a fill ring shows) to jump to the end state.","+  - Every cutscene has `apply()`, which sets its end state. Skipping and tests call it.","+- **Writing style** (Dragon Quest-like):","+  - Short, punchy lines; exclamations; earnest heroism softened with jokes; sewing puns; NPCs with verbal tics.","+  - The silent Builder answers only through choices (\"Of course!\" / \"What's a bed?\").","+  - System lines are cheerful: \"You got 3 Straw!\", \"Thimbleton is now Level 2!\", \"A Lintling bounces into view!\"","+  - Avoid modern slang. Keep it family-friendly. Never reuse Dragon Quest names, places or iconic phrases verbatim.","+","+### 6.16 UI screens and HUD (10-foot, controller first; `DQ.Hud`, `DQ.Menus`)","+All UI is pixel art drawn with `E.ui`, `E.font` and `px` inside `r.overlay`. Panels are dark felt (`E.ui.box` gradient `#2a2350 → #1a1636`) with stitched cream borders. Text is at least scale 1 at 240p; headers scale 2; the title logo scale 3–4. At most about 6–8 entries per screen and generous spacing: no dense tables. Information is never conveyed by colour alone (icons plus text).","+","+- **HUD (in play):**","+  - Top left: HP bar, Belly bar, and the equipped weapon icon.","+  - Top centre: the objective tracker.","+  - Top right, *below* `game.cornerArea()`: the clock dial with the day, and the Banner badge (level, Cheer bar).","+  - Bottom centre: the hotbar. 8 slots of 22×22 px; the selected slot is raised and outlined, with its name and count above. L1/R1 or wheel glyphs sit at the ends.","+  - Bottom left: context prompts.","+  - Bottom right: pickup toasts.","+  - Centre: Notion, Room, Level and Quest popups (queued, 2.5 s each).","+  - Siege: the Banner HP bar and the wave label. Boss: a big HP bar with the name, phase pips and a \"TANGLED!\" flash.","+  - **Fades:** the HUD fades to 30% when idle for 6 s outside combat. Hold ○ for HUD-less screenshots? No: keep it simple and leave this out.","+- **Title:**","+  - Behind the menu, a living diorama: the finished Thimbleton built from the attract stamp, at dusk, with a slow camera orbit. The logo reads \"DRAGON QUILT BUILDERS\", each letter a patchwork fabric colour with a stitched outline and extrusion (`E.font.title`), and a needle-and-thread dragon emblem.","+  - Menu (`E.Menu`, centred bottom): Continue (if a save exists), New Game, Load Game (`saves.show('load')`), Quilting Bee (solo challenge), Settings (`game.menu('settings')`), About & Credits.","+  - \"Press ✕ / Enter\" prompt; a version label (`E.versionLabel()`).","+  - After 10 s without input, the attract mode starts.","+- **New Game:** name entry (letter grid plus keyboard typing), look A/B, 4 palettes, difficulty (Relaxed/Normal/Hard). The live rig preview turns.","+- **Intro crawl:** 4 pages over the quilt void with Granny's voice and gentle music. Skippable.","+- **Satchel** (Create / Tab / M / N), with tabs switched by L1/R1 or Q/E:","+  - **Bag:** a category strip (Materials, Building, Furniture, Food, Tools, Key) and a 6×4 grid of large slots. Detail pane: icon at ×3, name, a Dragon Quest-style description, the count. Actions: ✕ Assign to hotbar, △ Use/Eat/Equip, □ Drop 1/All. The \"Pocket Notions\" button opens pocket crafting.","+  - **Map:** described below.","+  - **Journal:** active quests (giver portrait, steps with ✓), completed ones, and the list of known Notions.","+- **Map screen:**","+  - The world drawn top-down at 2 px per column from top-block base colours, shaded by height. Water is blue satin; void is navy with stitched edges; unexplored areas are blank linen (fog revealed within 10 blocks as you go).","+  - Markers: you (an arrow), the Banner, residents, discovered portals, quest targets, the Lost Bundle.","+  - Controls: the stick pans, R2/L2 zoom, ✕ sets a waypoint marker, ○ goes back. Mouse: drag to pan, wheel to zoom, click to set a waypoint.","+- **Crafting, Chest, Travel and Banner screens:** §6.5–6.9.","+- **Pause menu:** the engine standard, plus Satchel, Dev Tools (hidden in hub sessions) and About & Credits. Save/Load come through `menu: { saves }` (enabled when `saves.canSave`: no monsters within 12 blocks, no siege or cutscene).","+- **Results** (chapter clear): the Builder's name and a portrait card. Stats: play time, blocks placed, blocks broken, items crafted, rooms built, monsters defeated, Cheer earned. Then \"Continue to credits\".","+- **Credits:** a scroll over the finale party, ending on \"To be continued... Chapter Two: The Calico Coast\" (a story teaser, not a stub) and \"Thank you for playing!\". Then back to free play in Thimbleton (`credits.onDone → play`), with all systems active.","+- **About & Credits** (title menu and pause menu): pages for Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback and Licenses (§6.24).","+","+### 6.17 Audio (`DQ.AudioX`)","+- **Music** (all original, in the engine's step sequencer format; §7.11 lists every song):","+  - The director picks the song by context: title, intro, cave, field per region, town (day/night), siege, mini-boss, boss, Bee round, results, credits. It crossfades with `music(song, { fade: 1 })`.","+  - **Dynamic town theme:** extra layers come in with town level (`audio.layer('strings', 1, 2)` at Lv2, `'bells'` at Lv3, `'drums'` at Lv4).","+  - Jingles use `audio.sting(song, { at: 'beat' })` over ducked music.","+- **SFX:** custom voices defined with `audio.define(name, voice)` (§7.12). Footsteps by top material, every 0.28 s while walking. Sound comes from code only, never files.","+- **Animalese voices** (`DQ.AudioX.voice`), driven by the Dialog `onLetter` hook:","+  - **Letters and pauses.** For each letter shown (skip spaces): punctuation adds a 90 ms pause, and `?` lifts the last 3 syllables by 20%.","+  - **Each letter becomes one syllable**, 55–70 ms (shorter at fast text speed):","+    1. A **consonant onset**:","+       - s/z/c/x: highpass noise at 4 kHz, 18 ms","+       - t/d/k/g/p/b/q: click (bandpass noise at 1.5 kHz, 8 ms, plus a low thump)","+       - m/n/l/r/w/y/v/f/h/j: a soft voiced onset (lowpass 600 Hz)","+    2. A **vowel body**: a sawtooth or pulse at the speaker's pitch × (1 + letter-hash × range), through two `BiquadFilter` bandpasses at the vowel formants. The vowel is the next vowel in the word.","+","+       | Vowel | F1 (Hz) | F2 (Hz) |","+       |---|---|---|","+       | a | 800 | 1200 |","+       | e | 500 | 1900 |","+       | i | 300 | 2300 |","+       | o | 500 | 900 |","+       | u | 350 | 800 |","+","+       Formants scale with the speaker's `formant` factor.","+  - **Contour:** +8% at word starts, falling 6% across a sentence. ALL-CAPS words are 15% louder and higher.","+  - **Determinism:** pitch jitter comes from `hash(char, index, speakerSeed)`, never `Math.random`.","+  - Routed through `_voiceBus` (the \"Voices\" volume setting). Profiles are in §7.8. The Builder is silent.","+  - In headless runs, voice calls are no-ops (`audio.ctx` is null).","+","+### 6.18 Save and load (`DQ.Save`)","+- Uses `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave, with place and level labels).","+- `write()` returns:","+  ```","+  { data: { v: 1, seed, world: world.diff(), objects: Objects.serialize(),","+            builder: {...}, bag, hotbar, chests,","+            town: {cheer, level, patterns, townChest},","+            residents: [...], story: story.state(), quests,","+            clock: {day, hour}, stats, explored (RLE),","+            lostBundle, flags },","+    place: regionName, level: 'Town Lv ' + level }","+  ```","+- `read()` regenerates the base world from the seed, then applies the diff and the objects, then recomputes rooms and the nav graph.","+- **Autosave:** on `questDone`, after sleeping, at the siege checkpoint, and every 5 minutes when `canSave`.","+- The title's Continue uses `saves.latest()`. `migrate(data, from)` is a stub for future versions; v1 is the only version, so implement it as identity with a version check.","+- In a hub session nothing is saved; the client's storage is in-memory anyway.","+","+### 6.19 Dev mode (`DQ.Dev`, from the pause menu → \"Dev Tools\")","+A full-screen pixel panel with tabs (L1/R1 or the mouse). Every toggle and slider takes effect immediately and is saved under `E.store('dqb-dev')`. It is hidden and disabled in hub sessions.","+","+| Tab | Tools |","+|---|---|","+| **Cheats** | God mode; Creative bag (infinite materials, every recipe known); Fly / no-clip (Space up, Shift down); Instant break; No hunger; One-hit kills; Freeze time of day; Invisible to monsters |","+| **Warp** | Teleport list: Lint Hollow, Thimbleton plaza, Corduroy Crags, Button Quarry, Tweedwood Lint Camp, Calico Coast shipwreck, Frayed Verge, Knot Gate, Knotted Spire top, the Rift. Plus \"Teleport to cursor\" |","+| **Spawn** | Any monster (×1/×5), either boss, any item ×1/×10/×99, any resident (arrive now) |","+| **Story** | Jump to beat: Start / Banner / Lv2 / Lv3 / Lv4 / Hall built / Seam Ripper / Spire / Siege / Boss / Chapter clear. Each beat calls `DQ.Quests.applyBeat(id)`, which sets flags, quests, residents, rooms (via stamps) and inventory to a consistent state. Also: complete the current quest step, set the town level, add Cheer ±50, set the hour, start or skip a siege wave |","+| **Tuning** | Live sliders (below) with **Reset to defaults** (all, or a single slider with △) |","+| **Debug** | Overlays: collision cells, room detector, nav graph and NPC paths, monster aggro rings, cutaway radius, light radii, Pattern ghost status. Perf readout: frame ms, queued runs, actors, lights. Time scale 0.25×–4×. Frame step (while paused, ✕ advances 1 step). Cutaway auto/always/off. Hub net stats (msgs/s, bytes), shown only in Bee solo/loopback |","+| **World** | Export a stamp: mark two corners with the cursor, then copy JSON to the clipboard and offer a download. Save and load a dev snapshot. Regenerate the world |","+","+**Sliders** (`DQ.TUNING_DEFS`: key, label, min, max, step, default):","+","+| Slider | Default | Range |","+|---|---|---|","+| Walk speed | 78 | 40–140 |","+| Sprint multiplier | 1.45 | 1–2.5 |","+| Jump velocity | 215 | 150–320 |","+| Gravity | 800 | 400–1400 |","+| Reach (blocks) | 4.5 | 2–8 |","+| Builder attack × | 1.0 | 0.25–4 |","+| Block damage × | 1.0 | 0.25–5 |","+| Max HP base | 40 | 10–200 |","+| Belly drain × | 1.0 | 0–4 |","+| Monster HP × | 1.0 | 0.25–4 |","+| Monster damage × | 1.0 | 0–4 |","+| Monster speed × | 1.0 | 0.5–2 |","+| Aggro radius (blocks) | 8 | 2–20 |","+| Max monsters | 10 | 0–40 |","+| Spawn interval night (s) | 5 | 1–30 |","+| Day length (min) | 12 | 2–60 |","+| Cheer × | 1.0 | 0.25–5 |","+| Drop rate × | 1.0 | 0–5 |","+| Siege wave size × | 1.0 | 0.25–3 |","+| Helper build rate (blocks/min) | 6 | 0–60 |","+| Ballista reload (s) | 2.5 | 0.5–6 |","+| Tangle window (s) | 8 | 2–20 |","+","+Gameplay code reads `DQ.tuning.get(key)` every time (no cached copies), so sliders are live.","+","+### 6.20 Attract mode (`DQ.Attract`)","+- **Start and exit.** It starts after 10 s without input on the title, name entry, or any title sub-menu (not the Settings screen). **Any input exits it** to the title with a fade: any key, mouse button, mouse movement over 8 px, gamepad button, or stick past 0.5. On touch-only devices it also runs, and a tap exits.","+- **Isolation.** It builds its own `ctx` with a separate world (generated from the seed, plus `stampDemoTown()`: a pre-built Lv4 Thimbleton with rooms, the Hall, ballistas and residents). It never touches the player's save or settings. Sound plays at 60% volume, if unlocked.","+- **The AI builder** is `DQ.Autopilot` running the vignettes below with cheats: invulnerable, infinite materials, placement at 0.15 s per block, teleporting between vignettes behind a wipe transition.","+- **Overlay:** a small logo top left, \"DEMO\" top right (below the corner area), and a blinking \"Press any button\" with the current device's glyph.","+- **Vignettes**, looping forever with a 4 s logo card between loops (each written as a `game.script` and also run by a test):","+","+| # | Vignette | Length |","+|---|---|---|","+| 1 | \"Morning in Thimbleton\": camera glide; residents at their jobs; banner flutter | 12 s |","+| 2 | \"Gathering\": breaks turf and tufts in the Glen; pickups; a Notion popup | 14 s |","+| 3 | \"Crafting\": opens the Mending Bench menu (scripted focus moves) and crafts a Straw Bed | 10 s |","+| 4 | \"Raising a room\": walls 2 high, door, bed, torch, then \"ROOM COMPLETE! Bedroom\" and Cheer bubbles | 24 s |","+| 5 | \"Skirmish\": a combo and a Spin Stitch against Lintlings and a Pinhog; drops | 16 s |","+| 6 | \"Nightfall\": the hour jumps to 21:00; lanterns glow; Mothlets; residents go to bed | 10 s |","+| 7 | \"Siege\": a wave at the walls; ballista fire; Mortimer fights; a Knotbrute smashes a wall | 18 s |","+| 8 | \"Gnarlgrim\": Gnarlgrim at 30% HP; manned ballista hits → TANGLED → Seam Ripper strike → he unravels; confetti | 16 s |","+| 9 | \"Quilting Bee\": 3 bot builders in seat colours raise the Quilt Barn on the Bee world | 10 s |","+","+### 6.21 Multiplayer: AI Hub sessions and the Quilting Bee (`DQ.Net`, `DQ.Bee`)","+**Mode:** `shared-world` (co-op building is the source's multiplayer), 1–4 players, 8-minute rounds. Head tags, written by `build.mjs`:","+```html","+<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Raise the Quilt Barn together, then defend it\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move stick/WASD · Jump ✕/Space · Break □/Click · Place △/Right-click\">","+```","+Also include a description meta and `hub:type`, plus `hub:players` \"1–4\", following the example pages' catalogue tags. `session.js` (unmodified, between its banner and last line) is the first script after `<meta charset>`.","+","+**Session flow** (only when `AIHub.active`; otherwise nothing changes):","+1. No title, attract, menus or saves. Boot straight into `bee` with the Bee world generated (fixed seed `0xBEE` plus the Bee stamp; identical on every copy).","+2. `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, fall back to the normal game (title).","+3. The **game's own card** (`hubcard` scene):","+   - The logo, the players lined up as builders in seat colours (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`; names drawn with the pixel font, never inserted as HTML), the goal, this player's control glyphs, ready ticks, and the countdown from the `card` event (`left`).","+   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a click → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **More time:** △, T or a click → `AIHub.answer('more')` (a second press takes it back).","+   - Nothing here changes the round. Any card randomness uses `AIHub.rng('card')`.","+4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built (no key press).","+5. On `start`: a 3-2-1 countdown while `AIHub.time() < 0`. Play begins when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`.","+6. **Round clock:** 8:00, or `limitMs` if shorter.","+   - **Build phase** (5:00): raise the Quilt Barn Pattern, scaled by player count:","+","+     | Players | Barn walls | Blocks |","+     |---|---|---|","+     | 1 | 2 high | 38 |","+     | 2 | 3 high | 57 |","+     | 3–4 | 3 high + 10 Felt crenellations | 67 |","+","+     Plus a door and 2 torches.","+   - **Raid phase** (3:00): 3 waves from the corners. Knotbrutes target the barn and the Banner (HP 200).","+7. **Scores** (per player):","+   - +3 per Pattern block placed (the host credits the placer)","+   - +5 per monster defeated (Knotbrute +15)","+   - +5 per door or torch crafted and placed in the Pattern","+   - +1 per 5 items gathered","+8. **Host ends the round.** At the time limit, on `time-up` (within `graceMs`), or when every player has left, the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats })`:","+   - `standings`: arrays of ids by score, ties grouped.","+   - `won`: the Pattern is complete and the Banner HP > 0.","+   - `stats`: per id `{ Blocks, Monsters }`.","+   - Awards: \"Master Quilter\" for the most blocks, \"Knot Cutter\" for the most kills.","+9. On `end`: stop input, `audio.mute(true)` and `music(null)`, show \"Round over\", then do nothing more. On `leave`: remove that builder (its placed blocks stay). In **server mode** (`AIHub.server`): run the host simulation with no local builder, camera or input, and skip drawing except a 1-fps static \"Hosting the Bee\" frame.","+","+**Authority and messages.** Every copy runs the voxel world locally and keeps it in sync through edits. The host owns monsters, drops, Pattern progress, the clock and scores. Each client owns its own builder's movement, inventory and hotbar.","+","+| Msg | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Payload (compact arrays, integers) |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `p` | client → host | no | 10 Hz | `[t, x, y, z, facing×100, anim, heldItem, hp]` |","+| `a` | client → host | yes | ≤ 6 Hz, batched | `ops: [['place', x,y,z, block, rot], ['break', x,y,z], ['hit', monId, dmg, kx, ky], ['take', dropId], ['craft', item]]` |","+| `s` | host → all | no | 10 Hz | `{ t, P: [[id,x,y,z,f,anim,held,hp]...], M: [[id,kind,x,y,z,f,hp,state]...], ph, left, prog, bhp }`, kept under 1,100 bytes (if more than 24 monsters, alternate halves) |","+| `e` | host → all | yes | ≤ 6 Hz, batched | `ev: [['vox', x,y,z, id, by], ['drop', id, item, n, x,y,z], ['gone', dropId], ['got', to, item, n], ['hurt', to, dmg, kx, ky], ['fx', kind, x,y,z], ['phase', name], ['score', id, n]]` |","+","+- Per copy that is ≤ 16 messages/s, under the 20/s cap. Every payload stays far below 16 KB; assert this in tests.","+- **Prediction:** a client applies its own place/break immediately and marks the cell pending; the host's `vox` event confirms or corrects it. Monsters on clients interpolate between snapshots (100 ms buffer).","+- **Hits:** a client sends `hit` when its local swing overlaps a monster's interpolated position, and the host applies damage. Old or out-of-order snapshots are dropped by `t`.","+- **Networking goes only through `AIHub.send`/`on`.** No sockets, fetch, `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. \"Quit to title\" does nothing in a session.","+","+**Outside the hub (the game on its own).** The title's **Quilting Bee** runs the same round solo: the local copy is the host, with a `LoopbackNet` that implements the same `send`/`on` surface in process. Optionally 1–3 **bot builders** run on `DQ.Autopilot` (\"Bee with friends: bots on/off\"). This exercises the host code paths outside the hub. Best scores go to `E.store`.","+","+### 6.22 Touch-only devices","+Detection: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, and no gamepad seen and no `keydown` yet. Re-evaluate when a pad connects or a key is pressed.","+","+On such devices:","+- Every scene has `touch: []` and `input.touchEnabled = false`: **no touch controls**.","+- The title shows a stitched panel, \"**Controller or keyboard required**\", with the line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\" The engine's corner **settings/menu button** stays (`corner` on).","+- The attract mode runs as usual, and a tap returns to the title panel.","+","+### 6.23 Settings and accessibility (additions to the standard Settings)","+| Setting | Default |","+|---|---|","+| Button glyphs | PlayStation, or Xbox (sets `input.glyphs`) |","+| Camera view | Isometric, or Three-quarter |","+| Auto-hop | On |","+| Sprint | Hold, or Toggle |","+| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast |","+| Voices volume | 80% |","+| HUD tracker | On |","+| Difficulty | Normal (Relaxed / Hard) |","+| Cutaway | Auto (Always, Off) |","+| Screen shake and flashes | Engine standard |","+","+Reduce motion: the engine handles it; it also disables the camera crossfade and the confetti density.","+","+### 6.24 About/Credits screen and exit interview","+- `tools/build.mjs` reads `./exit-interview.json`, if present, and embeds its `sourceInformation`, `testingFeedback`, `engineFeedback` and `promptFeedback` as `DQ.ABOUT`. The About pages render them.","+  - If the file is missing during development, a dev-only notice says so. A release build fails without it.","+  - Order matters: write `exit-interview.json` before the final build.","+- **Credits page:**","+  - \"Dragon Quilt Builders: an original game inspired by Dragon Quest Builders (Square Enix). Not affiliated with or endorsed by Square Enix. No assets from the original.\"","+  - Design, code, art, music and writing: the AI model (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5) under direction.","+  - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT) by michaelcrosato, with the list of our engine changes.","+  - AI Hub Session client 1.4.0.","+  - Plan: PLAN.md.","+- **Source Information** fields (TASK.md), with \"unknown\" where something cannot be confirmed:","+  - Date `2026-11-03 17:47:40`","+  - Source `Dragon Quest Builders`","+  - Plan `PLAN.md`","+  - Genre and perspective: \"Sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building); isometric 2.5D third person, rotatable\"","+  - Tech, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment (`Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown`), model (`Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max`), usage","+- **Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback** answer TASK.md's questions in order. The same text goes in the final chat reply.","+- **`exit-interview.json`** (the exact shape in TASK.md). Validate it with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Suggested `aiHub` values:","+","+  | Field | Value |","+  |---|---|","+  | name | \"Dragon Quilt Builders\" |","+  | tagline | \"Stitch a frayed world back together\" |","+  | description | \"Gather, craft and build block by block to mend a patchwork kingdom unravelled by a dragon. Raise rooms for quirky residents, defend your town and unpick a knotted boss, or raise a barn together in co-op Quilting Bee rounds.\" |","+  | type | \"Game\" |","+  | genre | \"RPG\" |","+  | source | \"Dragon Quest Builders\" |","+  | series | \"Dragon Quest\" |","+  | players | \"1–4\" |","+  | controls | \"Stick/WASD move · ✕/Space jump · □/Click break · △/Right-click place · L1 R1/wheel items · ○/F talk\" |","+  | tags | [\"building\", \"crafting\", \"co-op\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"] |","+","+---"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2044,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2044,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2hT3eCfK6KuBJrP5iG\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01QaynHKQCv9hNnGJBKVhQBA\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":339,\"limit\":260},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6719,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":488975,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6719},\"output_tokens\":7,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"71161949-a1da-4d35-ab2f-06e1f3234c74\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:59.552Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2hSqFR3sBwEwikCwR1\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01QaynHKQCv9hNnGJBKVhQBA\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":339,\"limit\":260}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01QaynHKQCv9hNnGJBKVhQBA\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"339\\t| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |\\n340\\t| | `call`: Mine / Yours / Auto | Q, I | Middle | 3 △/Y |\\n341\\t| | `view`: Broadcast ↔ Serve Cam | V | — | 11 R3 |\\n342\\t| EXPLORE | `interact` | E, Space, Enter | Left (on a person or thing) | 0 ✕/A |\\n343\\t| | `run` (hold) | Left Shift | — | 1 ○/B, 7 R2 |\\n344\\t| | `bag`: gift bag | G | — | 2 □/X |\\n345\\t| | `leave`: island map | M, Tab | — | 3 △/Y |\\n346\\t| | `snap`: postcard (not in sessions) | C | — | 8 Create/View |\\n347\\t| MENU | `confirm` | Enter, Space | Left | 0 ✕/A |\\n348\\t| | `cancel` | Backspace (Esc on non-pausable screens) | Right | 1 ○/B |\\n349\\t| | `alt` | F | — | 2 □/X |\\n350\\t| | `extra` | R | — | 3 △/Y |\\n351\\t| | `tabL` / `tabR` | Q / E | wheel | 4 L1 / 5 R1 |\\n352\\t| POOLHOP | `hopA` / `hopB` / `hopX` / `hopY` | J, Space / L, Shift / K, E / I, Q | Left = hopA, Right = hopX | 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 |\\n353\\t| CASINO | MENU, plus blackjack H hit, S stand, D double, P split; slots J K L stop reels 1-2-3 | | | |\\n354\\t\\n355\\t- **Split keyboard (Beach Match).** The engine's half-keys give P1 WASD plus F G H R and P2 the arrows plus `.` `/` `,`\\n356\\t  `L`. Order the MATCH actions `play, dive, shot, call` so the halves come out as F/`.` = play, G/`/` = dive, H/`,` =\\n357\\t  shot, R/L = call. Show this on the join screen as keycaps.\\n358\\t- **Escape.** In pausable scenes Escape opens the pause menu, and Backspace or right click goes back inside our canvas\\n359\\t  screens. On title and menu screens Escape goes back.\\n360\\t\\n361\\t**4.1.2 Device and glyph logic.**\\n362\\t\\n363\\t- `G.dev(input)` returns `'ps' | 'xbox' | 'kbm'`. `lastDevice === 'gamepad'` gives `padStyle()`, which follows the\\n364\\t  Button symbols setting; keyboard or mouse gives `kbm`.\\n365\\t- `G.prompt(g, x, y, action, text, { input })` draws a glyph icon and the text and returns its width. Prompts redraw from\\n366\\t  the current device every frame; never cache them.\\n367\\t- **Glyph icons** are pixel art drawn with `px`:\\n368\\t\\n369\\t| Device | How it is drawn |\\n370\\t| --- | --- |\\n371\\t| PlayStation | a 9×9 dark disc with the symbol in its color: ✕ `#8fb8ff`, ○ `#ff7a7a`, □ `#f59ad8`, △ `#5fe0b4` |\\n372\\t| Xbox | a disc in the letter's color, with a dark letter: A `#6ad66a`, B `#ff5a5a`, X `#4aa8ff`, Y `#ffd23a` |\\n373\\t| Pad shoulders and system buttons | rounded pills: L1/R1/L2/R2 or LB/RB/LT/RT; Options/Create or Menu/View; d-pad and stick icons |\\n374\\t| Keyboard | a keycap (light rounded rectangle, darker bottom edge) with `input.label(action, 'keyboard')` |\\n375\\t| Mouse | a 7×9 mouse with the bound button lit |\\n376\\t\\n377\\t- `G.ui.promptBar([[action, text], …])` sits at the bottom centre of every screen. Text never says \\\"press A\\\": the glyph\\n378\\t  always comes from the action map.\\n379\\t\\n380\\t**4.1.3 Mouse.**\\n381\\t\\n382\\t- **Canvas UI:** hover moves focus (`input.pointer()` hit-tested against the widgets laid out last frame); left click\\n383\\t  activates; right click goes back; the wheel scrolls or pages lists.\\n384\\t- **World:** hovering an NPC or an interactable highlights it and shows its name (`r.actor(…, { pick: npc })` with\\n385\\t  `r.pick`). Clicking walks there and interacts.\\n386\\t- **Matches:** while the last device is keyboard or mouse, a reticle follows `game.mouseGround()` on the opponents' half.\\n387\\t  Spike, shot and serve aim at it.\\n388\\t- **Photo mode:** right-drag orbits and the wheel zooms.\\n389\\t\\n390\\t**4.1.4 Rumble.** Use `input.rumble`: spikes and serves (.35, .1 s), blocks (.5, .12 s), dives (.3, .15 s), the jackpot\\n391\\t(.6, .5 s).\\n392\\t\\n393\\t**4.1.5 Touch-only gate.**\\n394\\t\\n395\\t- `G.touchOnly()` is `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches &&\\n396\\t  !G.sawKeyOrPad`. Check it at boot and on each pointer event.\\n397\\t- While it is true:\\n398\\t  - there are no touch controls (patch 7);\\n399\\t  - the title and menu show a centred panel, **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"**, with the line \\\"Connect a controller\\n400\\t    or keyboard to play. The demo keeps running.\\\" and a big **Settings** button (a tap opens `game.menu('settings')`);\\n401\\t  - the engine corner's menu button stays;\\n402\\t  - taps do nothing else, and the attract mode runs as usual (a tap ends it, as any input does).\\n403\\t- The first key or gamepad button sets `G.sawKeyOrPad` and normal play resumes.\\n404\\t- In an AI Hub session a touch-only player's fighter is played by the AI, with the banner \\\"Connect a controller or\\n405\\t  keyboard to take over\\\".\\n406\\t\\n407\\t### 4.2 The 10-foot canvas UI kit (`11-ui.js`)\\n408\\t\\n409\\t**Readability rules.** Each one is a review item.\\n410\\t\\n411\\t- **Text sizes:** the smallest text anywhere is `E.font` 5×7 at scale 1 with a shadow. Headings are scale 2; screen\\n412\\t  titles are `E.font.title` at scale 3; numbers that matter (money, score) are scale 2.\\n413\\t- **Density:** at most 8 focusable items per screen. Item grids are 3×2 (shops, gifts, wardrobe) or 4×2 (album), paged\\n414\\t  with L1/R1, Q/E or the wheel. There is one detail panel. Never show stat tables: use icons, bars, hearts and short\\n415\\t  phrases.\\n416\\t- **Safe area:** keep content inside a 5% margin of `r.W`/`r.H` (TV overscan) and clear of `game.cornerArea()` and\\n417\\t  `input.touchArea()`.\\n418\\t- **Focus:** a 2-px gold outline with a 1-px white inner line, a soft additive glow pulse and a 1-px lift. Sounds:\\n419\\t  `ui_tick` on move, `ui_select` on confirm, `ui_back` on back, `ui_error` on refusal.\\n420\\t- **Navigation:** d-pad, stick, WASD and arrows move focus spatially to the nearest widget in that direction, repeating\\n421\\t  via `input.repeat` (0.35 s delay, 0.09 s rate). Confirm and back come from MENU; tabs are L1/R1 and Q/E; the mouse\\n422\\t  works as in §4.1.3.\\n423\\t- **Themes:**\\n424\\t\\n425\\t| Theme | Panel bg | Border | Ink | Muted | Accent |\\n426\\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n427\\t| Day | `['#0f4c5c', '#0a2d3d']` | `#f6d38a` | `#fff8e8` | `#9fd3d6` | `#ff9e5e` |\\n428\\t| Night (casino, night villa) | `['#2a1240', '#12081e']` | `#ff5fa2` | as day | as day | `#5ff0ff` |\\n429\\t\\n430\\t**Widgets:**\\n431\\t\\n432\\t| Widget | Purpose |\\n433\\t| --- | --- |\\n434\\t| `Panel` | gradient window (`E.ui.box`) |\\n435\\t| `Button` | label, optional glyph, disabled state |\\n436\\t| `List` | vertical menu, scrolls past 8 |\\n437\\t| `Grid` | cards in rows and columns, paged |\\n438\\t| `Tabs` | categories; L1/R1 |\\n439\\t| `Slider` | number; left/right steps, held accelerates, mouse drag; shows the default as a tick |\\n440\\t| `Toggle`, `Stepper` | ◀ value ▶ |\\n441\\t| `Card` | item: icon or live rig preview, name, price, NEW/OWNED/WEARING badges |\\n442\\t| `CharCard` | portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, hearts, mood icon and word |\\n443\\t| `MoneyBadge` | coin icon and amount, animated count |\\n444\\t| `ClockBadge` | \\\"Day 2 · Afternoon\\\" with sun/moon and weather icons |\\n445\\t| `Confirm` | yes/no; default No when destructive |\\n446\\t| `Toast` | slides in at the top for 3 s |\\n447\\t| `PromptBar` | glyph prompts at the bottom |\\n448\\t| `Tip` | one line under the focused card |\\n449\\t\\n450\\t- **Layout:** `ui.frame(r)` lays out widgets from `r.W`/`r.H` each draw and records hit rects; `update` uses last\\n451\\t  frame's rects.\\n452\\t- **E.Shell theme**, for the engine's standard pause, settings and controls screens and for toasts: the day palette,\\n453\\t  `font: '600 20px/1.35 \\\"Trebuchet MS\\\", system-ui, sans-serif'`.\\n454\\t- **Pause actions:** Resume (engine), **How to Play**, **Take a Postcard** (walkable places and match results only),\\n455\\t  **Dev Mode**, then the engine's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit to title (which asks first).\\n456\\t- **Game settings** (via `menu.settings`, group Game):\\n457\\t\\n458\\t| Setting | Values |\\n459\\t| --- | --- |\\n460\\t| Difficulty | Easy, Normal, Hard, Pro |\\n461\\t| Timing assist | Tight, Normal, Generous |\\n462\\t| Auto-run to the ball | on, off |\\n463\\t| Auto-receive | off by default |\\n464\\t| Timing ring | on, off |\\n465\\t| Match camera | Broadcast, Serve Cam |\\n466\\t| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast, Instant |\\n467\\t| Commentary | on, off |\\n468\\t| Button symbols | PlayStation, Xbox (patch 2) |\\n469\\t\\n470\\t  The Voices volume is in the Sound group (patch 4).\\n471\\t\\n472\\t### 4.3 The court and its coordinates\\n473\\t\\n474\\tOne `E.TileMap` is used both as the beach to walk around and as the match court.\\n475\\t\\n476\\t| Name | Value | Notes |\\n477\\t| --- | --- | --- |\\n478\\t| tile | 16 units | engine standard |\\n479\\t| map | 44 × 28 tiles (704 × 448) | rows 0–5 sea (floor tag `sea`, `block: true`), row 6 wet sand `wet`, rows 7–27 sand `sand`; `outside: false` so the backdrop shows past the far edge |\\n480\\t| court X0, X1 | 224, 480 | length 256 (128 a side) |\\n481\\t| net | x = NET_X = 352; top tape z = NET_H = 44; mesh z 28–44 | posts at y = Y0−10 and Y1+10 (h 52); antennae at y = Y0 and Y1, up to z 62 |\\n482\\t| court Y0, Y1 | 176, 304 | width 128; CY = 240 |\\n483\\t| serve zones | x < X0 (left) or x > X1 (right), y within the court | the server stands 20 behind the line |\\n484\\t| lines | 2-unit blue rope lines in `floorTex` on x = X0, X1 and y = Y0, Y1 | beach courts have no centre line |\\n485\\t| far-side strip | y 112–175 | bleachers, umbrellas, Sonny's DJ booth, Pepper's scorer table and flip scoreboard |\\n486\\t| left and right sand | x < 224, x > 480 | tiki bar (left), lifeguard tower and loungers (right) |\\n487\\t| near side | y > 304 | **low props only** (towels, sandcastle, cooler): tall ones would hide the court in Broadcast |\\n488\\t\\n489\\t- Draw order: the backdrop (sky, sun, clouds, distant islands, sea) is drawn first, then `map.drawFloor`. Match the\\n490\\t  `sea` floor color to the backdrop's sea layer by screenshot.\\n491\\t- Time of day sets the backdrop, `lights.ambient`, the tint, and torches and floodlights (lamppost shapes with lights)\\n492\\t  at night.\\n493\\t\\n494\\t### 4.4 Ball flight (`20-ball.js`)\\n495\\t\\n496\\tThe ball is **not** an `E.Body`. It is the current **launch**:\\n497\\t`{ t0, p: [x, y, z], v: [vx, vy, vz], k, g, ay, wob: { a, w, ph } | null, by, kind }`. `t0` is on the match clock,\\n498\\t`M.now()` in seconds: `game.time` locally, or `AIHub.time() / 1000` in a hub session.\\n499\\t\\n500\\t**Closed form.** With τ = t − t0, e = exp(−kτ), k ≥ 1e-4:\\n501\\t\\n502\\t```\\n503\\tx = x0 + vx(1−e)/k\\n504\\ty = y0 + vy(1−e)/k + ay(τ/k − (1−e)/k²) + wobble(τ)            wobble = a·sin(wτ + ph)·min(1, τ/0.3)  (float serves)\\n505\\tz = z0 + (vz + g/k)(1−e)/k − gτ/k\\n506\\tvelocity: (vx·e,  vy·e + ay(1−e)/k,  (vz + g/k)e − g/k)\\n507\\t```\\n508\\t\\n509\\t- `ball.at(t)` and `ball.vel(t)` are sampled every step for drawing. There is no integration drift, and every machine\\n510\\t  agrees, which the online play relies on.\\n511\\t- **Aiming** (`aim(from, to, T)`): given a flight time T,\\n512\\t  - vx = (xT − x0)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)), and vy the same way (subtract the wind term when `ay` ≠ 0);\\n513\\t  - vz = ((zT − z0) + gT/k)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)) − g/k.\\n514\\t- **Flight times by kind:**\\n515\\t\\n516\\t| Kind | T |\\n517\\t| --- | --- |\\n518\\t| pass | `T.passT` (1.05 s) |\\n519\\t| set | `T.setT` (1.1 s); quick set .75 |\\n520\\t| float serve | `T.serveT` (1.3 s) |\\n521\\t| jump serve | `T.jumpServeT` (.85 s) |\\n522\\t| spike | from speed: horizontal distance / (spikeSpeed · cos 15°) |\\n523\\t| shot | `T.shotT` (.95 s) |\\n524\\t| free ball | 1.2 s |\\n525\\t| setter dump | .6 s |\\n526\\t\\n527\\t- **Precomputed events.** Each new launch computes these once:\\n528\\t  - `tNet`, when x crosses NET_X (x is monotonic). At that moment:\\n529\\t    - **clear** if z − r > NET_H;\\n530\\t    - **tape** (net cord) if z + r ≥ NET_H − 3. A new launch starts from the crossing point: with probability\\n531\\t      `T.netCordOver` it keeps going (vx·.35, vz 60 ± 20, from the `match` rng), otherwise it drops back (vx·−.3);\\n532\\t    - **net** if lower: it bounces back (vx·−.25, vy·.5, vz·.3), and the team still has its touches;\\n533\\t    - **antenna/outside** if |y − CY| > 64 + r: a fault on the team that hit it.\\n534\\t  - `tLand`, when z = r. Use bisection on the descending branch to 1e-4 s. The ball is **in** when\\n535\\t    X0 − r ≤ x ≤ X1 + r and Y0 − r ≤ y ≤ Y1 + r (touching the line is in).\\n536\\t  - `timeAtHeight(h)` (descending branch) and `posAt(t)`, for contact planning.\\n537\\t- **The ball itself:** radius r = 3.5; a 10-px sprite (white with blue and yellow panels) whose rotation follows its\\n538\\t  speed; a ground shadow `r.shadow(x, y, 4 − min(2, z·.03), .4)`. The shadow is essential for reading depth.\\n539\\t- **Landing:** dust (`particles.dust`), `sfx('sand')`, and a ball-mark decal for 2.5 s. The ball rolls about 6 units\\n540\\t  for show after the point is decided.\\n541\\t- Players may chase and play the ball outside the court lines, but never past the net plane.\\n542\\t\\n543\\t**Default feel** (all of these are sliders): g 330, k .12, r 3.5. With these numbers:\\n544\\t\\n545\\t| Shot | Path | Apex / timing |\\n546\\t| --- | --- | --- |\\n547\\t| pass | from z 18 to set height 40 | apex ≈ 75 |\\n548\\t| set | from 40 to the spike contact ≈ 62 | apex ≈ 100 |\\n549\\t| float serve | from 52 to the floor in 1.3 s | apex ≈ 98; clears the net by ≈ 40 |\\n550\\t| spike from 20 behind the net, 330 u/s | to 100 beyond the net | lands in ≈ .38 s; clears the tape by ≈ 7 |\\n551\\t\\n552\\tA spike hit from far behind the net with a short, sharp target hits the net. Errors come out of the physics.\\n553\\t\\n554\\t### 4.5 Rules and referee (`21-rules.js`)\\n555\\t\\n556\\t- **Scoring:** rally scoring; one set to `pointsToWin` (vacation 7, final 11, exhibition 7/11/15/21, hub 7); win by 2;\\n557\\t  hard cap at pointsToWin + 4 (to 7, the first to 11 wins even at 11–10). Exhibition can play best of 3 sets of the\\n558\\t  same length.\\n559\\t- **Touches:** at most 3 a side. A block counts as a touch (the beach rule). The same player may not touch twice in a\\n560\\t  row, except straight after her own block.\\n561\\t- **Faults** (point to the other team):\\n562\\t  - the ball lands out after the team's last touch;\\n563\\t  - a 4th touch;\\n564\\t  - a double touch;\\n565\\t  - the ball crosses outside the antennae or under the net;\\n566\\t  - a **net touch**: an airborne player's hands or body pass NET_X ± 2 while the ball is live within 40 units (rare;\\n567\\t    mostly from early, fast blocks);\\n568\\t  - a **serve fault**: into the net, out, or no hit within 1.2 s of the toss.\\n569\\t- **Serve rotation:** on a side-out the receiving team serves, and its server is the player who did not serve last time\\n570\\t  for that team. The first serve goes by coin toss: the player's team, unless an event says otherwise.\\n571\\t- **After a point:** `dead` (1.0 s: the ball settles) → `point` (1.6 s: celebrations) → optional replay → `serveSetup`.\\n572\\t- **Calls:** big banners with a whistle: \\\"IN!\\\", \\\"OUT!\\\", \\\"NET!\\\", \\\"4 TOUCHES\\\", \\\"DOUBLE TOUCH\\\", \\\"ANTENNA\\\", \\\"ACE!\\\", \\\"KILL!\\\",\\n573\\t  \\\"BLOCK!\\\", \\\"NET TOUCH\\\". Each is text plus an icon, never color alone.\\n574\\t- **Stats:**\\n575\\t\\n576\\t| Scope | Counted |\\n577\\t| --- | --- |\\n578\\t| per player | serves, aces, serve faults, digs, perfect passes, sets, kills, attack errors, blocks, points |\\n579\\t| per match | rallies, longest rally |\\n580\\t\\n581\\t### 4.6 Players, actions and the timing judge (`22-players.js`)\\n582\\t\\n583\\t**The player entity:** `{ id, side: 0 | 1, slot: 0 | 1, cast, rig, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, facing, act, input | null, ai,\\n584\\tcall: 'auto' | 'mine' | 'yours', lockT, stats }`.\\n585\\t\\n586\\t**Movement.**\\n587\\t\\n588\\t- Speed is `T.runSpeed × (0.86 + 0.03 × SPD)`, default 96, with acceleration 900 u/s². Players face the ball while it\\n589\\t  is live.\\n590\\t- They can't cross NET_X (clamp at ±6). They can leave the court, but not the map.\\n591\\t- **Auto-run** (`T.autoMove`, Settings): while a human's stick is neutral and she is assigned the next contact, she\\n592\\t  steers toward the contact point at `autoMove ×` her speed.\\n593\\t\\n594\\t**Contact planning.** `planContacts(side)` runs whenever a launch heads to a side and after each touch on that side.\\n595\\tFor each player on that side it computes:\\n596\\t\\n597\\t- **kind**, by touch number: 0 = receive/dig, 1 = set, 2 = attack. A ball arriving from the other side is always\\n598\\t  touch 0.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"69105862-3904-44be-a512-218d91d10b7c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:59.558Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |\\n| | `call`: Mine / Yours / Auto | Q, I | Middle | 3 △/Y |\\n| | `view`: Broadcast ↔ Serve Cam | V | — | 11 R3 |\\n| EXPLORE | `interact` | E, Space, Enter | Left (on a person or thing) | 0 ✕/A |\\n| | `run` (hold) | Left Shift | — | 1 ○/B, 7 R2 |\\n| | `bag`: gift bag | G | — | 2 □/X |\\n| | `leave`: island map | M, Tab | — | 3 △/Y |\\n| | `snap`: postcard (not in sessions) | C | — | 8 Create/View |\\n| MENU | `confirm` | Enter, Space | Left | 0 ✕/A |\\n| | `cancel` | Backspace (Esc on non-pausable screens) | Right | 1 ○/B |\\n| | `alt` | F | — | 2 □/X |\\n| | `extra` | R | — | 3 △/Y |\\n| | `tabL` / `tabR` | Q / E | wheel | 4 L1 / 5 R1 |\\n| POOLHOP | `hopA` / `hopB` / `hopX` / `hopY` | J, Space / L, Shift / K, E / I, Q | Left = hopA, Right = hopX | 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 |\\n| CASINO | MENU, plus blackjack H hit, S stand, D double, P split; slots J K L stop reels 1-2-3 | | | |\\n\\n- **Split keyboard (Beach Match).** The engine's half-keys give P1 WASD plus F G H R and P2 the arrows plus `.` `/` `,`\\n  `L`. Order the MATCH actions `play, dive, shot, call` so the halves come out as F/`.` = play, G/`/` = dive, H/`,` =\\n  shot, R/L = call. Show this on the join screen as keycaps.\\n- **Escape.** In pausable scenes Escape opens the pause menu, and Backspace or right click goes back inside our canvas\\n  screens. On title and menu screens Escape goes back.\\n\\n**4.1.2 Device and glyph logic.**\\n\\n- `G.dev(input)` returns `'ps' | 'xbox' | 'kbm'`. `lastDevice === 'gamepad'` gives `padStyle()`, which follows the\\n  Button symbols setting; keyboard or mouse gives `kbm`.\\n- `G.prompt(g, x, y, action, text, { input })` draws a glyph icon and the text and returns its width. Prompts redraw from\\n  the current device every frame; never cache them.\\n- **Glyph icons** are pixel art drawn with `px`:\\n\\n| Device | How it is drawn |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| PlayStation | a 9×9 dark disc with the symbol in its color: ✕ `#8fb8ff`, ○ `#ff7a7a`, □ `#f59ad8`, △ `#5fe0b4` |\\n| Xbox | a disc in the letter's color, with a dark letter: A `#6ad66a`, B `#ff5a5a`, X `#4aa8ff`, Y `#ffd23a` |\\n| Pad shoulders and system buttons | rounded pills: L1/R1/L2/R2 or LB/RB/LT/RT; Options/Create or Menu/View; d-pad and stick icons |\\n| Keyboard | a keycap (light rounded rectangle, darker bottom edge) with `input.label(action, 'keyboard')` |\\n| Mouse | a 7×9 mouse with the bound button lit |\\n\\n- `G.ui.promptBar([[action, text], …])` sits at the bottom centre of every screen. Text never says \\\"press A\\\": the glyph\\n  always comes from the action map.\\n\\n**4.1.3 Mouse.**\\n\\n- **Canvas UI:** hover moves focus (`input.pointer()` hit-tested against the widgets laid out last frame); left click\\n  activates; right click goes back; the wheel scrolls or pages lists.\\n- **World:** hovering an NPC or an interactable highlights it and shows its name (`r.actor(…, { pick: npc })` with\\n  `r.pick`). Clicking walks there and interacts.\\n- **Matches:** while the last device is keyboard or mouse, a reticle follows `game.mouseGround()` on the opponents' half.\\n  Spike, shot and serve aim at it.\\n- **Photo mode:** right-drag orbits and the wheel zooms.\\n\\n**4.1.4 Rumble.** Use `input.rumble`: spikes and serves (.35, .1 s), blocks (.5, .12 s), dives (.3, .15 s), the jackpot\\n(.6, .5 s).\\n\\n**4.1.5 Touch-only gate.**\\n\\n- `G.touchOnly()` is `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches &&\\n  !G.sawKeyOrPad`. Check it at boot and on each pointer event.\\n- While it is true:\\n  - there are no touch controls (patch 7);\\n  - the title and menu show a centred panel, **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"**, with the line \\\"Connect a controller\\n    or keyboard to play. The demo keeps running.\\\" and a big **Settings** button (a tap opens `game.menu('settings')`);\\n  - the engine corner's menu button stays;\\n  - taps do nothing else, and the attract mode runs as usual (a tap ends it, as any input does).\\n- The first key or gamepad button sets `G.sawKeyOrPad` and normal play resumes.\\n- In an AI Hub session a touch-only player's fighter is played by the AI, with the banner \\\"Connect a controller or\\n  keyboard to take over\\\".\\n\\n### 4.2 The 10-foot canvas UI kit (`11-ui.js`)\\n\\n**Readability rules.** Each one is a review item.\\n\\n- **Text sizes:** the smallest text anywhere is `E.font` 5×7 at scale 1 with a shadow. Headings are scale 2; screen\\n  titles are `E.font.title` at scale 3; numbers that matter (money, score) are scale 2.\\n- **Density:** at most 8 focusable items per screen. Item grids are 3×2 (shops, gifts, wardrobe) or 4×2 (album), paged\\n  with L1/R1, Q/E or the wheel. There is one detail panel. Never show stat tables: use icons, bars, hearts and short\\n  phrases.\\n- **Safe area:** keep content inside a 5% margin of `r.W`/`r.H` (TV overscan) and clear of `game.cornerArea()` and\\n  `input.touchArea()`.\\n- **Focus:** a 2-px gold outline with a 1-px white inner line, a soft additive glow pulse and a 1-px lift. Sounds:\\n  `ui_tick` on move, `ui_select` on confirm, `ui_back` on back, `ui_error` on refusal.\\n- **Navigation:** d-pad, stick, WASD and arrows move focus spatially to the nearest widget in that direction, repeating\\n  via `input.repeat` (0.35 s delay, 0.09 s rate). Confirm and back come from MENU; tabs are L1/R1 and Q/E; the mouse\\n  works as in §4.1.3.\\n- **Themes:**\\n\\n| Theme | Panel bg | Border | Ink | Muted | Accent |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Day | `['#0f4c5c', '#0a2d3d']` | `#f6d38a` | `#fff8e8` | `#9fd3d6` | `#ff9e5e` |\\n| Night (casino, night villa) | `['#2a1240', '#12081e']` | `#ff5fa2` | as day | as day | `#5ff0ff` |\\n\\n**Widgets:**\\n\\n| Widget | Purpose |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `Panel` | gradient window (`E.ui.box`) |\\n| `Button` | label, optional glyph, disabled state |\\n| `List` | vertical menu, scrolls past 8 |\\n| `Grid` | cards in rows and columns, paged |\\n| `Tabs` | categories; L1/R1 |\\n| `Slider` | number; left/right steps, held accelerates, mouse drag; shows the default as a tick |\\n| `Toggle`, `Stepper` | ◀ value ▶ |\\n| `Card` | item: icon or live rig preview, name, price, NEW/OWNED/WEARING badges |\\n| `CharCard` | portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, hearts, mood icon and word |\\n| `MoneyBadge` | coin icon and amount, animated count |\\n| `ClockBadge` | \\\"Day 2 · Afternoon\\\" with sun/moon and weather icons |\\n| `Confirm` | yes/no; default No when destructive |\\n| `Toast` | slides in at the top for 3 s |\\n| `PromptBar` | glyph prompts at the bottom |\\n| `Tip` | one line under the focused card |\\n\\n- **Layout:** `ui.frame(r)` lays out widgets from `r.W`/`r.H` each draw and records hit rects; `update` uses last\\n  frame's rects.\\n- **E.Shell theme**, for the engine's standard pause, settings and controls screens and for toasts: the day palette,\\n  `font: '600 20px/1.35 \\\"Trebuchet MS\\\", system-ui, sans-serif'`.\\n- **Pause actions:** Resume (engine), **How to Play**, **Take a Postcard** (walkable places and match results only),\\n  **Dev Mode**, then the engine's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit to title (which asks first).\\n- **Game settings** (via `menu.settings`, group Game):\\n\\n| Setting | Values |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Difficulty | Easy, Normal, Hard, Pro |\\n| Timing assist | Tight, Normal, Generous |\\n| Auto-run to the ball | on, off |\\n| Auto-receive | off by default |\\n| Timing ring | on, off |\\n| Match camera | Broadcast, Serve Cam |\\n| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast, Instant |\\n| Commentary | on, off |\\n| Button symbols | PlayStation, Xbox (patch 2) |\\n\\n  The Voices volume is in the Sound group (patch 4).\\n\\n### 4.3 The court and its coordinates\\n\\nOne `E.TileMap` is used both as the beach to walk around and as the match court.\\n\\n| Name | Value | Notes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| tile | 16 units | engine standard |\\n| map | 44 × 28 tiles (704 × 448) | rows 0–5 sea (floor tag `sea`, `block: true`), row 6 wet sand `wet`, rows 7–27 sand `sand`; `outside: false` so the backdrop shows past the far edge |\\n| court X0, X1 | 224, 480 | length 256 (128 a side) |\\n| net | x = NET_X = 352; top tape z = NET_H = 44; mesh z 28–44 | posts at y = Y0−10 and Y1+10 (h 52); antennae at y = Y0 and Y1, up to z 62 |\\n| court Y0, Y1 | 176, 304 | width 128; CY = 240 |\\n| serve zones | x < X0 (left) or x > X1 (right), y within the court | the server stands 20 behind the line |\\n| lines | 2-unit blue rope lines in `floorTex` on x = X0, X1 and y = Y0, Y1 | beach courts have no centre line |\\n| far-side strip | y 112–175 | bleachers, umbrellas, Sonny's DJ booth, Pepper's scorer table and flip scoreboard |\\n| left and right sand | x < 224, x > 480 | tiki bar (left), lifeguard tower and loungers (right) |\\n| near side | y > 304 | **low props only** (towels, sandcastle, cooler): tall ones would hide the court in Broadcast |\\n\\n- Draw order: the backdrop (sky, sun, clouds, distant islands, sea) is drawn first, then `map.drawFloor`. Match the\\n  `sea` floor color to the backdrop's sea layer by screenshot.\\n- Time of day sets the backdrop, `lights.ambient`, the tint, and torches and floodlights (lamppost shapes with lights)\\n  at night.\\n\\n### 4.4 Ball flight (`20-ball.js`)\\n\\nThe ball is **not** an `E.Body`. It is the current **launch**:\\n`{ t0, p: [x, y, z], v: [vx, vy, vz], k, g, ay, wob: { a, w, ph } | null, by, kind }`. `t0` is on the match clock,\\n`M.now()` in seconds: `game.time` locally, or `AIHub.time() / 1000` in a hub session.\\n\\n**Closed form.** With τ = t − t0, e = exp(−kτ), k ≥ 1e-4:\\n\\n```\\nx = x0 + vx(1−e)/k\\ny = y0 + vy(1−e)/k + ay(τ/k − (1−e)/k²) + wobble(τ)            wobble = a·sin(wτ + ph)·min(1, τ/0.3)  (float serves)\\nz = z0 + (vz + g/k)(1−e)/k − gτ/k\\nvelocity: (vx·e,  vy·e + ay(1−e)/k,  (vz + g/k)e − g/k)\\n```\\n\\n- `ball.at(t)` and `ball.vel(t)` are sampled every step for drawing. There is no integration drift, and every machine\\n  agrees, which the online play relies on.\\n- **Aiming** (`aim(from, to, T)`): given a flight time T,\\n  - vx = (xT − x0)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)), and vy the same way (subtract the wind term when `ay` ≠ 0);\\n  - vz = ((zT − z0) + gT/k)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)) − g/k.\\n- **Flight times by kind:**\\n\\n| Kind | T |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| pass | `T.passT` (1.05 s) |\\n| set | `T.setT` (1.1 s); quick set .75 |\\n| float serve | `T.serveT` (1.3 s) |\\n| jump serve | `T.jumpServeT` (.85 s) |\\n| spike | from speed: horizontal distance / (spikeSpeed · cos 15°) |\\n| shot | `T.shotT` (.95 s) |\\n| free ball | 1.2 s |\\n| setter dump | .6 s |\\n\\n- **Precomputed events.** Each new launch computes these once:\\n  - `tNet`, when x crosses NET_X (x is monotonic). At that moment:\\n    - **clear** if z − r > NET_H;\\n    - **tape** (net cord) if z + r ≥ NET_H − 3. A new launch starts from the crossing point: with probability\\n      `T.netCordOver` it keeps going (vx·.35, vz 60 ± 20, from the `match` rng), otherwise it drops back (vx·−.3);\\n    - **net** if lower: it bounces back (vx·−.25, vy·.5, vz·.3), and the team still has its touches;\\n    - **antenna/outside** if |y − CY| > 64 + r: a fault on the team that hit it.\\n  - `tLand`, when z = r. Use bisection on the descending branch to 1e-4 s. The ball is **in** when\\n    X0 − r ≤ x ≤ X1 + r and Y0 − r ≤ y ≤ Y1 + r (touching the line is in).\\n  - `timeAtHeight(h)` (descending branch) and `posAt(t)`, for contact planning.\\n- **The ball itself:** radius r = 3.5; a 10-px sprite (white with blue and yellow panels) whose rotation follows its\\n  speed; a ground shadow `r.shadow(x, y, 4 − min(2, z·.03), .4)`. The shadow is essential for reading depth.\\n- **Landing:** dust (`particles.dust`), `sfx('sand')`, and a ball-mark decal for 2.5 s. The ball rolls about 6 units\\n  for show after the point is decided.\\n- Players may chase and play the ball outside the court lines, but never past the net plane.\\n\\n**Default feel** (all of these are sliders): g 330, k .12, r 3.5. With these numbers:\\n\\n| Shot | Path | Apex / timing |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| pass | from z 18 to set height 40 | apex ≈ 75 |\\n| set | from 40 to the spike contact ≈ 62 | apex ≈ 100 |\\n| float serve | from 52 to the floor in 1.3 s | apex ≈ 98; clears the net by ≈ 40 |\\n| spike from 20 behind the net, 330 u/s | to 100 beyond the net | lands in ≈ .38 s; clears the tape by ≈ 7 |\\n\\nA spike hit from far behind the net with a short, sharp target hits the net. Errors come out of the physics.\\n\\n### 4.5 Rules and referee (`21-rules.js`)\\n\\n- **Scoring:** rally scoring; one set to `pointsToWin` (vacation 7, final 11, exhibition 7/11/15/21, hub 7); win by 2;\\n  hard cap at pointsToWin + 4 (to 7, the first to 11 wins even at 11–10). Exhibition can play best of 3 sets of the\\n  same length.\\n- **Touches:** at most 3 a side. A block counts as a touch (the beach rule). The same player may not touch twice in a\\n  row, except straight after her own block.\\n- **Faults** (point to the other team):\\n  - the ball lands out after the team's last touch;\\n  - a 4th touch;\\n  - a double touch;\\n  - the ball crosses outside the antennae or under the net;\\n  - a **net touch**: an airborne player's hands or body pass NET_X ± 2 while the ball is live within 40 units (rare;\\n    mostly from early, fast blocks);\\n  - a **serve fault**: into the net, out, or no hit within 1.2 s of the toss.\\n- **Serve rotation:** on a side-out the receiving team serves, and its server is the player who did not serve last time\\n  for that team. The first serve goes by coin toss: the player's team, unless an event says otherwise.\\n- **After a point:** `dead` (1.0 s: the ball settles) → `point` (1.6 s: celebrations) → optional replay → `serveSetup`.\\n- **Calls:** big banners with a whistle: \\\"IN!\\\", \\\"OUT!\\\", \\\"NET!\\\", \\\"4 TOUCHES\\\", \\\"DOUBLE TOUCH\\\", \\\"ANTENNA\\\", \\\"ACE!\\\", \\\"KILL!\\\",\\n  \\\"BLOCK!\\\", \\\"NET TOUCH\\\". Each is text plus an icon, never color alone.\\n- **Stats:**\\n\\n| Scope | Counted |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| per player | serves, aces, serve faults, digs, perfect passes, sets, kills, attack errors, blocks, points |\\n| per match | rallies, longest rally |\\n\\n### 4.6 Players, actions and the timing judge (`22-players.js`)\\n\\n**The player entity:** `{ id, side: 0 | 1, slot: 0 | 1, cast, rig, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, facing, act, input | null, ai,\\ncall: 'auto' | 'mine' | 'yours', lockT, stats }`.\\n\\n**Movement.**\\n\\n- Speed is `T.runSpeed × (0.86 + 0.03 × SPD)`, default 96, with acceleration 900 u/s². Players face the ball while it\\n  is live.\\n- They can't cross NET_X (clamp at ±6). They can leave the court, but not the map.\\n- **Auto-run** (`T.autoMove`, Settings): while a human's stick is neutral and she is assigned the next contact, she\\n  steers toward the contact point at `autoMove ×` her speed.\\n\\n**Contact planning.** `planContacts(side)` runs whenever a launch heads to a side and after each touch on that side.\\nFor each player on that side it computes:\\n\\n- **kind**, by touch number: 0 = receive/dig, 1 = set, 2 = attack. A ball arriving from the other side is always\\n  touch 0.\",\"numLines\":260,\"startLine\":339,\"totalLines\":2180}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01QaynHKQCv9hNnGJBKVhQBA\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"14f29d82-1b4f-41b6-992e-b1a155bad9ad\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"82679889-a86e-4c3f-976a-ae9e4ba93493\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2076,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2076,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4500,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"28f46fee-d9eb-4cfc-b217-632f45d10047\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4600,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"39f7bc67-33a8-492b-b127-14bad79b15e8\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4750,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"030764ff-8eeb-4961-8277-3407f7d8e8bd\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"6bd019c2-7cd0-4abd-933a-afbf67b54a6a\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"1455cffa-5052-404c-a8dd-d07e67a04832\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":4,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/src/06-data-story.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ArZBGdfNjRzVzKNg3n7ZML","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
