{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K3j2if3avbj48BEAnNo7iP","type":"tool_result","content":"109:Ports and processes: `tools/hub-serve.mjs` runs `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` and parses the printed port. It requests `/` and checks that the page title contains\n204:- **Scenes:** `title` (menu and attract countdown), `attract`, `newgame` (name, look), `intro` (story crawl), `play` (`pausable: true`, `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, whe\n247:### 6.1 Voxel world (the riskiest system; built first, see §9 M1)\n259:- **Level 0 is Backing Cloth** (unbreakable). Below and outside the world is the **Unravel**, a void. Anything falling below z = 8 units, or outside the world, respawns at its \n264:solidAt(x,y,z)  opaqueAt(x,y,z)  liquidAt(x,y,z)   (integer cells; out of bounds: solid below z=0, air above, void outside)\n282:- **Zoom steps.** The player's zoom is quantized to `[0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]`. Apply with `game.setZoom(step)`. Read `input.zoom()` and accumulate it; snap when the accumulated\n293:  - the hero has been hidden by blocks for more than 0.4 s (the x-ray silhouette is showing).\n295:  Blocks at `z ≥ cut` within radius 6.5 cells of the hero are skipped. A 1.5-cell band at the edge is drawn every other pixel (`px.polyDither`). A block just below the cut with\n325:- **Zoom:** right stick ↑/↓, `-`/`=`, and wheel *only while the Map is open*. Quantized steps (§6.1.3). R3/R resets rotation and zoom (`game.resetCamera()`).\n359:- **Belly** drains 4 per in-game hour equivalent (default 1 point every 9 s of real time, about 100 → 0 in 15 min); sprint ×1.5, fighting ×1.2. At 0, HP drops 1 every 4 s. \"You\n416:  - Each row: icon, name, and ingredients as icons with have/need counts. Have ≥ need shows white with a ✓, otherwise red with ✗ (counts in text, never colour alone).\n456:   - WALL: opaque solid at L and L+1, or a stair or table object up to it.\n488:  - **Placement:** the player uses a Pattern scroll (key item) and a ghost footprint follows the cursor. Turn it 90° with Q/E or the stick flick. Confirm on valid ground inside\n489:  - **Ghosts:** each unbuilt cell draws a translucent ghost of its target block (`px.blend(.35)`) with a dashed outline; wrong blocks get a red ✗. The HUD shows a panel: \"Quilt\n593:- **Engine pieces:** `E.Story` (story module) runs conversations as data nodes, with `who`, `say`, `choices`, `set`, `quest`, `done`, `emote` and `event`. One `E.Dialog` instan\n600:- **Objective tracker** (top centre, collapsible with a long press of Create or the N key): the quest title, the current step text, and a marker. The marker is the engine's `r.\n624:  - Behind the menu, a living diorama: the finished Thimbleton built from the attract stamp, at dusk, with a slow camera orbit. The logo reads \"DRAGON QUILT BUILDERS\", each let\n633:  - **Journal:** active quests (giver portrait, steps with ✓), completed ones, and the list of known Notions.\n733:- **Start and exit.** It starts after 10 s without input on the title, name entry, or any title sub-menu (not the Settings screen). **Any input exits it** to the title with a f\n902:| **The Fraying** | x 101–140, y 94–140 | L9 ± 3 with void holes | frayed / earth / stone | Void holes (columns emptied to L0: falling = unravel respawn), dead trees, ash weath\n1143:Reward: the Banner of Mending (key) and the Mending Bench and Lattice Door notions. Cutscene: the frayed world revealed, a camera pan over the Glen to the ruins. Granny: \"Plan\n1152:Planting cutscene: the banner rises, a gold light ring spreads, the border stitch runs around, and \"Thimbleton has been founded!\" appears. Wren walks in from the road. Granny \n1219:The Pattern needs 35 Cobble, 70 Planks, 6 each of Red/Blue/Yellow Felt, 1 Plank Door and 4 Moth Lanterns. Reward: Cheer +100, Heartpatch #3, and the Bobbin Ballista notion. Re\n1460:Each milestone ends with: `node tests/run.mjs` green, `node tools/build.mjs` producing a playable HTML, and a short note in `DEVLOG.md` in the dev folder. Build the **core loo\n1464:| **M0** | Setup | Folder layout, engine copy, `vendor/aihub`, `build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the loader (vm context with `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` stand-ins\n1465:| **M1** | **Voxel core** (riskiest; §10) | `VoxelWorld`, `VoxelRenderer` (atlas, runs, AO, cutaway, x-ray, water, void), `VoxelBody`, picking, break/place in a dev \"sandbox\" \n1478:Parallel work (for teams): after M1's API is frozen (end of M1), M3 (data and crafting), M4 (worldgen) and M8 (audio) can proceed alongside M2. M11 can start with the loopback\n1486:| **Voxel rendering in a 2D engine** (sorting, overhangs, cutaway) | The engine sorts single points; overhangs can draw actors over roofs | M1 first, against the diorama with \n1491:| **Shared-world netcode** | Latency, loss, message caps, host or server modes | Keep the Bee world small; voxel edits are reliable and idempotent; snapshots are unreliable wi\n1493:| **Animalese quality / annoyance** | Synth voices can grate | Prototype the test page in M8 day 1; soft envelopes, low volume (.18), a Voices volume setting, text speed | A o\n1494:| **10-foot legibility** | Pixel font at 240p | Text at scale 1 or more; a 1080p screenshot review in M9 | Use `res: 'snes'` (taller pixels) for menus only, through the scene \n1539:| `attract.test` | Start after 10.0 s idle on the title (not 9.9 s); 3 full loops (about 7.5 min simulated) with no errors and each vignette reaching its end condition; any in","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"25323773-d068-4e2f-8ad5-9dd739557c52","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:44:42.794Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"109:Ports and processes: `tools/hub-serve.mjs` runs `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` and parses the printed port. It requests `/` and checks that the page title contains\n204:- **Scenes:** `title` (menu and attract countdown), `attract`, `newgame` (name, loo