portrait at the left, typed text with Animalese blips, and a ▼ bobbing at page end.\n[1460] Each milestone ends with: `node tests/run.mjs` green, `node tools/build.mjs` producing a playable HTML, and a short note in `DEVLOG.md` in the dev folder. Build the **core loop end to end early** (M1–M6 make Act 1 playable), then widen.\n[1478] Parallel work (for teams): after M1's API is frozen (end of M1), M3 (data and crafting), M4 (worldgen) and M8 (audio) can proceed alongside M2. M11 can start with the loopback once the Builder and VoxelWorld APIs exist.\n[1486] | **Voxel rendering in a 2D engine** (sorting, overhangs, cutaway) | The engine sorts single points; overhangs can draw actors over roofs | M1 first, against the diorama with every hard case (§11.2): lift and sink in `_liftOrder`, runs as occluders, x-ray, cutaway. Use filmstrips in 4 rotations | (a) Draw each block as its own queue item instead of runs; (b) if overhang sorting still glitches, always cut away blocks above `heroLevel+2` within the radius, and let NPCs under roofs be hidden by the roof (sink rule only); (c) as a last resort, limit placement so blocks need support below or a neighbour (no floating roofs). Decide by the end of M1 and record it in DEVLOG |\n[1491] | **Shared-world netcode** | Latency, loss, message caps, host or server modes | Keep the Bee world small; voxel edits are reliable and idempotent; snapshots are unreliable with timestamps; a loopback suite with simulated latency, jitter and loss; run the harness early (a skeleton round in M6) | Reduce the Bee round to the build phase plus a single raid wave; lower snapshot rates to 6 Hz |\n[1493] | **Animalese quality / annoyance** | Synth voices can grate | Prototype the test page in M8 day 1; soft envelopes, low volume (.18), a Voices volume setting, text speed | A one-blip-per-two-letters mode |\n[1494] | **10-foot legibility** | Pixel font at 240p | Text at scale 1 or more; a 1080p screenshot review in M9 | Use `res: 'snes'` (taller pixels) for menus only, through the scene `res` |\n300:The renderer sorts by `view.order(x,y,z) = fx*x + fy*y + z*1e-3`. Runs in one column sort bottom to top, and columns sort by depth. For things that stand on blocks or sit under overhangs, the renderer calls `r._map._liftOrder(view, x, y, z, k)` for every queued item above `z > .5`. `VoxelRenderer.queue` sets `r._map = world`. Implement both directions:\n793:9. On `end`: stop input, `audio.mute(true)` and `music(null)`, show \"Round over\", then do nothing more. On `leave`: remove that builder (its placed blocks stay). In **server mode** (`AIHub.server`): run the host simulation with no local builder, camera or input, and skip drawing except a 1-fps static \"Hosting the Bee\" frame.\n1464:| **M0** | Setup | Folder layout, e\n1465:| **M1** | **Voxel core** (riskiest\n1466:| **M2** | Builder and controls | M\n1467:| **M3** | Items, crafting, objects\n1468:| **M4** | World | `generateWorld` \n1469:| **M5** | Rooms and town | Room de\n1470:| **M6** | Residents and story (Act\n1471:| **M7** | Combat, monsters, bosses\n1472:| **M8** | Audio | Every song and j\n1473:| **M9** | UI polish | Title dioram\n1474:| **M10** | Save, dev mode, attract\n1475:| **M11** | Multiplayer | `DQ.Net` \n1476:| **M12** | Finish | Balance pass w","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NTFNzYjBryhrYvQg3HoBWw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3RKMhWHSfRkudTtr2x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UCigmHSKJgEn1ZvTYZhup3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /var/tmp/opus-plan-x7ef5ea-scripts/fix1.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re, sys\np = sys.argv[1]\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    if n != count:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"expected {count} match(es), found {n}: {old[:70]!r}\")\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nrep(\"It requests `/` and checks that the page title contains \\\"Dragon Quilt Builders\\\" before trusting anything.\",\n    \"It fetches the game page and checks that its `<title>` contains \\\"Dragon Quilt Builders\\\" before trusting anything.\")\nrep(\"`play` (`pausable: true`, `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, wheel: false }`)\",\n    \"`play` (`pausable: true`, `camera: { zoom: false }`: the engine's continuous player zoom stays off, because our own zoom steps call `game.setZoom`, §6.1.3)\")\nrep(\"see §9 M1)\", \"see §9 MS1)\")\nrep(\"Anything falling below z = 8 units, or outside the world, respawns\",\n    \"Anything falling below z = −16 (through a void hole or off the world's edge) respawns\")\nrep(\"(integer cells; out of bounds: solid below z=0, air above, void outside)\",\n    \"(integer cells; outside the world and below level 0 is void, which reads as air)\")\nrep(\"highest solid top ≤ z+step under the circle footprint (world units; feeds E.Body-style physics)\",\n    \"highest solid top ≤ z+step under the circle footprint, −Infinity over void (world units; feeds E.Body-style physics)\")\nrep(\"- **Zoom steps.** The player's zoom is quantized to `[0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]`. Apply with `game.setZoom(step)`. Read `input.zoom()` and accumulate it; snap when the accumulated factor crosses the next step.\",\n    \"- **Zoom steps.** Zoom is quantized to `[0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]` (default 1). Our own zoom actions (− / =, right stick ↑/↓) step through them with `game.setZoom(step)`. The play scene sets `camera: { zoom: false }`, so the engine's continuous player zoom stays off and the atlas only ever needs these five scales. The chosen step is remembered in our settings (`dqZoom`).\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Cutaway** (seeing inside roofs, tunnels and canopies). Each frame, decide `cut = heroLevel + 2` if either of these holds:\n  - there is any opaque block in the hero's column, or the 2 columns toward the camera, at levels `heroLevel+2 .. heroLevel+5`;\n  - the hero has been hidden by blocks for more than 0.4 s (the x-ray silhouette is showing).\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Cutaway** (seeing inside roofs, tunnels and canopies). Each frame, set `cut = heroLevel + 2` when an opaque block sits at a level in `[heroLevel+2, heroLevel+6]` in either of these places:\n  - the hero's own column;\n  - any of the 3 columns toward the camera. Step from the hero's cell by `(round(view.fx), round(view.fy))`, the ground direction that points at the camera; in iso both components are ±1.\n\n  Ordinary 2-high room walls (levels `heroLevel` and `heroLevel+1`) are never cut; the x-ray silhouette shows the hero behind them.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"The cut eases in and out over 0.2 s (radius grows from 0). Turn it off for 0.5 s after the hero leaves cover.\",\n    \"The cut eases in and out over 0.2 s (the radius grows from 0). It stays on for 0.5 s after the hero leaves cover (hysteresis), so it does not flicker at doorways.\")\nrep(\"`VoxelRenderer.queue` sets `r._map = world`. Implement both directions:\",\n    \"`VoxelRenderer.queue` sets `r._map = world`. Call it before queuing any actor or object: the renderer reads `r._map` at queue time and resets it to null at the start of every frame. Implement both directions:\")\nrep(\"- **Zoom:** right stick ↑/↓, `-`/`=`, and wheel *only while the Map is open*. Quantized steps (§6.1.3). R3/R resets rotation and zoom (`game.resetCamera()`).\",\n    \"- **Zoom:** right stick ↑/↓ or `−`/`=` step through the zoom levels (§6.1.3). In play the mouse wheel belongs to the hotbar; it zooms only on the Map screen. R3/R resets rotation and zoom (`game.resetCamera()`, then zoom step 1).\")\nrep(\"- **Belly** drains 4 per in-game hour equivalent (default 1 point every 9 s of real time, about 100 → 0 in 15 min);\",\n    \"- **Belly** drains 1 point every 9 s of real time (100 → 0 in 15 minutes);\")\nrep(\"Have ≥ need shows white with a ✓, otherwise red with ✗ (counts in text, never colour alone).\",\n    \"Have ≥ need shows white with a tick icon, otherwise red with a cross icon (counts in text too, never colour alone). The pixel font has no ✓ or ✗, so draw them as `DQ.Glyphs` icons.\")\nrep(\"   - WALL: opaque solid at L and L+1, or a stair or table object up to it.\\n   - DOOR: a door object at L.\",\n    \"   - WALL: opaque solid blocks at both L and L+1.\\n   - DOOR: a door object at L, set in a straight wall: the two cells beside it along the wall are WALL or DOOR. A door on a corner does not count.\")\nrep(\"Turn it 90° with Q/E or the stick flick.\",\n    \"Turn it 90° with L1/R1 (pad), or the mouse wheel or [ / ] (keyboard); the camera still turns with Q/E and the right stick.\")\nrep(\"wrong blocks get a red ✗. The HUD shows a panel: \\\"Quilters' Hall: 37/127\\\"\",\n    \"wrong blocks get a red cross icon. The HUD shows a panel: \\\"Quilters' Hall: 37/129\\\"\")\nrep(\"and a ▼ bobbing at page end.\",\n    \"and a bobbing arrow sprite at page end (the font has no ▼).\")\nrep(\"(top centre, collapsible with a long press of Create or the N key)\",\n    \"(top centre; switch it off per quest with Track on/off in the Journal, or entirely with the HUD tracker setting)\")\nrep(\"with a slow camera orbit.\", \"with a slow camera pan.\")\nrep(\"steps with ✓\", \"steps with tick icons\")\nrep(\"It starts after 10 s without input on the title, name entry, or any title sub-menu (not the Settings screen).\",\n    \"It starts after 10 s without input on the title screen or its menus (main menu, Load list, About). It does not start on the Settings screen or during name entry, where the player is busy choosing.\")\nrep(\"Void holes (columns emptied to L0: falling = unravel respawn)\",\n    \"Void holes (columns emptied entirely, Backing Cloth included: falling in = unravel respawn)\")\nrep(\"Reward: the Banner of Mending (key) and the Mending Bench and Lattice Door notions.\",\n    \"Reward: the Banner of Mending (key).\")\nrep(\"Granny teaches the Mending Bench (a Pocket recipe).\",\n    \"Granny teaches the Mending Bench (a Pocket recipe) and Lattice Door notions.\")\nrep(\"The Pattern needs 35 Cobble, 70 Planks, 6 each of Red/Blue/Yellow Felt, 1 Plank Door and 4 Moth Lanterns.\",\n    \"The Pattern (outer 11×9, interior 9×7 = 63 cells) has 129 cells:\\n- level 1: 35 Cobble (the perimeter minus the door)\\n- level 2: 35 Planks\\n- level 3: 36 Planks (a lintel over the door)\\n- level 4: 18 Felt crenellations, 6 per colour, on every other perimeter cell\\n- 1 Plank Door\\n- 4 Moth Lanterns in the interior corners\\n\\n\")\n# milestones: MS prefix (quests keep M1–M14)\nfor i in range(13):\n    rep(f\"| **M{i}** |\", f\"| **MS{i}** |\")\nrep(\"(M1–M6 make Act 1 playable), then widen.\",\n    \"(MS1–MS6 make Act 1 playable), then widen. Milestones are numbered MS0–MS12; quests keep their own IDs, M1–M14 and S1–S3.\")\nrep(\"after M1's API is frozen (end of M1), M3 (data and crafting), M4 (worldgen) and M8 (audio) can proceed alongside M2. M11 can start\",\n    \"after MS1's API is frozen (end of MS1), MS3 (data and crafting), MS4 (worldgen) and MS8 (audio) can proceed alongside MS2. MS11 can start\")\nrep(\"| M1 first, against the diorama\", \"| MS1 first, against the diorama\")\nrep(\"Decide by the end of M1 and record it in DEVLOG\", \"Decide by the end of MS1 and record it in DEVLOG\")\nrep(\"(a skeleton round in M6)\", \"(a skeleton round in MS6)\")\nrep(\"Prototype the test page in M8 day 1;\", \"Prototype the test page on the first day of MS8;\")\nrep(\"a 1080p screenshot review in M9\", \"a 1080p screenshot review in MS9\")\nrep(\"(about 7.5 min simulated)\", \"(about 7 minutes simulated)\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPYEOF\npython3 -I /var/tmp/opus-plan-x7ef5ea-scripts/fix1.py /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","description":"Apply consistency fixes to PLAN.md with asserted replacements"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7384,"cache_read_input_tokens":412930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7384},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"c59cd5be-e517-485c-a320-4f88082128a1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:45:53.485Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3RK5amCvw8T9WRzvNr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UCigmHSKJgEn1ZvTYZhup3":{"command":"cat > /var/tmp/opus-plan-x7ef5ea-scripts/fix1.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re, sys\np = sys.argv[1]\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    if n != count:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"expected {count} match(es), found {n}: {old[:70]!r}\")\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nrep(\"It requests `/` and checks that the page title contains \\\"Dragon Quilt Builders\\\" before trusting anything.\",\n    \"It fetches the game page and checks that its `<title>` contains \\\"Dragon Quilt Builders\\\" before trusting anything.\")\nrep(\"`play` (`pausable: true`, `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, wheel: false }`)\",\n    \"`play` (`pausable: true`, `camera: { zoom: false }`: the engine's continuous player zoom stays off, because our own zoom steps call `game.setZoom`, §6.1.3)\")\nrep(\"see §9 M1)\", \"see §9 MS1)\")\nrep(\"Anything falling below z = 8 units, or outside the world, respawns\",\n    \"Anything falling below z = −16 (through a void hole or off the world's edge) respawns\")\nrep(\"(integer cells; out of bounds: solid below z=0, air above, void outside)\",\n    \"(integer cells; outside the world and below level 0 is void, which reads as air)\")\nrep(\"highest solid top ≤ z+step under the circle footprint (world units; feeds E.Body-style physics)\",\n    \"highest solid top ≤ z+step under the circle footprint, −Infinity over void (world units; feeds E.Body-style physics)\")\nrep(\"- **Zoom steps.** The player's zoom is quantized to `[0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]`. Apply with `game.setZoom(step)`. Read `input.zoom()` and accumulate it; snap when the accumulated factor crosses the next step.\",\n    \"- **Zoom steps.** Zoom is quantized to `[0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5, 2]` (default 1). Our own zoom actions (− / =, right stick ↑/↓) step through them with `game.setZoom(step)`. The play scene sets `camera: { zoom: false }`, so the engine's continuous player zoom stays off and the atlas only ever needs these five scales. The chosen step is remembered in our settings (`dqZoom`).\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Cutaway** (seeing inside roofs, tunnels and canopies). Each frame, decide `cut = heroLevel + 2` if either of these holds:\n  - there is any opaque block in the hero's column, or the 2 columns toward the camera, at levels `heroLevel+2 .. heroLevel+5`;\n  - the hero has been hidden by blocks for more than 0.4 s (the x-ray silhouette is showing).\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Cutaway** (seeing inside roofs, tunnels and canopies). Each frame, set `cut = heroLevel + 2` when an opaque block sits at a level in `[heroLevel+2, heroLevel+6]` in either of these places:\n  - the hero's own column;\n  - any of the 3 columns toward the camera. Step from the hero's cell by `(round(view.fx), round(view.fy))`, the ground direction that points at the camera; in iso both components are ±1.\n\n  Ordinary 2-high room walls (levels `heroLevel` and `heroLevel+1`) are never cut; the x-ray silhouette shows the hero behind them.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"The cut eases in and out over 0.2 s (radius grows from 0). Turn it off for 0.5 s after the hero leaves cover.\",\n    \"The cut eases in and out over 0.2 s (the radius grows from 0). It stays on for 0.5 s after the hero leaves cover (hysteresis), so it does not flicker at doorways.\")\nrep(\"`VoxelRenderer.queue` sets `r._map = world`. Implement both directions:\",\n    \"`VoxelRenderer.queue` sets `r._map = world`. Call it before queuing any actor or object: the renderer reads `r._map` at queue time and resets it to null at the start of every frame. Implement both directions:\")\nrep(\"- **Zoom:** right stick ↑/↓, `-`/`=`, and wheel *only while the Map is open*. Quantized steps (§6.1.3). R3/R resets rotation and zoom (`game.resetCamera()`).\",\n    \"- **Zoom:** right stick ↑/↓ or `−`/`=` step through the zoom levels (§6.1.3). In play the mouse wheel belongs to the hotbar; it zooms only on the Map screen. R3/R resets rotation and zoom (`game.resetCamera()`, then zoom step 1).\")\nrep(\"- **Belly** drains 4 per in-game hour equivalent (default 1 point every 9 s of real time, about 100 → 0 in 15 min);\",\n    \"- **Belly** drains 1 point every 9 s of real time (100 → 0 in 15 minutes);\")\nrep(\"Have ≥ need shows white with a ✓, otherwise red with ✗ (counts in text, never colour alone).\",\n    \"Have ≥ need shows white with a tick icon, otherwise red with a cross icon (counts in text too, never colour alone). The pixel font has no ✓ or ✗, so draw them as `DQ.Glyphs` icons.\")\nrep(\"   - WALL: opaque solid at L and L+1, or a stair or table object up to it.\\n   - DOOR: a door object at L.\",\n    \"   - WALL: opaque solid blocks at both L and L+1.\\n   - DOOR: a door object at L, set in a straight wall: the two cells beside it along the wall are WALL or DOOR. A door on a corner does not count.\")\nrep(\"Turn it 90° with Q/E or the stick flick.\",\n    \"Turn it 90° with L1/R1 (pad), or the mouse wheel or [ / ] (keyboard); the camera still turns with Q/E and the right stick.\")\nrep(\"wrong blocks get a red ✗. The HUD shows a panel: \\\"Quilters' Hall: 37/127\\\"\",\n    \"wrong blocks get a red cross icon. The HUD shows a panel: \\\"Quilters' Hall: 37/129\\\"\")\nrep(\"and a ▼ bobbing at page end.\",\n    \"and a bobbing arrow sprite at page end (the font has no ▼).\")\nrep(\"(top centre, collapsible with a long press of Create or the N key)\",\n    \"(top centre; switch it off per quest with Track on/off in the Journal, or entirely with the HUD tracker setting)\")\nrep(\"with a slow camera orbit.\", \"with a slow camera pan.\")\nrep(\"steps with ✓\", \"steps with tick icons\")\nrep(\"It starts after 10 s without input on the title, name entry, or any title sub-menu (not the Settings screen).\",\n    \"It starts after 10 s without input on the title screen or its menus (main menu, Load list, About). It does not start on the Settings screen or during name entry, where the player is busy choosing.\")\nrep(\"Void holes (columns emptied to L0: falling = unravel respawn)\",\n    \"Void holes (columns emptied entirely, Backing Cloth included: falling in = unravel respawn)\")\nrep(\"Reward: the Banner of Mending (key) and the Mending Bench and Lattice Door notions.\",\n    \"Reward: the Banner of Mending (key).\")\nrep(\"Granny teaches the Mending Bench (a Pocket recipe).\",\n    \"Granny teaches the Mending Bench (a Pocket recipe) and Lattice Door notions.\")\nrep(\"The Pattern needs 35 Cobble, 70 Planks, 6 each of Red/Blue/Yellow Felt, 1 Plank Door and 4 Moth Lanterns.\",\n    \"The Pattern (outer 11×9, interior 9×7 = 63 cells) has 129 cells:\\n- level 1: 35 Cobble (the perimeter minus the door)\\n- level 2: 35 Planks\\n- level 3: 36 Planks (a lintel over the door)\\n- level 4: 18 Felt crenellations, 6 per colour, on every other perimeter cell\\n- 1 Plank Door\\n- 4 Moth Lanterns in the interior corners\\n\\n\")\n# milestones: MS prefix (quests keep M1–M14)\nfor i in range(13):\n    rep(f\"| **M{i}** |\", f\"| **MS{i}** |\")\nrep(\"(M1–M6 make Act 1 playable), then widen.\",\n    \"(MS1–MS6 make Act 1 playable), then widen. Milestones are numbered MS0–MS12; quests keep their own IDs, M1–M14 and S1–S3.\")\nrep(\"after M1's API is frozen (end of M1), M3 (data and crafting), M4 (worldgen) and M8 (audio) can proceed alongside M2. M11 can start\",\n    \"after MS1's API is frozen (end of MS1), MS3 (data and crafting), MS4 (worldgen) and MS8 (audio) can proceed alongside MS2. MS11 can start\")\nrep(\"| M1 first, against the diorama\", \"| MS1 first, against the diorama\")\nrep(\"Decide by the end of M1 and record it in DEVLOG\", \"Decide by the end of MS1 and record it in DEVLOG\")\nrep(\"(a skeleton round in M6)\", \"(a skeleton round in MS6)\")\nrep(\"Prototype the test page in M8 day 1;\", \"Prototype the test page on the first day of MS8;\")\nrep(\"a 1080p screenshot review in M9\", \"a 1080p screenshot review in MS9\")\nrep(\"(about 7.5 min simulated)\", \"(about 7 minutes simulated)\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPYEOF\npython3 -I /var/tmp/opus-plan-x7ef5ea-scripts/fix1.py /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","description":"Apply consistency fixes to PLAN.md with asserted replacements"}}}
