{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L4i2UFFWHhES1wEbgMfHMt","type":"tool_result","content":"510\t  - **Marigold** (cook): with a Kitchen, cooks at the Hearth Pot (stirring loop) twice a day from Town Chest ingredients into the chest. At 18:00 she sets a dish on the Mess Hall table. In sieges she throws hot pies (5 damage, arc).\n511\t  - **Professor Selvage** (helper): builds Patterns from the Town Chest at the helper rate, or reads in the Workshop. In sieges he hides in the Hall.\n512\t  - **Lintwick** (fluff-farmer): puts 2 Lint into the Town Chest daily and dances (a Blob hop loop) when happy. In sieges he rolls into monsters (3 damage + knockback).\n513\t- **Needs and Cheer bubbles.** At most once per day per need, each satisfied need spawns a floating pink heart bubble (+5 Cheer) over the resident, which stays until collected:\n514\t  - sleep: slept in a bed\n515\t  - meal: ate a dish\n516\t  - comfort: their favourite room exists (Wren: Bedroom, Mortimer: Guard Post, Marigold: Kitchen, Professor: Workshop, Lintwick: a Bedroom with a Felt block in its walls)\n517\t\n518\t  Collect a bubble by walking within 2 blocks of it. Unhappy residents show a `dots` balloon and say why when you talk to them.\n519\t- **Requests:** a resident with an available quest shows a bouncing \"!\" balloon (`story.emote`). Talking starts it, and its steps appear in the Journal and HUD. When the steps are done, a \"?\" balloon shows; talk to them to turn it in.\n520\t- **Arrival cutscene:** the resident walks in along the east road, the camera pans to them, and they say their intro line. \"Mortimer has moved into Thimbleton!\" shows with a jingle.\n521\t- **Navigation** (`DQ.Nav`):\n522\t  - **Graph:** nodes are standable `(x, y, L)`. Edges:\n523\t    - 8-neighbour moves (diagonals only if both orthogonal neighbours are open), cost 1 (diagonal 1.41)\n524\t    - step up 1 level (a hop), cost 2\n525\t    - drop down 1–3 levels, cost 1.5\n526\t    - doors open for residents, closed for monsters\n527\t  - **A\\*** with a binary heap, capped at 3,000 expanded nodes. Smooth paths by line-of-walk. Re-path when an edit touches a path cell.\n528\t  - **Stuck rule:** if a resident has not progressed for 8 s and is off-screen, teleport them to the target. On screen, try a hop, then re-path.\n529\t- **Talk:** dialog with a portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) and the resident's voice. Lines vary by flags, time of day, mood and town level (`E.Story` nodes with `if` conditions).\n530\t\n531\t### 6.11 Monsters and combat (`DQ.Monsters`, `DQ.Combat`)\n532\t- **AI states:** `idle/wander → notice` (a \"!\" over the head plus a squeak, 0.3 s) `→ chase → windup` (telegraph: flash, crouch or squash, a sound) `→ attack → recover`. Then `→ flee` (below 20% HP for Lintlings) or `→ hurt` (stagger 0.25 s) `→ dead` (pop, particles, drops, `monsterKilled`).\n533\t  - Aggro uses radius `tuning.aggro`, scaled by type (§7.9), plus `world.raycast` sight from eye height.\n534\t  - Leash: return home after chasing 24 blocks away from home.\n535\t- **Spawning:**\n536\t  - Region tables (§7.1) by day or night. Spawn on standable cells under open sky, ≥ 10 blocks from the builder, outside the town border, never inside rooms or during cutscenes.\n537\t  - Rate: 1 spawn per `tuning.spawnEvery` s (day 8, night 5) while the active count is below `tuning.maxMonsters` (default 10).\n538\t  - Despawn: more than 40 blocks away for 20 s.\n539\t- **Damage:**\n540\t  - `dmg = max(1, round((atk − def/2) × U(0.9, 1.1)))`, where U is drawn from the combat stream.\n541\t  - Builder crits: 5%, ×1.5 (Spin Stitch never crits).\n542\t  - Multipliers: `tuning.monsterHp`, `tuning.monsterDmg`, `tuning.builderAtk`, and difficulty (Relaxed 0.5 damage taken, Normal 1, Hard 1.4).\n543\t- **Hit feedback:**\n544\t  - `game.hitFx(x,y,z,{ power, damage, angle })` (hit-stop, shake, impact star, damage number), plus `E.knockback(builder, mon, 120, 40)`.\n545\t  - Monster hits on the builder: knockback 90, i-frames 0.8 s, a red vignette flash under `game.flash` limits.\n546\t  - Each move has its own sound.\n547\t- **Drops:** rolled on death from the drop table (`tuning.dropRate` multiplier on chances); items fly out.\n548\t\n549\t### 6.12 Siege and bosses (`DQ.Siege`, `DQ.Bosses`)\n550\t- **Siege director** (used once in the story, M13–M14, and in the Bee round). It is a `game.script` generator:\n551\t  1. **Prep.** Mortimer's rally line, then a 90 s countdown banner (\"The Knotted army approaches! 1:30\"). Build defences meanwhile; the music turns tense with the drum layer.\n552\t  2. **Autosave checkpoint** `siege`.\n553\t  3. **Waves** W1 → W2 → W3 (§7.9). Each wave spawns over 10 s from the east road (96,76), the Rift (96,80) and the north path (72,52). It ends when all of its monsters are defeated. Between waves: a 25 s breather with \"Wave cleared!\" and a repair prompt.\n554\t  4. **Boss.** Gnarlgrim enters through the Rift (cutscene, §7.10).\n555\t- **Monster targets in sieges:** first the Banner (HP 300; its HP bar is on the HUD during the siege), then ballistas, then the nearest town-structure block in the way (flagged `town` when placed inside the border), then residents, then the builder.\n556\t  - Monsters path with **breaker A\\***: wall blocks count as passable at cost 8 per block, and doors at cost 4.\n557\t  - On reaching a blocking block or door, a monster attacks it (Lintling 3, Pinhog 6, Frayed Knight 8, Knotbrute 25, Gnarlgrim 60 block damage per hit).\n558\t- **Fail:** the Banner falls, or the builder is KO'd while Gnarlgrim is active. Then \"The Banner has fallen...\" / \"You've come undone...\", and a choice: \"Try again from the start of the siege\" (reload the checkpoint) or \"Return to title\". Waves already cleared stay cleared only within a single attempt.\n559\t- **Sir Buttonsworth** (mini-boss, Button Quarry floor):\n560\t  - Intro: he rises from a heap of buttons.\n561\t  - Moves:\n562\t    - **Slam:** wind .6 s; a shockwave ring of radius 3 blocks expands over .5 s. Jump to avoid it; it deals 12.\n563\t    - **Button Volley:** wind .4 s; 5 buttons in a 50° spread (`E.Bullets`, 110 u/s, 8 damage).\n564\t    - **Stomp Charge:** wind .7 s; charges 140 u/s toward the builder, breaks blocks in its path, and is dizzy for 2 s after hitting a wall. Dizzy takes double damage.\n565\t  - Below 50% HP he summons 3 Lintlings once.\n566\t  - The arena has 4 cobble pillars that break under charges.\n567\t  - Defeat: he pops into buttons and drops the Golden Needle and 3 Steel Thread.\n568\t- **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** (final boss, in and around the Thimbleton plaza), HP 600 in three phases (100–66%, 66–33%, 33–0%):\n569\t  - **Tightly wound.** Def 25, so normal hits do about 1 damage. Mortimer and Granny hint \"Use the Ballistas!\" after 3 such hits.\n570\t  - **Tangled.** 2 manned-ballista hits within 8 s, or 1 hit during his charge, make him Tangled for 5 s: he sits in a heap with `down: .6`, his chest **Heart Knot** glows, and his def drops to 0.\n571\t    - Hits on the Heart Knot (front arc) with the Seam Ripper do ×4, other weapons ×2.\n572\t    - A stagger plays at 100 damage per Tangle; leaving the Tangle triggers a roar knockback.\n573\t  - **Phase 1:** Yarn Slam (ring, radius 3.5) and Tangle Toss (lobbed yarn ball via `E.arc`, landing in 1.1 s on a shadow telegraph; 10 damage and leaves a temporary Tangle block for 20 s).\n574\t  - **Phase 2:** adds Charge (breaks blocks in its path and targets a ballista) and summons 4 Lintlings at the phase start.\n575\t  - **Phase 3:** all moves 25% faster, a double Tangle Toss, and a Knotbrute summon.\n576\t  - Phase transitions: a roar (`shout` expression) and a knockback ring; the music switches to the next layer.\n577\t  - Defeat cutscene: he unravels into heaps of yarn (thread particles) and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner. The rift heals (§7.10).\n578\t\n579\t### 6.13 Day, night, lighting, weather (`DQ.Clock`)\n580\t- One day = `tuning.dayMinutes` (12) real minutes; the story starts on Day 1 at 08:00.\n581\t- **Phases:** dawn 05–07, day 07–17, dusk 17–19, night 19–05.\n582\t- `game.lights.enabled = true` always. `ambient` follows the hour: night .30 with a cool blue tint, dawn and dusk .65 with a warm tint, day 1.0. Use `lights.tint`, setting `lights.dark` per phase, then `lights.refresh()`.\n583\t- Light sources add light pools (§6.7). At night, stars twinkle in the void, Mothlets spawn and Frayed Knights roam the Rift.\n584\t- **HUD clock:** a sun/moon dial with \"Day 3\".\n585\t- **Weather (cosmetic, engine `game.weather`):** the Fraying always has `ash` (purple tint). The Glen rains lightly some days (Day 2 afternoon, Day 4 morning). Weather resets per region when it changes.\n586\t- **Sleeping** is in §6.7. **Night-time Granny line:** the first night she warns \"Monsters get bolder after dark, dearie. A lit room is a safe room!\"\n587\t\n588\t### 6.14 Health and hunger\n589\t- The HUD shows HP as a red patch bar with numbers (\"HP 32/40\") and Belly as a bread-loaf bar.\n590\t- Low HP (< 25%) adds a heartbeat sfx and a red vignette (follows the reduce-flash setting).\n591\t- Food is in §7.3. Eating restores Belly and HP; raw Thimbleberries restore Belly +5.\n592\t- Starving: HP −1 every 4 s, with the prompt \"Your belly is empty! Eat something!\"\n593\t\n594\t### 6.15 Story, quests, dialog, cutscenes (`DQ.Quests`, `DQ.Cutscenes`)\n595\t- **Engine pieces:** `E.Story` (story module) runs conversations as data nodes, with `who`, `say`, `choices`, `set`, `quest`, `done`, `emote` and `event`. One `E.Dialog` instance is skinned as a Dragon Quest-style box: a dark indigo panel with a cream stitched border (dashed 1-px line 2 px inside the edge), a name tab, a portrait at the left, typed text with Animalese blips, and a bobbing arrow sprite at page end (the font has no ▼).\n596\t- **Granny Gossamer's box:** a golden stitched border with gold text and a glowing spool portrait (a custom portrait function).\n597\t- **Text:** 3 lines per page, at most 52 characters per line, `E.font` scale 1 (≈ 31 px tall on a 1080p TV).\n598\t- **Quest data** (§7.10): `{ id, title, giver, steps: [{ text, done: condition }], reward, next, unlock }`. Conditions are data:\n599\t  - `{ have: {item: n} }`, `{ crafted: id }`, `{ placed: objId }`, `{ room: type }`, `{ level: n }`, `{ talk: npc }`\n600\t  - `{ killed: {monster: n} }`, `{ at: poi, radius }`, `{ pattern: id }`, `{ flag: k }`, `{ siegeDone: true }`, `{ boss: id }`\n601\t- **Quest director:** evaluates the current steps on relevant events (cheap) and once per second as a fallback. It advances steps and emits `questStep`/`questDone`. Rewards: `{ cheer, items, notions, flags, heartpatch }`. HUD: \"Quest complete: Wren's Bed\" with a jingle.\n602\t- **Objective tracker** (top centre; switch it off per quest with Track on/off in the Journal, or entirely with the HUD tracker setting): the quest title, the current step text, and a marker. The marker is the engine's `r.marker(x,y,z,{label})`, which becomes an edge arrow off screen, with the distance in blocks. Targets: the POI, NPC or Pattern from the step, or for gather steps the nearest matching plant or block within 40 blocks (scanned once per second).\n603\t- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens on a proxy, dialog awaits (`yield E.until(() => !talk.open)`), NPC walks (autopilot), and effects.\n604\t  - Skip: hold ○, Esc or right click for 1 s (a fill ring shows) to jump to the end state.\n605\t  - Every cutscene has `apply()`, which sets its end state. Skipping and tests call it.\n606\t- **Writing style** (Dragon Quest-like):\n607\t  - Short, punchy lines; exclamations; earnest heroism softened with jokes; sewing puns; NPCs with verbal tics.\n608\t  - The silent Builder answers only through choices (\"Of course!\" / \"What's a bed?\").\n609\t  - System lines are cheerful: \"You got 3 Straw!\", \"Thimbleton is now Level 2!\", \"A Lintling bounces into view!\"\n610\t  - Avoid modern slang. Keep it family-friendly. Never reuse Dragon Quest names, places or iconic phrases verbatim.\n611\t\n612\t### 6.16 UI screens and HUD (10-foot, controller first; `DQ.Hud`, `DQ.Menus`)\n613\tAll UI is pixel art drawn with `E.ui`, `E.font` and `px` inside `r.overlay`. Panels are dark felt (`E.ui.box` gradient `#2a2350 → #1a1636`) with stitched cream borders. Text is at least scale 1 at 240p; headers scale 2; the title logo scale 3–4. At most about 6–8 entries per screen and generous spacing: no dense tables. Information is never conveyed by colour alone (icons plus text).\n614\t\n615\t- **HUD (in play):**\n616\t  - Top left: HP bar, Belly bar, and the equipped weapon icon.\n617\t  - Top centre: the objective tracker.\n618\t  - Top right, *below* `game.cornerArea()`: the clock dial with the day, and the Banner badge (level, Cheer bar).\n619\t  - Bottom centre: the hotbar. 8 slots of 22×22 px; the selected slot is raised and outlined, with its name and count above. L1/R1 or wheel glyphs sit at the ends.\n620\t  - Bottom left: context prompts.\n621\t  - Bottom right: pickup toasts.\n622\t  - Centre: Notion, Room, Level and Quest popups (queued, 2.5 s each).\n623\t  - Siege: the Banner HP bar and the wave label. Boss: a big HP bar with the name, phase pips and a \"TANGLED!\" flash.\n624\t  - **Fades:** the HUD fades to 30% when idle for 6 s outside combat, and returns at full opacity on any input, damage or popup.\n625\t- **Title:**\n626\t  - Behind the menu, a living diorama: the finished Thimbleton built from the attract stamp, at dusk, with a slow camera pan. The logo reads \"DRAGON QUILT BUILDERS\", each letter a patchwork fabric colour with a stitched outline and extrusion (`E.font.title`), and a needle-and-thread dragon emblem.\n627\t  - Menu (`E.Menu`, centred bottom): Continue (if a save exists), New Game, Load Game (`saves.show('load')`), Quilting Bee (solo challenge), Settings (`game.menu('settings')`), About & Credits.\n628\t  - \"Press ✕ / Enter\" prompt; a version label (`E.versionLabel()`).\n629\t  - After 10 s without input, the attract mode starts.\n630\t- **New Game:** name entry (letter grid plus keyboard typing), look A/B, 4 palettes, difficulty (Relaxed/Normal/Hard). The live rig preview turns.\n631\t- **Intro crawl:** 4 pages over the quilt void with Granny's voice and gentle music. Skippable.\n632\t- **Satchel** (Create / Tab / M / N), with tabs switched by L1/R1 or Q/E:\n633\t  - **Bag:** a category strip (Materials, Building, Furniture, Food, Tools, Key) and a 6×4 grid of large slots. Detail pane: icon at ×3, name, a Dragon Quest-style description, the count. Actions: ✕ Assign to hotbar, △ Use/Eat/Equip, □ Drop 1/All. The \"Pocket Notions\" button opens pocket crafting.\n634\t  - **Map:** described below.\n635\t  - **Journal:** active quests (giver portrait, steps with tick icons), completed ones, and the list of known Notions.\n636\t- **Map screen:**\n637\t  - The world drawn top-down at 2 px per column from top-block base colours, shaded by height. Water is blue satin; void is navy with stitched edges; unexplored areas are blank linen (fog revealed within 10 blocks as you go).\n638\t  - Markers: you (an arrow), the Banner, residents, discovered portals, quest targets, the Lost Bundle.\n639\t  - Controls: the stick pans, R2/L2 zoom, ✕ sets a waypoint marker, ○ goes back. Mouse: drag to pan, wheel to zoom, click to set a waypoint.\n640\t- **Crafting, Chest, Travel and Banner screens:** §6.5–6.9.\n641\t- **Pause menu:** the engine standard, plus Satchel, Dev Tools (hidden in hub sessions) and About & Credits. Save/Load come through `menu: { saves }` (enabled when `saves.canSave`: no monsters within 12 blocks, no siege or cutscene).\n642\t- **Results** (chapter clear): the Builder's name and a portrait card. Stats: play time, blocks placed, blocks broken, items crafted, rooms built, monsters defeated, Cheer earned. Then \"Continue to credits\".\n643\t- **Credits:** a scroll over the finale party, ending on \"To be continued... Chapter Two: The Calico Coast\" (a story teaser, not a stub) and \"Thank you for playing!\". Then back to free play in Thimbleton (`credits.onDone → play`), with all systems active.\n644\t- **About & Credits** (title menu and pause menu): pages for Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback and Licenses (§6.24).\n645\t\n646\t### 6.17 Audio (`DQ.AudioX`)\n647\t- **Music** (all original, in the engine's step sequencer format; §7.11 lists every song):\n648\t  - The director picks the song by context: title, intro, cave, field per region, town (day/night), siege, mini-boss, boss, Bee round, results, credits. It crossfades with `music(song, { fade: 1 })`.\n649\t  - **Dynamic town theme:** extra layers come in with town level (`audio.layer('strings', 1, 2)` at Lv2, `'bells'` at Lv3, `'drums'` at Lv4).\n650\t  - Jingles use `audio.sting(song, { at: 'beat' })` over ducked music.\n651\t- **SFX:** custom voices defined with `audio.define(name, voice)` (§7.12). Footsteps by top material, every 0.28 s while walking. Sound comes from code only, never files.\n652\t- **Animalese voices** (`DQ.AudioX.voice`), driven by the Dialog `onLetter` hook:\n653\t  - **Letters and pauses.** For each letter shown (skip spaces): punctuation adds a 90 ms pause, and `?` lifts the last 3 syllables by 20%.\n654\t  - **Each letter becomes one syllable**, 55–70 ms (shorter at fast text speed):\n655\t    1. A **consonant onset**:\n656\t       - s/z/c/x: highpass noise at 4 kHz, 18 ms\n657\t       - t/d/k/g/p/b/q: click (bandpass noise at 1.5 kHz, 8 ms, plus a low thump)\n658\t       - m/n/l/r/w/y/v/f/h/j: a soft voiced onset (lowpass 600 Hz)\n659\t    2. A **vowel body**: a sawtooth or pulse at the speaker's pitch × (1 + letter-hash × range), through two `BiquadFilter` bandpasses at the vowel formants. The vowel is the next vowel in the word.\n660\t\n661\t       | Vowel | F1 (Hz) | F2 (Hz) |\n662\t       |---|---|---|\n663\t       | a | 800 | 1200 |\n664\t       | e | 500 | 1900 |\n665\t       | i | 300 | 2300 |\n666\t       | o | 500 | 900 |\n667\t       | u | 350 | 800 |\n668\t\n669\t       Formants scale with the speaker's `formant` factor.\n670\t  - **Contour:** +8% at word starts, falling 6% across a sentence. ALL-CAPS words are 15% louder and higher.\n671\t  - **Determinism:** pitch jitter comes from `hash(char, index, speakerSeed)`, never `Math.random`.\n672\t  - Routed through `_voiceBus` (the \"Voices\" volume setting). Profiles are in §7.8. The Builder is silent.\n673\t  - In headless runs, voice calls are no-ops (`audio.ctx` is null).\n674\t\n675\t### 6.18 Save and load (`DQ.Save`)\n676\t- Uses `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave, with place and level labels).\n677\t- `write()` returns:\n678\t  ```\n679\t  { data: { v: 1, seed, world: world.diff(), objects: Objects.serialize(),\n680\t            builder: {...}, bag, hotbar, chests,\n681\t            town: {cheer, level, patterns, townChest},\n682\t            residents: [...], story: story.state(), quests,\n683\t            clock: {day, hour}, stats, explored (RLE),\n684\t            lostBundle, flags },\n685\t    place: regionName, level: 'Town Lv ' + level }\n686\t  ```\n687\t- `read()` regenerates the base world from the seed, then applies the diff and the objects, then recomputes rooms and the nav graph.\n688\t- **Autosave:** on `questDone`, after sleeping, at the siege checkpoint, and every 5 minutes when `canSave`.\n689\t- The title's Continue uses `saves.latest()`. `migrate(data, from)` is a stub for future versions; v1 is the only version, so implement it as identity with a version check.\n690\t- In a hub session nothing is saved; the client's storage is in-memory anyway.\n691\t\n692\t### 6.19 Dev mode (`DQ.Dev`, from the pause menu → \"Dev Tools\")\n693\tA full-screen pixel panel with tabs (L1/R1 or the mouse). Every toggle and slider takes effect immediately and is saved under `E.store('dqb-dev')`. It is hidden and disabled in hub sessions.\n694\t\n695\t| Tab | Tools |\n696\t|---|---|\n697\t| **Cheats** | God mode; Creative bag (infinite materials, every recipe known); Fly / no-clip (Space up, Shift down); Instant break; No hunger; One-hit kills; Freeze time of day; Invisible to monsters |\n698\t| **Warp** | Teleport list: Lint Hollow, Thimbleton plaza, Corduroy Crags, Button Quarry, Tweedwood Lint Camp, Calico Coast shipwreck, Frayed Verge, Knot Gate, Knotted Spire top, the Rift. Plus \"Teleport to cursor\" |\n699\t| **Spawn** | Any monster (×1/×5), either boss, any item ×1/×10/×99, any resident (arrive now) |\n700\t| **Story** | Jump to beat: Start / Banner / Lv2 / Lv3 / Lv4 / Hall built / Seam Ripper / Spire / Siege / Boss / Chapter clear. Each beat calls `DQ.Quests.applyBeat(id)`, which sets flags, quests, residents, rooms (via stamps) and inventory to a consistent state. Also: complete the current quest step, set the town level, add Cheer ±50, set the hour, start or skip a siege wave |\n701\t| **Tuning** | Live sliders (below) with **Reset to defaults** (all, or a single slider with △) |\n702\t| **Debug** | Overlays: collision cells, room detector, nav graph and NPC paths, monster aggro rings, cutaway radius, light radii, Pattern ghost status. Perf readout: frame ms, queued runs, actors, lights. Time scale 0.25×–4×. Frame step (while paused, ✕ advances 1 step). Cutaway auto/always/off. Hub net stats (msgs/s, bytes), shown only in Bee solo/loopback |\n703\t| **World** | Export a stamp: mark two corners with the cursor, then copy JSON to the clipboard and offer a download. Save and load a dev snapshot. Regenerate the world |\n704\t\n705\t**Sliders** (`DQ.TUNING_DEFS`: key, label, min, max, step, default):\n706\t\n707\t| Slider | Default | Range |\n708\t|---|---|---|\n709\t| Walk speed | 78 | 40–140 |\n710\t| Sprint multiplier | 1.45 | 1–2.5 |\n711\t| Jump velocity | 215 | 150–320 |\n712\t| Gravity | 800 | 400–1400 |\n713\t| Reach (blocks) | 4.5 | 2–8 |\n714\t| Builder attack × | 1.0 | 0.25–4 |\n715\t| Block damage × | 1.0 | 0.25–5 |\n716\t| Max HP base | 40 | 10–200 |\n717\t| Belly drain × | 1.0 | 0–4 |\n718\t| Monster HP × | 1.0 | 0.25–4 |\n719\t| Monster damage × | 1.0 | 0–4 |\n720\t| Monster speed × | 1.0 | 0.5–2 |\n721\t| Aggro radius (blocks) | 8 | 2–20 |\n722\t| Max monsters | 10 | 0–40 |\n723\t| Spawn interval night (s) | 5 | 1–30 |\n724\t| Day length (min) | 12 | 2–60 |\n725\t| Cheer × | 1.0 | 0.25–5 |\n726\t| Drop rate × | 1.0 | 0–5 |\n727\t| Siege wave size × | 1.0 | 0.25–3 |\n728\t| Helper build rate (blocks/min) | 6 | 0–60 |\n729\t| Ballista reload (s) | 2.5 | 0.5–6 |\n730\t| Tangle window (s) | 8 | 2–20 |\n731\t\n732\tGameplay code reads `DQ.tuning.get(key)` every time (no cached copies), so sliders are live.\n733\t\n734\t### 6.20 Attract mode (`DQ.Attract`)\n735\t- **Start and exit.** It starts after 10 s without input on the title screen or its menus (main menu, Load list, About). It does not start on the Settings screen or during name entry, where the player is busy choosing. **Any input exits it** to the title with a fade: any key, mouse button, mouse movement over 8 px, gamepad button, or stick past 0.5. On touch-only devices it also runs, and a tap exits.\n736\t- **Isolation.** It builds its own `ctx` with a separate world (generated from the seed, plus `stampDemoTown()`: a pre-built Lv4 Thimbleton with rooms, the Hall, ballistas and residents). It never touches the player's save or settings. Sound plays at 60% volume, if unlocked.\n737\t- **The AI builder** is `DQ.Autopilot` running the vignettes below with cheats: invulnerable, infinite materials, placement at 0.15 s per block, teleporting between vignettes behind a wipe transition.\n738\t- **Overlay:** a small logo top left, \"DEMO\" top right (below the corner area), and a blinking \"Press any button\" with the current device's glyph.\n739\t- **Vignettes**, looping forever with a 4 s logo card between loops (each written as a `game.script` and also run by a test):\n740\t\n741\t| # | Vignette | Length |\n742\t|---|---|---|\n743\t| 1 | \"Morning in Thimbleton\": camera glide; residents at their jobs; banner flutter | 12 s |\n744\t| 2 | \"Gathering\": breaks turf and tufts in the Glen; pickups; a Notion popup | 14 s |\n745\t| 3 | \"Crafting\": opens the Mending Bench menu (scripted focus moves) and crafts a Straw Bed | 10 s |\n746\t| 4 | \"Raising a room\": walls 2 high, door, bed, torch, then \"ROOM COMPLETE! Bedroom\" and Cheer bubbles | 24 s |\n747\t| 5 | \"Skirmish\": a combo and a Spin Stitch against Lintlings and a Pinhog; drops | 16 s |\n748\t| 6 | \"Nightfall\": the hour jumps to 21:00; lanterns glow; Mothlets; residents go to bed | 10 s |\n749\t| 7 | \"Siege\": a wave at the walls; ballista fire; Mortimer fights; a Knotbrute smashes a wall | 18 s |\n750\t| 8 | \"Gnarlgrim\": Gnarlgrim at 30% HP; manned ballista hits → TANGLED → Seam Ripper strike → he unravels; confetti | 16 s |\n751\t| 9 | \"Quilting Bee\": 3 bot builders in seat colours raise the Quilt Barn on the Bee world | 10 s |\n752\t\n753\t### 6.21 Multiplayer: AI Hub sessions and the Quilting Bee (`DQ.Net`, `DQ.Bee`)\n754\t**Mode:** `shared-world` (co-op building is the source's multiplayer), 1–4 players, 8-minute rounds. Head tags, written by `build.mjs`:\n755\t```html\n756\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n757\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n758\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n759\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n760\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Raise the Quilt Barn together, then defend it\">\n761\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move stick/WASD · Jump ✕/Space · Break □/Click · Place △/Right-click\">\n762\t```\n763\tAlso include a description meta and `hub:type`, plus `hub:players` \"1–4\", following the example pages' catalogue tags. `session.js` (unmodified, between its banner and last line) is the first script after `<meta charset>`.\n764\t\n765\t**Session flow** (only when `AIHub.active`; otherwise nothing changes):\n766\t1. No title, attract, menus or saves. Boot straight into `bee` with the Bee world generated (fixed seed `0xBEE` plus the Bee stamp; identical on every copy).\n767\t2. `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, fall back to the normal game (title).\n768\t3. The **game's own card** (`hubcard` scene):\n769\t   - The logo, the players lined up as builders in seat colours (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`; names drawn with the pixel font, never inserted as HTML), the goal, this player's control glyphs, ready ticks, and the countdown from the `card` event (`left`).\n770\t   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a click → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **More time:** △, T or a click → `AIHub.answer('more')` (a second press takes it back).\n771\t   - Nothing here changes the round. Any card randomness uses `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n772\t4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built (no key press).\n773\t5. On `start`: a 3-2-1 countdown while `AIHub.time() < 0`. Play begins when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`.\n774\t6. **Round clock:** 8:00, or `limitMs` if shorter.\n775\t   - **Build phase** (5:00): raise the Quilt Barn Pattern, scaled by player count:\n776\t\n777\t     | Players | Barn walls | Blocks |\n778\t     |---|---|---|\n779\t     | 1 | 2 high | 38 |\n780\t     | 2 | 3 high | 57 |\n781\t     | 3–4 | 3 high + 10 Felt crenellations | 67 |\n782\t\n783\t     Plus a door and 2 torches.\n784\t   - **Raid phase** (3:00): 3 waves from the corners. Knotbrutes target the barn and the Banner (HP 200).\n785\t7. **Scores** (per player):\n786\t   - +3 per Pattern block placed (the host credits the placer)\n787\t   - +5 per monster defeated (Knotbrute +15)\n788\t   - +5 per door or torch crafted and placed in the Pattern\n789\t   - +1 per 5 items gathered\n790\t8. **Host ends the round.** At the time limit, on `time-up` (within `graceMs`), or when every player has left, the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats })`:\n791\t   - `standings`: arrays of ids by score, ties grouped.\n792\t   - `won`: the Pattern is complete and the Banner HP > 0.\n793\t   - `stats`: per id `{ Blocks, Monsters }`.\n794\t   - Awards: \"Master Quilter\" for the most blocks, \"Knot Cutter\" for the most kills.\n795\t9. On `end`: stop input, `audio.mute(true)` and `music(null)`, show \"Round over\", then do nothing more. On `leave`: remove that builder (its placed blocks stay). In **server mode** (`AIHub.server`): run the host simulation with no local builder, camera or input, and skip drawing except a 1-fps static \"Hosting the Bee\" frame.\n796\t10. **The round never pauses.** Build the game with `autoPause: false`, `corner: false` and `menu: false` when `AIHub.active`, and make the `bee` scene `pausable: false` in a session. Options/Esc only show the toast \"Round in progress!\". There are no settings menus mid-round, and settings are at their defaults in a session, because the hub gives the game empty storage.\n797\t11. **A hidden tab keeps the world running.** `requestAnimationFrame` stops in hidden tabs, so while `document.hidden`, a `setInterval` of 250 ms calls `game.advance(elapsed)` (capped at 1 s per call). The host keeps simulating and every copy keeps sending; the hub voids a round only after 20 s hidden.\n798\t12. **Names** come from the hub and are drawn with the pixel font. Characters it lacks become `?`. They are never inserted as HTML.\n799\t\n800\t**Authority and messages.** Every copy runs the voxel world locally and keeps it in sync through edits. The host owns monsters, drops, Pattern progress, the clock and scores. Each client owns its own builder's movement, inventory and hotbar.\n801\t\n802\t| Msg | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Payload (compact arrays, integers) |\n803\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n804\t| `p` | client → host | no | 10 Hz | `[t, x, y, z, facing×100, anim, heldItem, hp]` |\n805\t| `a` | client → host | yes | ≤ 6 Hz, batched | `ops: [['place', x,y,z, block, rot], ['break', x,y,z], ['hit', monId, dmg, kx, ky], ['take', dropId], ['craft', item]]` |\n806\t| `s` | host → all | no | 10 Hz | `{ t, P: [[id,x,y,z,f,anim,held,hp]...], M: [[id,kind,x,y,z,f,hp,state]...], ph, left, prog, bhp }`, kept under 1,100 bytes (if more than 24 monsters, alternate halves) |\n807\t| `e` | host → all | yes | ≤ 6 Hz, batched | `ev: [['vox', x,y,z, id, by], ['drop', id, item, n, x,y,z], ['gone', dropId], ['got', to, item, n], ['hurt', to, dmg, kx, ky], ['fx', kind, x,y,z], ['phase', name], ['score', id, n]]` |\n808\t\n809\t- Per copy that is ≤ 16 messages/s, under the 20/s cap. Every payload stays far below 16 KB; assert this in tests.\n810\t- **Prediction:** a client applies its own place/break immediately and marks the cell pending; the host's `vox` event confirms or corrects it. Monsters on clients interpolate between snapshots (100 ms buffer).\n811\t- **Hits:** a client sends `hit` when its local swing overlaps a monster's interpolated position, and the host applies damage. Old or out-of-order snapshots are dropped by `t`.\n812\t- **Networking goes only through `AIHub.send`/`on`.** No sockets, fetch, `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. \"Quit to title\" does nothing in a session.\n813\t\n814\t**Outside the hub (the game on its own).** The title's **Quilting Bee** runs the same round solo: the local copy is the host, with a `LoopbackNet` that implements the same `send`/`on` surface in process. Optionally 1–3 **bot builders** run on `DQ.Autopilot` (\"Bee with friends: bots on/off\"). This exercises the host code paths outside the hub. Best scores go to `E.store`.\n815\t\n816\t### 6.22 Touch-only devices\n817\tDetection: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, and no gamepad seen and no `keydown` yet. Re-evaluate when a pad connects or a key is pressed.\n818\t\n819\tOn such devices:\n820\t- Every scene has `touch: []` and `input.touchEnabled = false`: **no touch controls**.\n821\t- The title shows a stitched panel, \"**Controller or keyboard required**\", with the line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\" The engine's corner **settings/menu button** stays (`corner` on).\n822\t- The attract mode runs as usual, and a tap returns to the title panel.\n823\t\n824\t### 6.23 Settings and accessibility (additions to the standard Settings)\n825\t| Setting | Default |\n826\t|---|---|\n827\t| Button glyphs | PlayStation, or Xbox (sets `input.glyphs`) |\n828\t| Camera view | Isometric, or Three-quarter |\n829\t| Auto-hop | On |\n830\t| Sprint | Hold, or Toggle |\n831\t| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast |\n832\t| Voices volume | 80% |\n833\t| HUD tracker | On |\n834\t| Difficulty | Normal (Relaxed / Hard) |\n835\t| Cutaway | Auto (Always, Off) |\n836\t| Screen shake and flashes | Engine standard |\n837\t\n838\tReduce motion: the engine handles it; it also disables the camera crossfade and the confetti density.\n839\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"e94e2622-009a-49b9-a4bf-3d81e30955c3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:55.234Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"  - **Marigold** (cook): with a Kitchen, cooks at the Hearth Pot (stirring loop) twice a day from Town Chest ingredients into the chest. At 18:00 she sets a dish on the Mess Hall table. In sieges she throws hot pies (5 damage, arc).\n  - **Professor Selvage** (helper): builds Patterns from the Town Chest at the helper rate, or reads in the Workshop. In sieges he hides in the Hall.\n  - **Lintwick** (fluff-farmer): puts 2 Lint into the Town Chest daily and dances (a Blob hop loop) when happy. In sieges he rolls into monsters (3 damage + knockback).\n- **Needs and Cheer bubbles.** At most once per day per need, each satisfied need spawns a floating pink heart bubble (+5 Cheer) over the resident, which stays until collected:\n  - sleep: slept in a bed\n  - meal: ate a dish\n  - comfort: their favourite room exists (Wren: Bedroom, Mortimer: Guard Post, Marigold: Kitchen, Professor: Workshop, Lintwick: a Bedroom with a Felt block in its walls)\n\n  Collect a bubble by walking within 2 blocks of it. Unhappy residents show a `dots` balloon and say why when you talk to them.\n- **Requests:** a resident with an available quest shows a bouncing \"!\" balloon (`story.emote`). Talking starts it, and its steps appear in the Journal and HUD. When the steps are done, a \"?\" balloon shows; talk to them to turn it in.\n- **Arrival cutscene:** the resident walks in along the east road, the camera pans to them, and they say their intro line. \"Mortimer has moved into Thimbleton!\" shows with a jingle.\n- **Navigation** (`DQ.Nav`):\n  - **Graph:** nodes are standable `(x, y, L)`. Edges:\n    - 8-neighbour moves (diagonals only if both orthogonal neighbours are open), cost 1 (diagonal 1.41)\n    - step up 1 level (a hop), cost 2\n    - drop down 1–3 levels, cost 1.5\n    - doors open for residents, closed for monsters\n  - **A\\*** with a binary heap, capped at 3,000 expanded nodes. Smooth paths by line-of-walk. Re-path when an edit touches a path cell.\n  - **Stuck rule:** if a resident has not progressed for 8 s and is off-screen, teleport them to the target. On screen, try a hop, then re-path.\n- **Talk:** dialog with a portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) and the resident's voice. Lines vary by flags, time of day, mood and town level (`E.Story` nodes with `if` conditions).\n\n### 6.11 Monsters and combat (`DQ.Monsters`, `DQ.Combat`)\n- **AI states:** `idle/wander → notice` (a \"!\" over the head plus a squeak, 0.3 s) `→ chase → windup` (telegraph: flash, crouch or squash, a sound) `→ attack → recover`. Then `→ flee` (below 20% HP for Lintlings) or `→ hurt` (stagger 0.25 s) `→ dead` (pop, particles, drops, `monsterKilled`).\n  - Aggro uses radius `tuning.aggro`, scaled by type (§7.9), plus `world.raycast` sight from eye height.\n  - Leash: return home after chasing 24 blocks away from home.\n- **Spawning:**\n  - Region tables (§7.1) by day or night. Spawn on standable cells under open sky, ≥ 10 blocks from the builder, outside the town border, never inside rooms or during cutscenes.\n  - Rate: 1 spawn per `tuning.spawnEvery` s (day 8, night 5) while the active count is below `tuning.maxMonsters` (default 10).\n  - Despawn: more than 40 blocks away for 20 s.\n- **Damage:**\n  - `dmg = max(1, round((atk − def/2) × U(0.9, 1.1)))`, where U is drawn from the combat stream.\n  - Builder crits: 5%, ×1.5 (Spin Stitch never crits).\n  - Multipliers: `tuning.monsterHp`, `tuning.monsterDmg`, `tuning.builderAtk`, and difficulty (Relaxed 0.5 damage taken, Normal 1, Hard 1.4).\n- **Hit feedback:**\n  - `game.hitFx(x,y,z,{ power, damage, angle })` (hit-stop, shake, impact star, damage number), plus `E.knockback(builder, mon, 120, 40)`.\n  - Monster hits on the builder: knockback 90, i-frames 0.8 s, a red vignette flash under `game.flash` limits.\n  - Each move has its own sound.\n- **Drops:** rolled on death from the drop table (`tuning.dropRate` multiplier on chances); items fly out.\n\n### 6.12 Siege and bosses (`DQ.Siege`, `DQ.Bosses`)\n- **Siege director** (used once in the story, M13–M14, and in the Bee round). It is a `game.script` generator:\n  1. **Prep.** Mortimer's rally line, then a 90 s countdown banner (\"The Knotted army approaches! 1:30\"). Build defences meanwhile; the music turns tense with the drum layer.\n  2. **Autosave checkpoint** `siege`.\n  3. **Waves** W1 → W2 → W3 (§7.9). Each wave spawns over 10 s from the east road (96,76), the Rift (96,80) and the north path (72,52). It ends when all of its monsters are defeated. Between waves: a 25 s breather with \"Wave cleared!\" and a repair prompt.\n  4. **Boss.** Gnarlgrim enters through the Rift (cutscene, §7.10).\n- **Monster targets in sieges:** first the Banner (HP 300; its HP bar is on the HUD during the siege), then ballistas, then the nearest town-structure block in the way (flagged `town` when placed inside the border), then residents, then the builder.\n  - Monsters path with **breaker A\\***: wall blocks count as passable at cost 8 per block, and doors at cost 4.\n  - On reaching a blocking block or door, a monster attacks it (Lintling 3, Pinhog 6, Frayed Knight 8, Knotbrute 25, Gnarlgrim 60 block damage per hit).\n- **Fail:** the Banner falls, or the builder is KO'd while Gnarlgrim is active. Then \"The Banner has fallen...\" / \"You've come undone...\", and a choice: \"Try again from the start of the siege\" (reload the checkpoint) or \"Return to title\". Waves already cleared stay cleared only within a single attempt.\n- **Sir Buttonsworth** (mini-boss, Button Quarry floor):\n  - Intro: he rises from a heap of buttons.\n  - Moves:\n    - **Slam:** wind .6 s; a shockwave ring of radius 3 blocks expands over .5 s. Jump to avoid it; it deals 12.\n    - **Button Volley:** wind .4 s; 5 buttons in a 50° spread (`E.Bullets`, 110 u/s, 8 damage).\n    - **Stomp Charge:** wind .7 s; charges 140 u/s toward the builder, breaks blocks in its path, and is dizzy for 2 s after hitting a wall. Dizzy takes double damage.\n  - Below 50% HP he summons 3 Lintlings once.\n  - The arena has 4 cobble pillars that break under charges.\n  - Defeat: he pops into buttons and drops the Golden Needle and 3 Steel Thread.\n- **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** (final boss, in and around the Thimbleton plaza), HP 600 in three phases (100–66%, 66–33%, 33–0%):\n  - **Tightly wound.** Def 25, so normal hits do about 1 damage. Mortimer and Granny hint \"Use the Ballistas!\" after 3 such hits.\n  - **Tangled.** 2 manned-ballista hits within 8 s, or 1 hit during his charge, make him Tangled for 5 s: he sits in a heap with `down: .6`, his chest **Heart Knot** glows, and his def drops to 0.\n    - Hits on the Heart Knot (front arc) with the Seam Ripper do ×4, other weapons ×2.\n    - A stagger plays at 100 damage per Tangle; leaving the Tangle triggers a roar knockback.\n  - **Phase 1:** Yarn Slam (ring, radius 3.5) and Tangle Toss (lobbed yarn ball via `E.arc`, landing in 1.1 s on a shadow telegraph; 10 damage and leaves a temporary Tangle block for 20 s).\n  - **Phase 2:** adds Charge (breaks blocks in its path and targets a ballista) and summons 4 Lintlings at the phase start.\n  - **Phase 3:** all moves 25% faster, a double Tangle Toss, and a Knotbrute summon.\n  - Phase transitions: a roar (`shout` expression) and a knockback ring; the music switches to the next layer.\n  - Defeat cutscene: he unravels into heaps of yarn (thread particles) and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner. The rift heals (§7.10).\n\n### 6.13 Day, night, lighting, weather (`DQ.Clock`)\n- One day = `tuning.dayMinutes` (12) real minutes; the story starts on Day 1 at 08:00.\n- **Phases:** dawn 05–07, day 07–17, dusk 17–19, night 19–05.\n- `game.lights.enabled = true` always. `ambient` follows the hour: night .30 with a cool blue tint, dawn and dusk .65 with a warm tint, day 1.0. Use `lights.tint`, setting `lights.dark` per phase, then `lights.refresh()`.\n- Light sources add light pools (§6.7). At night, stars twinkle in the void, Mothlets spawn and Frayed Knights roam the Rift.\n- **HUD clock:** a sun/moon dial with \"Day 3\".\n- **Weather (cosmetic, engine `game.weather`):** the Fraying always has `ash` (purple tint). The Glen rains lightly some days (Day 2 afternoon, Day 4 morning). Weather resets per region when it changes.\n- **Sleeping** is in §6.7. **Night-time Granny line:** the first night she warns \"Monsters get bolder after dark, dearie. A lit room is a safe room!\"\n\n### 6.14 Health and hunger\n- The HUD shows HP as a red patch bar with numbers (\"HP 32/40\") and Belly as a bread-loaf bar.\n- Low HP (< 25%) adds a heartbeat sfx and a red vignette (follows the reduce-flash setting).\n- Food is in §7.3. Eating restores Belly and HP; raw Thimbleberries restore Belly +5.\n- Starving: HP −1 every 4 s, with the prompt \"Your belly is empty! Eat something!\"\n\n### 6.15 Story, quests, dialog, cutscenes (`DQ.Quests`, `DQ.Cutscenes`)\n- **Engine pieces:** `E.Story` (story module) runs conversations as data nodes, with `who`, `say`, `choices`, `set`, `quest`, `done`, `emote` and `event`. One `E.Dialog` instance is skinned as a Dragon Quest-style box: a dark indigo panel with a cream stitched border (dashed 1-px line 2 px inside the edge), a name tab, a portrait at the left, typed text with Animalese blips, and a bobbing arrow sprite at page end (the font has no ▼).\n- **Granny Gossamer's box:** a golden stitched border with gold text and a glowing spool portrait (a custom portrait function).\n- **Text:** 3 lines per page, at most 52 characters per line, `E.font` scale 1 (≈ 31 px tall on a 1080p TV).\n- **Quest data** (§7.10): `{ id, title, giver, steps: [{ text, done: condition }], reward, next, unlock }`. Conditions are data:\n  - `{ have: {item: n} }`, `{ crafted: id }`, `{ placed: objId }`, `{ room: type }`, `{ level: n }`, `{ talk: npc }`\n  - `{ killed: {monster: n} }`, `{ at: poi, radius }`, `{ pattern: id }`, `{ flag: k }`, `{ siegeDone: true }`, `{ boss: id }`\n- **Quest director:** evaluates the current steps on relevant events (cheap) and once per second as a fallback. It advances steps and emits `questStep`/`questDone`. Rewards: `{ cheer, items, notions, flags, heartpatch }`. HUD: \"Quest complete: Wren's Bed\" with a jingle.\n- **Objective tracker** (top centre; switch it off per quest with Track on/off in the Journal, or entirely with the HUD tracker setting): the quest title, the current step text, and a marker. The marker is the engine's `r.marker(x,y,z,{label})`, which becomes an edge arrow off screen, with the distance in blocks. Targets: the POI, NPC or Pattern from the step, or for gather steps the nearest matching plant or block within 40 blocks (scanned once per second).\n- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens on a proxy, dialog awaits (`yield E.until(() => !talk.open)`), NPC walks (autopilot), and effects.\n  - Skip: hold ○, Esc or right click for 1 s (a fill ring shows) to jump to the end state.\n  - Every cutscene has `apply()`, which sets its end state. Skipping and tests call it.\n- **Writing style** (Dragon Quest-like):\n  - Short, punchy lines; exclamations; earnest heroism softened with jokes; sewing puns; NPCs with verbal tics.\n  - The silent Builder answers only through choices (\"Of course!\" / \"What's a bed?\").\n  - System lines are cheerful: \"You got 3 Straw!\", \"Thimbleton is now Level 2!\", \"A Lintling bounces into view!\"\n  - Avoid modern slang. Keep it family-friendly. Never reuse Dragon Quest names, places or iconic phrases verbatim.\n\n### 6.16 UI screens and HUD (10-foot, controller first; `DQ.Hud`, `DQ.Menus`)\nAll UI is pixel art drawn with `E.ui`, `E.font` and `px` inside `r.overlay`. Panels are dark felt (`E.ui.box` gradient `#2a2350 → #1a1636`) with stitched cream borders. Text is at least scale 1 at 240p; headers scale 2; the title logo scale 3–4. At most about 6–8 entries per screen and generous spacing: no dense tables. Information is never conveyed by colour alone (icons plus text).\n\n- **HUD (in play):**\n  - Top left: HP bar, Belly bar, and the equipped weapon icon.\n  - Top centre: the objective tracker.\n  - Top right, *below* `game.cornerArea()`: the clock dial with the day, and the Banner badge (level, Cheer bar).\n  - Bottom centre: the hotbar. 8 slots of 22×22 px; the selected slot is raised and outlined, with its name and count above. L1/R1 or wheel glyphs sit at the ends.\n  - Bottom left: context prompts.\n  - Bottom right: pickup toasts.\n  - Centre: Notion, Room, Level and Quest popups (queued, 2.5 s each).\n  - Siege: the Banner HP bar and the wave label. Boss: a big HP bar with the name, phase pips and a \"TANGLED!\" flash.\n  - **Fades:** the HUD fades to 30% when idle for 6 s outside combat, and returns at full opacity on any input, damage or popup.\n- **Title:**\n  - Behind the menu, a living diorama: the finished Thimbleton built from the attract stamp, at dusk, with a slow camera pan. The logo reads \"DRAGON QUILT BUILDERS\", each letter a patchwork fabric colour with a stitched outline and extrusion (`E.font.title`), and a needle-and-thread dragon emblem.\n  - Menu (`E.Menu`, centred bottom): Continue (if a save exists), New Game, Load Game (`saves.show('load')`), Quilting Bee (solo challenge), Settings (`game.menu('settings')`), About & Credits.\n  - \"Press ✕ / Enter\" prompt; a version label (`E.versionLabel()`).\n  - After 10 s without input, the attract mode starts.\n- **New Game:** name entry (letter grid plus keyboard typing), look A/B, 4 palettes, difficulty (Relaxed/Normal/Hard). The live rig preview turns.\n- **Intro crawl:** 4 pages over the quilt void with Granny's voice and gentle music. Skippable.\n- **Satchel** (Create / Tab / M / N), with tabs switched by L1/R1 or Q/E:\n  - **Bag:** a category strip (Materials, Building, Furniture, Food, Tools, Key) and a 6×4 grid of large slots. Detail pane: icon at ×3, name, a Dragon Quest-style description, the count. Actions: ✕ Assign to hotbar, △ Use/Eat/Equip, □ Drop 1/All. The \"Pocket Notions\" button opens pocket crafting.\n  - **Map:** described below.\n  - **Journal:** active quests (giver portrait, steps with tick icons), completed ones, and the list of known Notions.\n- **Map screen:**\n  - The world drawn top-down at 2 px per column from top-block base colours, shaded by height. Water is blue satin; void is navy with stitched edges; unexplored areas are blank linen (fog revealed within 10 blocks as you go).\n  - Markers: you (an arrow), the Banner, residents, discovered portals, quest targets, the Lost Bundle.\n  - Controls: the stick pans, R2/L2 zoom, ✕ sets a waypoint marker, ○ goes back. Mouse: drag to pan, wheel to zoom, click to set a waypoint.\n- **Crafting, Chest, Travel and Banner screens:** §6.5–6.9.\n- **Pause menu:** the engine standard, plus Satchel, Dev Tools (hidden in hub sessions) and About & Credits. Save/Load come through `menu: { saves }` (enabled when `saves.canSave`: no monsters within 12 blocks, no siege or cutscene).\n- **Results** (chapter clear): the Builder's name and a portrait card. Stats: play time, blocks placed, blocks broken, items crafted, rooms built, monsters defeated, Cheer earned. Then \"Continue to credits\".\n- **Credits:** a scroll over the finale party, ending on \"To be continued... Chapter Two: The Calico Coast\" (a story teaser, not a stub) and \"Thank you for playing!\". Then back to free play in Thimbleton (`credits.onDone → play`), with all systems active.\n- **About & Credits** (title menu and pause menu): pages for Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback and Licenses (§6.24).\n\n### 6.17 Audio (`DQ.AudioX`)\n- **Music** (all original, in the engine's step sequencer format; §7.11 lists every song):\n  - The director picks the song by context: title, intro, cave, field per region, town (day/night), siege, mini-boss, boss, Bee round, results, credits. It crossfades with `music(song, { fade: 1 })`.\n  - **Dynamic town theme:** extra layers come in with town level (`audio.layer('strings', 1, 2)` at Lv2, `'bells'` at Lv3, `'drums'` at Lv4).\n  - Jingles use `audio.sting(song, { at: 'beat' })` over ducked music.\n- **SFX:** custom voices defined with `audio.define(name, voice)` (§7.12). Footsteps by top material, every 0.28 s while walking. Sound comes from code only, never files.\n- **Animalese voices** (`DQ.AudioX.voice`), driven by the Dialog `onLetter` hook:\n  - **Letters and pauses.** For each letter shown (skip spaces): punctuation adds a 90 ms pause, and `?` lifts the last 3 syllables by 20%.\n  - **Each letter becomes one syllable**, 55–70 ms (shorter at fast text speed):\n    1. A **consonant onset**:\n       - s/z/c/x: highpass noise at 4 kHz, 18 ms\n       - t/d/k/g/p/b/q: click (bandpass noise at 1.5 kHz, 8 ms, plus a low thump)\n       - m/n/l/r/w/y/v/f/h/j: a soft voiced onset (lowpass 600 Hz)\n    2. A **vowel body**: a sawtooth or pulse at the speaker's pitch × (1 + letter-hash × range), through two `BiquadFilter` bandpasses at the vowel formants. The vowel is the next vowel in the word.\n\n       | Vowel | F1 (Hz) | F2 (Hz) |\n       |---|---|---|\n       | a | 800 | 1200 |\n       | e | 500 | 1900 |\n       | i | 300 | 2300 |\n       | o | 500 | 900 |\n       | u | 350 | 800 |\n\n       Formants scale with the speaker's `formant` factor.\n  - **Contour:** +8% at word starts, falling 6% across a sentence. ALL-CAPS words are 15% louder and higher.\n  - **Determinism:** pitch jitter comes from `hash(char, index, speakerSeed)`, never `Math.random`.\n  - Routed through `_voiceBus` (the \"Voices\" volume setting). Profiles are in §7.8. The Builder is silent.\n  - In headless runs, voice calls are no-ops (`audio.ctx` is null).\n\n### 6.18 Save and load (`DQ.Save`)\n- Uses `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave, with place and level labels).\n- `write()` returns:\n  ```\n  { data: { v: 1, seed, world: world.diff(), objects: Objects.serialize(),\n            builder: {...}, bag, hotbar, chests,\n            town: {cheer, level, patterns, townChest},\n            residents: [...], story: story.state(), quests,\n            clock: {day, hour}, stats, explored (RLE),\n            lostBundle, flags },\n    place: regionName, level: 'Town Lv ' + level }\n  ```\n- `read()` regenerates the base world from the seed, then applies the diff and the objects, then recomputes rooms and the nav graph.\n- **Autosave:** on `questDone`, after sleeping, at the siege checkpoint, and every 5 minutes when `canSave`.\n- The title's Continue uses `saves.latest()`. `migrate(data, from)` is a stub for future versions; v1 is the only version, so implement it as identity with a version check.\n- In a hub session nothing is saved; the client's storage is in-memory anyway.\n\n### 6.19 Dev mode (`DQ.Dev`, from the pause menu → \"Dev Tools\")\nA full-screen pixel panel with tabs (L1/R1 or the mouse). Every toggle and slider takes effect immediately and is saved under `E.store('dqb-dev')`. It is hidden and disabled in hub sessions.\n\n| Tab | Tools |\n|---|---|\n| **Cheats** | God mode; Creative bag (infinite materials, every recipe known); Fly / no-clip (Space up, Shift down); Instant break; No hunger; One-hit kills; Freeze time of day; Invisible to monsters |\n| **Warp** | Teleport list: Lint Hollow, Thimbleton plaza, Corduroy Crags, Button Quarry, Tweedwood Lint Camp, Calico Coast shipwreck, Frayed Verge, Knot Gate, Knotted Spire top, the Rift. Plus \"Teleport to cursor\" |\n| **Spawn** | Any monster (×1/×5), either boss, any item ×1/×10/×99, any resident (arrive now) |\n| **Story** | Jump to beat: Start / Banner / Lv2 / Lv3 / Lv4 / Hall built / Seam Ripper / Spire / Siege / Boss / Chapter clear. Each beat calls `DQ.Quests.applyBeat(id)`, which sets flags, quests, residents, rooms (via stamps) and inventory to a consistent state. Also: complete the current quest step, set the town level, add Cheer ±50, set the hour, start or skip a siege wave |\n| **Tuning** | Live sliders (below) with **Reset to defaults** (all, or a single slider with △) |\n| **Debug** | Overlays: collision cells, room detector, nav graph and NPC paths, monster aggro rings, cutaway radius, light radii, Pattern ghost status. Perf readout: frame ms, queued runs, actors, lights. Time scale 0.25×–4×. Frame step (while paused, ✕ advances 1 step). Cutaway auto/always/off. Hub net stats (msgs/s, bytes), shown only in Bee solo/loopback |\n| **World** | Export a stamp: mark two corners with the cursor, then copy JSON to the clipboard and offer a download. Save and load a dev snapshot. Regenerate the world |\n\n**Sliders** (`DQ.TUNING_DEFS`: key, label, min, max, step, default):\n\n| Slider | Default | Range |\n|---|---|---|\n| Walk speed | 78 | 40–140 |\n| Sprint multiplier | 1.45 | 1–2.5 |\n| Jump velocity | 215 | 150–320 |\n| Gravity | 800 | 400–1400 |\n| Reach (blocks) | 4.5 | 2–8 |\n| Builder attack × | 1.0 | 0.25–4 |\n| Block damage × | 1.0 | 0.25–5 |\n| Max HP base | 40 | 10–200 |\n| Belly drain × | 1.0 | 0–4 |\n| Monster HP × | 1.0 | 0.25–4 |\n| Monster damage × | 1.0 | 0–4 |\n| Monster speed × | 1.0 | 0.5–2 |\n| Aggro radius (blocks) | 8 | 2–20 |\n| Max monsters | 10 | 0–40 |\n| Spawn interval night (s) | 5 | 1–30 |\n| Day length (min) | 12 | 2–60 |\n| Cheer × | 1.0 | 0.25–5 |\n| Drop rate × | 1.0 | 0–5 |\n| Siege wave size × | 1.0 | 0.25–3 |\n| Helper build rate (blocks/min) | 6 | 0–60 |\n| Ballista reload (s) | 2.5 | 0.5–6 |\n| Tangle window (s) | 8 | 2–20 |\n\nGameplay code reads `DQ.tuning.get(key)` every time (no cached copies), so sliders are live.\n\n### 6.20 Attract mode (`DQ.Attract`)\n- **Start and exit.** It starts after 10 s without input on the title screen or its menus (main menu, Load list, About). It does not start on the Settings screen or during name entry, where the player is busy choosing. **Any input exits it** to the title with a fade: any key, mouse button, mouse movement over 8 px, gamepad button, or stick past 0.5. On touch-only devices it also runs, and a tap exits.\n- **Isolation.** It builds its own `ctx` with a separate world (generated from the seed, plus `stampDemoTown()`: a pre-built Lv4 Thimbleton with rooms, the Hall, ballistas and residents). It never touches the player's save or settings. Sound plays at 60% volume, if unlocked.\n- **The AI builder** is `DQ.Autopilot` running the vignettes below with cheats: invulnerable, infinite materials, placement at 0.15 s per block, teleporting between vignettes behind a wipe transition.\n- **Overlay:** a small logo top left, \"DEMO\" top right (below the corner area), and a blinking \"Press any button\" with the current device's glyph.\n- **Vignettes**, looping forever with a 4 s logo card between loops (each written as a `game.script` and also run by a test):\n\n| # | Vignette | Length |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"Morning in Thimbleton\": camera glide; residents at their jobs; banner flutter | 12 s |\n| 2 | \"Gathering\": breaks turf and tufts in the Glen; pickups; a Notion popup | 14 s |\n| 3 | \"Crafting\": opens the Mending Bench menu (scripted focus moves) and crafts a Straw Bed | 10 s |\n| 4 | \"Raising a room\": walls 2 high, door, bed, torch, then \"ROOM COMPLETE! Bedroom\" and Cheer bubbles | 24 s |\n| 5 | \"Skirmish\": a combo and a Spin Stitch against Lintlings and a Pinhog; drops | 16 s |\n| 6 | \"Nightfall\": the hour jumps to 21:00; lanterns glow; Mothlets; residents go to bed | 10 s |\n| 7 | \"Siege\": a wave at the walls; ballista fire; Mortimer fights; a Knotbrute smashes a wall | 18 s |\n| 8 | \"Gnarlgrim\": Gnarlgrim at 30% HP; manned ballista hits → TANGLED → Seam Ripper strike → he unravels; confetti | 16 s |\n| 9 | \"Quilting Bee\": 3 bot builders in seat colours raise the Quilt Barn on the Bee world | 10 s |\n\n### 6.21 Multiplayer: AI Hub sessions and the Quilting Bee (`DQ.Net`, `DQ.Bee`)\n**Mode:** `shared-world` (co-op building is the source's multiplayer), 1–4 players, 8-minute rounds. Head tags, written by `build.mjs`:\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Raise the Quilt Barn together, then defend it\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move stick/WASD · Jump ✕/Space · Break □/Click · Place △/Right-click\">\n```\nAlso include a description meta and `hub:type`, plus `hub:players` \"1–4\", following the example pages' catalogue tags. `session.js` (unmodified, between its banner and last line) is the first script after `<meta charset>`.\n\n**Session flow** (only when `AIHub.active`; otherwise nothing changes):\n1. No title, attract, menus or saves. Boot straight into `bee` with the Bee world generated (fixed seed `0xBEE` plus the Bee stamp; identical on every copy).\n2. `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, fall back to the normal game (title).\n3. The **game's own card** (`hubcard` scene):\n   - The logo, the players lined up as builders in seat colours (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`; names drawn with the pixel font, never inserted as HTML), the goal, this player's control glyphs, ready ticks, and the countdown from the `card` event (`left`).\n   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a click → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **More time:** △, T or a click → `AIHub.answer('more')` (a second press takes it back).\n   - Nothing here changes the round. Any card randomness uses `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built (no key press).\n5. On `start`: a 3-2-1 countdown while `AIHub.time() < 0`. Play begins when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`.\n6. **Round clock:** 8:00, or `limitMs` if shorter.\n   - **Build phase** (5:00): raise the Quilt Barn Pattern, scaled by player count:\n\n     | Players | Barn walls | Blocks |\n     |---|---|---|\n     | 1 | 2 high | 38 |\n     | 2 | 3 high | 57 |\n     | 3–4 | 3 high + 10 Felt crenellations | 67 |\n\n     Plus a door and 2 torches.\n   - **Raid phase** (3:00): 3 waves from the corners. Knotbrutes target the barn and the Banner (HP 200).\n7. **Scores** (per player):\n   - +3 per Pattern block placed (the host credits the placer)\n   - +5 per monster defeated (Knotbrute +15)\n   - +5 per door or torch crafted and placed in the Pattern\n   - +1 per 5 items gathered\n8. **Host ends the round.** At the time limit, on `time-up` (within `graceMs`), or when every player has left, the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats })`:\n   - `standings`: arrays of ids by score, ties grouped.\n   - `won`: the Pattern is complete and the Banner HP > 0.\n   - `stats`: per id `{ Blocks, Monsters }`.\n   - Awards: \"Master Quilter\" for the most blocks, \"Knot Cutter\" for the most kills.\n9. On `end`: stop input, `audio.mute(true)` and `music(null)`, show \"Round over\", then do nothing more. On `leave`: remove that builder (its placed blocks stay). In **server mode** (`AIHub.server`): run the host simulation with no local builder, camera or input, and skip drawing except a 1-fps static \"Hosting the Bee\" frame.\n10. **The round never pauses.** Build the game with `autoPause: false`, `corner: false` and `menu: false` when `AIHub.active`, and make the `bee` scene `pausable: false` in a session. Options/Esc only show the toast \"Round in progress!\". There are no settings menus mid-round, and settings are at their defaults in a session, because the hub gives the game empty storage.\n11. **A hidden tab keeps the world running.** `requestAnimationFrame` stops in hidden tabs, so while `document.hidden`, a `setInterval` of 250 ms calls `game.advance(elapsed)` (capped at 1 s per call). The host keeps simulating and every copy keeps sending; the hub voids a round only after 20 s hidden.\n12. **Names** come from the hub and are drawn with the pixel font. Characters it lacks become `?`. They are never inserted as HTML.\n\n**Authority and messages.** Every copy runs the voxel world locally and keeps it in sync through edits. The host owns monsters, drops, Pattern progress, the clock and scores. Each client owns its own builder's movement, inventory and hotbar.\n\n| Msg | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Payload (compact arrays, integers) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `p` | client → host | no | 10 Hz | `[t, x, y, z, facing×100, anim, heldItem, hp]` |\n| `a` | client → host | yes | ≤ 6 Hz, batched | `ops: [['place', x,y,z, block, rot], ['break', x,y,z], ['hit', monId, dmg, kx, ky], ['take', dropId], ['craft', item]]` |\n| `s` | host → all | no | 10 Hz | `{ t, P: [[id,x,y,z,f,anim,held,hp]...], M: [[id,kind,x,y,z,f,hp,state]...], ph, left, prog, bhp }`, kept under 1,100 bytes (if more than 24 monsters, alternate halves) |\n| `e` | host → all | yes | ≤ 6 Hz, batched | `ev: [['vox', x,y,z, id, by], ['drop', id, item, n, x,y,z], ['gone', dropId], ['got', to, item, n], ['hurt', to, dmg, kx, ky], ['fx', kind, x,y,z], ['phase', name], ['score', id, n]]` |\n\n- Per copy that is ≤ 16 messages/s, under the 20/s cap. Every payload stays far below 16 KB; assert this in tests.\n- **Prediction:** a client applies its own place/break immediately and marks the cell pending; the host's `vox` event confirms or corrects it. Monsters on clients interpolate between snapshots (100 ms buffer).\n- **Hits:** a client sends `hit` when its local swing overlaps a monster's interpolated position, and the host applies damage. Old or out-of-order snapshots are dropped by `t`.\n- **Networking goes only through `AIHub.send`/`on`.** No sockets, fetch, `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. \"Quit to title\" does nothing in a session.\n\n**Outside the hub (the game on its own).** The title's **Quilting Bee** runs the same round solo: the local copy is the host, with a `LoopbackNet` that implements the same `send`/`on` surface in process. Optionally 1–3 **bot builders** run on `DQ.Autopilot` (\"Bee with friends: bots on/off\"). This exercises the host code paths outside the hub. Best scores go to `E.store`.\n\n### 6.22 Touch-only devices\nDetection: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, and no gamepad seen and no `keydown` yet. Re-evaluate when a pad connects or a key is pressed.\n\nOn such devices:\n- Every scene has `touch: []` and `input.touchEnabled = false`: **no touch controls**.\n- The title shows a stitched panel, \"**Controller or keyboard required**\", with the line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\" The engine's corner **settings/menu button** stays (`corner` on).\n- The attract mode runs as usual, and a tap returns to the title panel.\n\n### 6.23 Settings and accessibility (additions to the standard Settings)\n| Setting | Default |\n|---|---|\n| Button glyphs | PlayStation, or Xbox (sets `input.glyphs`) |\n| Camera view | Isometric, or Three-quarter |\n| Auto-hop | On |\n| Sprint | Hold, or Toggle |\n| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast |\n| Voices volume | 80% |\n| HUD tracker | On |\n| Difficulty | Normal (Relaxed / Hard) |\n| Cutaway | Auto (Always, Off) |\n| Screen shake and flashes | Engine standard |\n\nReduce motion: the engine handles it; it also disables the camera crossfade and the confetti density.\n","numLines":330,"startLine":510,"totalLines":1613}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L4i2UFFWHhES1wEbgMfHMt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
