{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jjn7E9TQVZvJFeyPoJtcvy","type":"tool_result","content":"839\t\n840\t### 6.24 About/Credits screen and exit interview\n841\t- `tools/build.mjs` reads `./exit-interview.json`, if present, and embeds its `sourceInformation`, `testingFeedback`, `engineFeedback` and `promptFeedback` as `DQ.ABOUT`. The About pages render them.\n842\t  - If the file is missing during development, a dev-only notice says so. A release build fails without it.\n843\t  - Order matters: write `exit-interview.json` before the final build.\n844\t- **Credits page:**\n845\t  - \"Dragon Quilt Builders: an original game inspired by Dragon Quest Builders (Square Enix). Not affiliated with or endorsed by Square Enix. No assets from the original.\"\n846\t  - Design, code, art, music and writing: the AI model (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5) under direction.\n847\t  - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT) by michaelcrosato, with the list of our engine changes.\n848\t  - AI Hub Session client 1.4.0.\n849\t  - Plan: PLAN.md.\n850\t- **Source Information** fields (TASK.md), with \"unknown\" where something cannot be confirmed:\n851\t  - Date `2026-11-03 17:47:40`\n852\t  - Source `Dragon Quest Builders`\n853\t  - Plan `PLAN.md`\n854\t  - Genre and perspective: \"Sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building); isometric 2.5D third person, rotatable\"\n855\t  - Tech, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment (`Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown`), model (`Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max`), usage\n856\t- **Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback** answer TASK.md's questions in order. The same text goes in the final chat reply.\n857\t- **`exit-interview.json`** (the exact shape in TASK.md). Validate it with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Suggested `aiHub` values:\n858\t\n859\t  | Field | Value |\n860\t  |---|---|\n861\t  | name | \"Dragon Quilt Builders\" |\n862\t  | tagline | \"Stitch a frayed world back together\" |\n863\t  | description | \"Gather, craft and build block by block to mend a patchwork kingdom unravelled by a dragon. Raise rooms for quirky residents, defend your town and unpick a knotted boss, or raise a barn together in co-op Quilting Bee rounds.\" |\n864\t  | type | \"Game\" |\n865\t  | genre | \"RPG\" |\n866\t  | source | \"Dragon Quest Builders\" |\n867\t  | series | \"Dragon Quest\" |\n868\t  | players | \"1–4\" |\n869\t  | controls | \"Stick/WASD move · ✕/Space jump · □/Click break · △/Right-click place · L1 R1/wheel items · ○/F talk\" |\n870\t  | tags | [\"building\", \"crafting\", \"co-op\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"] |\n871\t\n872\t---\n873\t## 7. Content\n874\t\n875\t### 7.1 The world: the Patchwork Realm around Thimbleton (144 × 144 columns, 24 levels, seed 20261103)\n876\t\n877\t```\n878\t x→ 0                 48                 96                 143\n879\ty 0 +-------------------+------------------+------------------+\n880\t  | CORDUROY CRAGS      |                  |   TWEEDWOOD      |\n881\t  |  Button Quarry(22,18)                  |   Lint Camp      |\n882\t  |  ledge button(48,8) |                  |   (116,30)       |\n883\t  |   Lint Hollow(38,40)>exit(50,42)      |   hollow-tree    |\n884\t48|...................  GINGHAM GLEN  .....|...button(134,52)|\n885\t  |  stream ~           (meadow)           |                  |\n886\t  |      ~       THIMBLETON  banner(72,76)  Rift(96,80)        |\n887\t  |        ~     border r=10..20       east road → (143,76)   |\n888\t96|   ~                                     |FRAYED VERGE| THE FRAYING\n889\t  | CALICO COAST         (glen south)       |x92-99 |KnotWall x99-100\n890\t  |  shipwreck+button(22,126)               |       | Knotted Spire(124,124)\n891\t  |  sea x<14, y>132                        |       | gate y112-114\n892\t143+-------------------+------------------+------------------+\n893\t```\n894\tSurface levels are approximate (generated with `E.noise2` plus per-region shaping). The outer 2-column ring is void with frayed fringe.\n895\t\n896\t| Region | Area | Surface | Top / under | Features | Spawns (day / night) |\n897\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n898\t| **Lint Hollow** (start) | centre (38,40), floor 12×10 | floor L7, rim L13–14 | earth, stone walls | Dead bushes (branches), 6 loose earth blocks, one Lintling. A dark 6-block tunnel (2-high, roofed: tests the cutaway) with stairs up to the exit at (50,42). A \"darkness zone\" (ambient .15 until a torch is placed at the marked spot) | 1 scripted Lintling |\n899\t| **Gingham Glen** | x 44–100, y 44–104 (minus the town) | L9 ± 2, gentle hills | grass / 3 earth / stone | Tufts (1 per 12 cells), cotton puffs, thimbleberry bushes near the town, buttercups, a shallow stream (1-deep water) from (30,58) winding to the coast at (18,132), trees in small groves | Lintling 70%, Dyed Lintling 30% / Lintling 40%, Mothlet 60% |\n900\t| **Thimbleton** | banner spot (72,76) on a cobble plaza 5×5 | L9 flattened in radius 12 | grass, cobble ruins | Ruined foundations: three 1-high cobble outlines of old houses (hints for room shapes), a broken well, a pond 3×4 (decor water), the east road (planks path) to (143,76), the Thimbleton Bobbin Portal at (70,80) | none inside the border |\n901\t| **Corduroy Crags** | x 4–60, y 4–56 | L11–20 ridges | stone, gravel on slopes, grass in hollows | Exposed copper (levels 7–12) and coal (8–14) veins as blobs, 4–7 blocks each, Poisson-spaced. The Button Quarry. A Bobbin Portal at the Hollow exit (52,44) and at the Quarry rim (34,20). The Ancient Button on a stone pillar ledge at (48,8), L19 (a stairs puzzle) | Lintling, Pinhog / Lintling, Pinhog |\n902\t| **Button Quarry** | open pit (22,18), 16×14, floor L6 | rim L15 | stone terraces | Ramp from the east, terraces with coal and copper, 4 cobble pillars, boss arena floor 12×10. Sir Buttonsworth sleeps here (wakes on entry after M10) | Pinhog (before the boss) |\n903\t| **Tweedwood** | x 92–140, y 6–60 | L10 ± 2 | grass / earth | Dense voxel trees: trunk 3–5 Plaid Logs, Pompom leaf blob radius 2, Poisson spacing ~4. Puffballs in shade, bluebells at the edges. The Lint Camp at (116,30): Lintwick in a Knot Cage (a 1×1 object, HP 30, tier 2), 3 Dyed Lintlings, knot-fence decor. A hollow tree with the Ancient Button at (134,52). A Bobbin Portal at (110,36) | Dyed Lintling / Mothlet, Dyed Lintling |\n904\t| **Calico Coast** | x 4–60, y 100–140 | sand L7–8; sea L5–6 water where height < 7 | sand / sand / stone | Beach, dunes, cotton puffs, a shipwreck stamp (plank hull) holding the Ancient Button at (22,126), a Bobbin Portal at (30,116) | Pinhog / Pinhog, Mothlet |\n905\t| **Frayed Verge** | x 92–99, y 92–140 | L9 | frayed cloth patches | The approach to the Knot Wall; a Bobbin Portal at (94,110) | Frayed Knight (night only, plus 2 fixed guards by day near the gate) |\n906\t| **The Knot Wall** | x 99–100, y 92–141, up to L17 | — | knot (tier 3) | The **Knot Gate** at y 112–114 (3 wide × 5 high) is the only way through (Seam Ripper) | — |\n907\t| **The Fraying** | x 101–140, y 94–140 | L9 ± 3 with void holes | frayed / earth / stone | Void holes (columns emptied entirely, Backing Cloth included: falling in = unravel respawn), dead trees, ash weather, purple ambient. The **Knotted Spire** at (124,124): a 9×9 base of knot and frayed blocks up to L22, with an outer spiral ramp 2 wide (stairs blocks), and a pedestal with the Golden Thread fragment on top | Frayed Knight, Knotbrute (rare) / the same, ×1.5 |\n908\t| **The Rift** | (96,80), radius 3 | void | — | A frayed hole east of town that is the siege's spawn point. Re-stitched at the chapter's end (a wave turns it into meadow) | Frayed Knight at night |\n909\t\n910\tStamps (`DQ.WORLD.stamps`, ASCII layers bottom to top with a legend; `' '` means keep the existing block, `.` air):\n911\t- `lintHollow`, `thimbletonRuins`, `buttonQuarry`, `lintCamp`, `shipwreck`, `knotGate`, `knottedSpire`, `rift`\n912\t- `portalPad` (×6), `demoTown` (the attract/title diorama: Lv4 Thimbleton), `beeMeadow` (48×48 Bee world)\n913\t- `beat_*` stamps for dev story beats (the rooms a player would have built by then)\n914\t\n915\tWorldgen order:\n916\t1. heightmap\n917\t2. layers\n918\t3. ores\n919\t4. water fill\n920\t5. trees\n921\t6. plants (objects)\n922\t7. stamps\n923\t8. portals\n924\t9. `escape` sweep\n925\t10. nav build\n926\t11. `world.base` snapshot\n927\t\n928\tMust be deterministic: test it by `world.hash()` equality across two runs.\n929\t\n930\t### 7.2 Blocks (`DQ.BLOCKS`)\n931\tTexture names refer to the patterns in §8.1. \"tier\" is the minimum tool tier to break it (∞ = never). Every face has stitched seams.\n932\t\n933\t| id | key | Name | hp | tier | Drops | Placeable | Texture (top / side) | Notes |\n934\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n935\t| 1 | backing | Backing Cloth | ∞ | ∞ | — | no | navy felt with a square stitch grid | level 0 |\n936\t| 2 | earth | Corduroy Earth | 6 | 1 | earth | yes | brown cord crosshatch / vertical cord ribs | |\n937\t| 3 | grass | Gingham Turf | 6 | 1 | earth | no (gives earth) | green gingham checks / earth with a 3-texel felt fringe | |\n938\t| 4 | sand | Calico Sand | 4 | 1 | sand | yes | pale yellow calico, tiny orange florets | |\n939\t| 5 | gravel | Button Gravel | 8 | 1 | pebble ×2 | no | grey with little round bumps | |\n940\t| 6 | stone | Tweed Stone | 20 | 2 | stone | yes | grey herringbone tweed | |\n941\t| 7 | copperOre | Copper Sequin Seam | 30 | 2 | copperOre | no | tweed with copper sequins (glint frame) | |\n942\t| 8 | coal | Charcloth Seam | 24 | 2 | coal | no | tweed with black felt lumps | |\n943\t| 9 | log | Plaid Log | 12 | 1 | log | yes | stitched rings / brown bark with tartan stripes | |\n944\t| 10 | leaves | Pompom Leaves | 2 | 1 | branch 35% | no | green bobbles with lit tops | |\n945\t| 11 | frayed | Frayed Cloth | 24 | 2 | frayedScrap | no | dark plum, torn weave, loose threads | |\n946\t| 12 | knot | Black Knot | 60 | 3 | blackYarn | no | tangled black-violet yarn loops | |\n947\t| 13 | water | Satin Water | — | — | — | no | blue satin shimmer (translucent) | static; 2+ deep blocks walkers |\n948\t| 20 | cobble | Cobble Patch | 22 | 2 | cobble | yes | grey quilted rounded stones | |\n949\t| 21 | planks | Plank Patch | 10 | 1 | planks | yes | tan boards with stitched seams | |\n950\t| 22 | thatch | Straw Thatch | 4 | 1 | thatch | yes | golden straw courses | |\n951\t| 23 | feltRed | Red Felt Patch | 6 | 1 | feltRed | yes | felt with a diamond stitch | also Blue (24) and Yellow (25) |\n952\t| 26 | glow | Glow Patch | 6 | 1 | glow | yes | pale gold felt with a stitched star (emissive) | light 48 |\n953\t| 27 | stairsPlank | Plank Stairs | 10 | 1 | stairsPlank | yes | planks (wedge) | `rot` from facing |\n954\t| 28 | stairsCobble | Cobble Stairs | 22 | 2 | stairsCobble | yes | cobble (wedge) | |\n955\t| 29 | tangle | Tangle | 12 | 1 | — | no | black yarn ball | Gnarlgrim residue, vanishes after 20 s |\n956\t| 30 | gildedFelt | Gilded Felt | 6 | 1 | gildedFelt | yes | gold felt with sparkle | S3 reward |\n957\t\n958\t### 7.3 Items and materials (`DQ.ITEMS`)\n959\tEvery item has an `icon`: a block cube rendered from the atlas, `E.shapeSprite` for objects, or a 16×16 `E.sprite` string (marked ✎) to author. Descriptions are in Dragon Quest style; examples are given for a few.\n960\t\n961\t| id | Name | Kind | From | Use / notes |\n962\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n963\t| earth, sand, stone, log, cobble, planks, thatch, feltRed/Blue/Yellow, glow, stairsPlank, stairsCobble, gildedFelt | (blocks) | block | breaking or crafting | place |\n964\t| pebble ✎ | Pebble | material | gravel | Cobble Club, Weapon Rack. \"A little stone with big dreams.\" |\n965\t| copperOre ✎ | Copper Ore | material | copper seams | Copper Ingot |\n966\t| coal ✎ | Charcloth | material | coal seams | ingots, Hearth Pot, Forge |\n967\t| branch ✎ | Branch | material | dead bushes, leaves | torches, doors, club |\n968\t| straw ✎ | Straw | material | tufts (1–2) | beds, thatch |\n969\t| grain ✎ | Wild Grain | ingredient | tufts 30% | buns, stew |\n970\t| cotton ✎ | Cotton Puff | material | cotton puffs (2) | thread, beds, felt, vest |\n971\t| thread ✎ | Thread | material | crafted | doors, lanterns, vest |\n972\t| lint ✎ | Lint | material | Lintlings, Lintwick | torches. \"Fluffy, flammable, faintly judgemental.\" |\n973\t| mothDust ✎ | Moth Dust | material | Mothlets | Glow Patch, Moth Lantern |\n974\t| pins ✎ | Pins | material | Pinhogs | Pin Trap |\n975\t| steelThread ✎ | Steel Thread | material | Frayed Knights 70%, Sir Buttonsworth ×3 | Ballista, Seam Ripper |\n976\t| blackYarn ✎ | Black Yarn | material | Knotbrutes, Black Knots | Gilded Felt alternate recipe (2 feltYellow + 1 blackYarn → 4, after S3). \"Tangled beyond all reason.\" |\n977\t| frayedScrap ✎ | Frayed Scrap | material | Frayed Cloth | fuel: replaces the 1 coal in the Hearth Pot's own recipe |\n978\t| copperIngot ✎ | Copper Ingot | material | Forge | gear, ballista, lantern |\n979\t| dyeRed/Blue/Yellow ✎ | Rose / Bluebell / Buttercup Dye | material | crafted from berries / bluebells / buttercups | felt |\n980\t| thimbleberry ✎ | Thimbleberry | food | berry bushes (2) | eat raw: Belly +5. Bun, stew, red dye |\n981\t| bluebell ✎, buttercup ✎ | flowers | material | flowers | dyes |\n982\t| puffball ✎ | Puffball | ingredient | Tweedwood | roast, stew |\n983\t| roastPuffball ✎ | Roast Puffball | food | Hearth Pot | Belly +20, HP +5 |\n984\t| bun ✎ | Thimbleberry Bun | food | Hearth Pot | Belly +35, HP +10 |\n985\t| stew ✎ | Glen Stew | food | Hearth Pot | Belly +60, HP +20 |\n986\t| pie ✎ | Marigold's Hearty Pie | food | Marigold only | Belly +100, HP full |\n987\t| darningStick ✎ | Darning Stick | weapon | start | atk 3, blockDmg 6, tier 1 |\n988\t| cobbleClub ✎ | Cobble Club | weapon | Bench | atk 7, blockDmg 10, tier 2 |\n989\t| copperBodkin ✎ | Copper Bodkin | weapon | Forge | atk 12, blockDmg 12, tier 2, swing ×0.9 time |\n990\t| seamRipper ✎ | Seam Ripper | weapon | Forge | atk 9, blockDmg 20, tier 3; ×4 against Black Knots and the Heart Knot |\n991\t| quiltedVest ✎ | Quilted Vest | body | Bench | def +3 |\n992\t| copperBuckler ✎ | Copper Buckler | shield | Forge | def +4 |\n993\t| heartpatch ✎ | Heartpatch | use | quests M5, M8, M10 | max HP +10 (consumed on use, with a sparkle and jingle) |\n994\t| banner ✎ | Banner of Mending | key | M1 reward | plant at Thimbleton |\n995\t| hallPattern ✎ | Pattern: Quilters' Hall | key | Professor (M10) | place the Pattern |\n996\t| goldenNeedle ✎ | Golden Needle | key | Sir Buttonsworth | Seam Ripper |\n997\t| goldenThread ✎ | Golden Thread (fragment) | key | Spire top | story |\n998\t| ancientButton ✎ | Ancient Button | key | 3 hidden | S3 |\n999\t| goldenThimble ✎ | Golden Thimble | key | S3 reward | unlocks Gilded Felt |\n1000\t\n1001\tItem counts and sources above are the balance defaults. The Dev → Tuning sliders scale drops, damage and drains on top of them; balance changes to the tables themselves go in the data files.\n1002\t\n1003\t### 7.4 Recipes (`DQ.RECIPES`: station, inputs → output, notion trigger)\n1004\t\n1005\t| Recipe | Station | Inputs → Output | Notion |\n1006\t|---|---|---|---|\n1007\t| Wick Torch | Pocket | 1 branch + 1 lint → 1 torch | pickup lint (Hollow) |\n1008\t| Mending Bench | Pocket | 3 branch + 4 earth → 1 bench | banner planted (Granny teaches) |\n1009\t| Straw Bed | Bench | 4 straw + 1 cotton → 1 strawBed | pickup straw |\n1010\t| Lattice Door | Bench | 3 branch → 1 latticeDoor | banner planted |\n1011\t| Storage Chest | Bench | 2 log + 2 branch → 1 chest | M3 reward |\n1012\t| Planks | Bench | 1 log → 3 planks | pickup log |\n1013\t| Thread | Bench | 2 cotton → 2 thread | pickup cotton |\n1014\t| Straw Thatch | Bench | 2 straw → 3 thatch | pickup straw |\n1015\t| Rose / Bluebell / Buttercup Dye | Bench | 2 thimbleberry / bluebell / buttercup → 1 dye | pickup the flower or berry, at Lv3 |\n1016\t| Cobble Club | Bench | 2 branch + 3 pebble → 1 | pickup pebble |\n1017\t| Cobble Patch | Bench | 1 stone + 1 earth → 2 cobble | Lv2 |\n1018\t| Stool | Bench | 2 planks → 1 | Lv2 |\n1019\t| Plank Table | Bench | 4 planks → 1 | Lv2 |\n1020\t| Plank Door | Bench | 2 planks + 1 thread → 1 | Lv2 |\n1021\t| Weapon Rack | Bench | 3 planks + 2 pebble → 1 | M6 start |\n1022\t| Plank Stairs | Bench | 2 planks → 2 | Lv2 |\n1023\t| Cobble Stairs | Bench | 2 cobble → 2 | Lv3 |\n1024\t| Quilted Vest | Bench | 4 cotton + 2 thread → 1 | Lv3 |\n1025\t| Felt Patch (colour) | Bench | 2 cotton + 1 dye → 4 felt | Lv3 |\n1026\t| Hearth Pot | Bench | 4 stone + 1 coal (or frayedScrap) → 1 | M8 start |\n1027\t| Thimble Forge | Bench | 6 stone + 2 coal + 2 cobble → 1 | M9 start |\n1028\t| Pin Trap | Bench | 3 pins + 1 planks → 2 | Lv4 |\n1029\t| Glow Patch | Bench | 1 mothDust + 1 feltYellow → 2 glow | pickup mothDust, at Lv3 |\n1030\t| Moth Lantern | Bench | 1 copperIngot + 1 mothDust + 1 thread → 1 | Lv4 |\n1031\t| Gilded Felt | Bench | 2 feltYellow + 1 copperIngot (or 1 blackYarn) → 4 | S3 reward |\n1032\t| Roast Puffball | Hearth | 1 puffball → 1 | pickup puffball |\n1033\t| Thimbleberry Bun | Hearth | 2 thimbleberry + 1 grain → 1 | Hearth placed |\n1034\t| Glen Stew | Hearth | 2 puffball + 1 thimbleberry + 1 grain → 1 | M8 reward |\n1035\t| Copper Ingot | Forge | 1 copperOre + 1 coal → 1 | Forge placed |\n1036\t| Copper Bodkin | Forge | 2 copperIngot + 1 log → 1 | Forge placed |\n1037\t| Copper Buckler | Forge | 2 copperIngot + 2 planks → 1 | Forge placed |\n1038\t| Bobbin Ballista | Forge | 2 log + 2 copperIngot + 2 steelThread → 1 | M10 (Professor) |\n1039\t| Seam Ripper | Forge | 1 goldenNeedle + 2 copperIngot + 2 steelThread → 1 | Golden Needle picked up |\n1040\t\n1041\t### 7.5 Objects (`DQ.OBJECTS`; each has an `E.SHAPES` entry, sized for the 26-unit hero)\n1042\t| id | Name | Cells | Solid | Light | Behaviour | Shape notes (materials) |\n1043\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1044\t| bench | Mending Bench | 1 | yes | — | crafting station | plank table, a pincushion, 2 spools, scissors (oak, wool, iron) |\n1045\t| torch | Wick Torch | 1 | no | 64, `#ffb060` | room light | stick + lint wick + `flames` |\n1046\t| lantern | Moth Lantern | 1 | no | 96, `#ffe7a0` | room light | copper cage, glow material |\n1047\t| latticeDoor | Lattice Door | 1×2 high | passable | — | door, HP 30 | crossed branches, two leaves that swing |\n1048\t| plankDoor | Plank Door | 1×2 high | passable | — | door, HP 50 | planks with a stitched heart |\n1049\t| strawBed | Straw Bed | 1 | low (z 6) | — | sleep slot | frame + straw + a patchwork quilt blanket (feltRed/Blue checks) |\n1050\t| table | Plank Table | 1 | yes | — | mess hall | core `table` with planks |\n1051\t| stool | Stool | 1 | low | — | seat | core `stool` |\n1052\t| chest | Storage Chest | 1 | yes | — | 20 slots, Town Chest flag | core `chest` |\n1053\t| hearthPot | Hearth Pot | 1 | yes | 48, `#ff8040` | cooking station | stone ring, iron pot, `flames` |\n1054\t| forge | Thimble Forge | 1 | yes | 56, `#ff7030` | smithing station | a giant thimble-shaped furnace with a glowing mouth |\n1055\t| weaponRack | Weapon Rack | 1 | yes | — | guard post | planks with 2 clubs |\n1056\t| pinTrap | Pin Trap | 1 | no | — | trap | a board with coloured pin heads |\n1057\t| ballista | Bobbin Ballista | 1 | yes | — | turret, HP 150 | wooden frame, steel-thread bowstring, a spool bolt |\n1058\t| banner | Banner of Mending | 1 | yes | 80, `#ffd870` | town core, HP 300 | pole plus a cloth banner, drawn in code (sine flutter) with a stripe per level |\n1059\t| portal | Bobbin Portal | 1×2 high | no | 40, `#c8a0ff` | travel | a bobbin-shaped arch with swirling thread (animated in code) |\n1060\t| cage | Knot Cage | 1 | yes | — | Lintwick, HP 30, tier 2 | knot bars |\n1061\t| tuft, cottonPuff, berryBush, bluebell, buttercup, puffball, deadBush | plants | 1 | no | — | harvest, regrow 1 day | core `grass`/`bush`/`flowers` recoloured; cotton balls and berries added as parts |\n1062\t| ancientButton | Ancient Button | 1 | no | glint | collectible | a big gold 4-hole button on a stand |\n1063\t| lostBundle | Lost Bundle | 1 | no | — | KO stash | a patch-sack |\n1064\t\n1065\t### 7.6 Rooms (`DQ.ROOMS`, checked in this priority order)\n1066\t| Type | Requirements (in addition to the room rule) | Cheer | maxAwards | Effect |\n1067\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1068\t| Quilters' Hall | Built from the Hall Pattern (complete), interior 50–64 cells | 100 | 1 | Landmark, plus Professor's comfort |\n1069\t| Guard Post | Weapon Rack + 2 lights | 30 | 1 | Mortimer's comfort; he stands watch |\n1070\t| Smithy | Thimble Forge + Chest | 30 | 1 | Forge works faster ×1.5 inside |\n1071\t| Kitchen | Hearth Pot + Chest | 25 | 1 | Marigold cooks here |\n1072\t| Mess Hall | Plank Table + 2 Stools | 25 | 1 | Supper spot; residents eat |\n1073\t| Workshop | Mending Bench + Chest | 25 | 1 | Professor's comfort |\n1074\t| Bedroom | ≥ 1 Straw Bed | 20 | 3 | Sleep slots = beds; Wren's and Lintwick's comfort |\n1075\t| Snug | (the room rule only) | 5 | 3 | — |\n1076\t\n1077\t### 7.7 Town levels (`DQ.LEVELS`)\n1078\t| Lv | Cheer | Border r (side) | Unlocks | Arrives |\n1079\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1080\t| 1 | 0 | 10 (21×21) | base recipes | Wren, at the planting |\n1081\t| 2 | 40 | 13 (27×27) | cobble, stool, table, plank door, plank stairs, Town Chest designation | Mortimer |\n1082\t| 3 | 130 | 16 (33×33) | dyes, felt, quilted vest, cobble stairs, glow patch | Marigold |\n1083\t| 4 | 250 | 18 (37×37) | pin trap, moth lantern | Professor Selvage (brings the Hall Pattern) |\n1084\t| 5 | 450 | 20 (41×41) | Chapter clear; Hearty Pie served to everyone | — (Lintwick joins through S1 at any level ≥ 2) |\n1085\t\n1086\tExpected pacing (keep it when balancing):\n1087\t- Bedroom (20) + Workshop (25) → Lv2.\n1088\t- + Guard Post (30) + Mess Hall (25) + M5/M6 rewards (25) + bubbles (about 15) → Lv3.\n1089\t- + Kitchen (25) + Smithy (30) + M8/M9 rewards (35) + S1 (20) + bubbles (about 30) → Lv4.\n1090\t- + Hall (100) + boss victory (+150) → Lv5.\n1091\t\n1092\t### 7.8 Characters\n1093\tAll humans are `E.Humanoid` with `build: 'chibi'` unless noted. Faces use `face: { eyes: 'big' }`. Portraits come from `rig.drawPortrait`.\n1094\t\n1095\t| Who | Role | Look (Humanoid / Blob options) | Voice (Animalese profile) | Personality, tics, sample lines |\n1096\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1097\t| **The Builder** (player, default \"Patch\") | Silent hero | Size 1.0. A: `hair:'spiky'`, `hat:{style:'band',color:'#c8443a'}`, `outfit:'tunic'` denim `#3a5f9a` with patch trim `#e8c870`. B: `hair:'ponytail'`, `outfit:'robe'` (apron dress) `#4a8a5a`. Skin `#f2c39a`, a tool-belt colour | silent | Choices only |\n1098\t| **Granny Gossamer** | The Great Quilter; voice from the sky | No body. Portrait: a glowing golden spool with kind half-moon eyes and a needle \"hairpin\" (custom portrait function) | 165 Hz, range ±25%, triangle, formant 0.9, slow, vibrato 5 Hz 3% | Warm, scatterbrained, fond of \"dearie\" and \"my little stitch\". \"Wakey wakey, dearie! Oh good, you're not a pincushion. I'd hate to have stitched you together for nothing.\" / \"Frayvern pulled the Golden Thread right out of the world, and everything came apart at the seams. Worse, he swallowed everyone's Knack! Not a soul can make so much as a potholder.\" / \"But you still have the Knack. You're a Builder, dearie!\" |\n1099\t| **Wren Tuck** | First resident; eager kid | Size 0.85, `hair:'ponytail'` orange `#e07a2a`, `outfit:'shirt'` green `#5aa04a`, freckles drawn on the portrait | 330 Hz ±35%, pulse 25%, formant 1.25, fast | Breathless, curious, invents words (\"bildering\"). \"Whoa! Are you a monster? You don't LOOK like a monster. Monsters don't usually wave.\" / \"You MADE that? With your hands? On PURPOSE?!\" / \"Granny says people used to sleep on things called 'beds'. Do they bite?\" |\n1100\t| **Mortimer Bodkin** | Old guard, grump | `build:'bulky'` size 1.05, `hair:'bald'`, a white beard drawn on the portrait, `hat:'helmet'` dented, `outfit:'coat'` grey `#6a6a78`, `armor:true`, weapon `'club'` | 110 Hz ±15%, saw with 0.2 noise, formant 0.8, slow | \"Hmph.\" Everything was harder in his day. \"In my day we slept on rocks, and we were GRATEFUL for the rocks.\" / \"A club is just a stick with ambition.\" / (later) \"...Not bad, Builder. Not bad at all. Don't let it go to your head.\" |\n1101\t| **Marigold Purl** | Cook without a kitchen | Size 1.0, `hair:'long'` blonde, `hat:{style:'cap',color:'#ffffff'}` (chef), `outfit:'robe'` `#e8a0a0` with apron trim | 240 Hz ±30%, triangle, formant 1.1, bouncy alternation | Food puns, big feelings. \"I've got Glen Stew in my head and not a single pot to stew it in! It's a crock, I tell you. A CROCK!\" / \"Supper's on! Wash your paws, Lintwick.\" |\n1102\t| **Professor Hemsley Selvage** | Scholar of the Knack | `build:'heroic'` size 1.05 (tall, thin), `hair:'short'` grey, `hat:'pointed'` dark green, `outfit:'robe'` `#3a6a5a`, glasses drawn on the portrait and the rig head | 200 Hz ±20%, pulse12 (nasal), formant 1.15, fast | Long words, \"Fascinating!\" \"A functioning door! Do you realise nobody has hinged anything in forty years?\" / \"This Pattern is a schematic of considerable grandeur. And considerable lumber.\" |\n1103\t| **Lintwick** | Reformed Lintling | `E.Blob({ R: 7, colors: {base:'#cfcad6', dk:'#9a94a8', lt:'#f0eef4'}, feet: true, mouth: true, face: 'front' })` plus a fuzz outline (dithered edge) and button eyes drawn over the eyes | 520 Hz ±40%, sine with an upward chirp, formant 1.4 | Third person, sweet. \"Lintwick not bad monster! Lintwick just fuzzy!\" / \"Lintwick want bed. Soft bed. Lintwick will not shed on it. ...Much.\" |\n1104\t| **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** | Frayvern's general | `build:'bulky'` size 2.6, colours black and violet yarn, `eyeGlow` magenta, `cape` (tattered threads), `hat:'crown'` recoloured as knotted spikes, a glowing Heart Knot drawn on the chest | 70 Hz ±10%, saw plus a waveshaper drive, formant 0.7 | Boastful, knot puns. \"YOU! The needle in my side! I'll tie you in knots, little Builder!\" / \"I'm... unravelling...!\" |\n1105\t| **Sir Buttonsworth** | Button Golem mini-boss | `build:'bulky'` size 2.0, tan felt `#c8a878`, big button eyes and a belly button drawn on, `weapon: null` | 90 Hz, square, formant 0.75 | Pompous. \"HALT! None shall pass without a proper fastening!\" |\n1106\t| **Frayvern** | The dragon (seen only as a silhouette) | A huge moth-winged dragon silhouette drawn with `px.poly` in the sky during 2 cutscenes | 55 Hz saw with an echo (delay node) | \"Mend all the patches you like, Builder. I hold the Golden Thread, and the whole quilt is mine to pull.\" |\n1107\t\n1108\t### 7.9 Monsters (`DQ.MONSTERS`; speeds in units/s, aggro in blocks)\n1109\t| id | Name | Body | HP | Atk | Def | Speed | Aggro | Moves (wind-up telegraphs) | Drops |\n1110\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1111\t| lintling | Lintling | Blob R6 `#b8b4c0`, fuzz edge, button eyes, `mouth:true` | 8 | 4 | 1 | 34 | 7 | Hop chase; lunge (squash wind .35 s, leap 60) | lint 100%, cotton 15% |\n1112\t| dyedLintling | Dyed Lintling | Blob R6 `#e88ab8` | 16 | 7 | 2 | 38 | 8 | Double-hop lunge (.3 s) | lint 100%, dyeRed 25% |\n1113\t| mothlet | Mothlet | Blob R5 `wings:true`, `mouth:'fangs'`, dusty violet; flies at z + 18..28 | 10 | 6 | 1 | 48 | 10 | Circles; swoop dive (rises .4 s, dives at 140); night only | mothDust 100% |\n1114\t| pinhog | Pinhog | Blob R7 `feet:true` with 10 coloured pins drawn radially | 22 | 9 | 5 | 30 (roll 110) | 8 | Curl (.6 s wind, shake), roll charge for 1.2 s, immune from the front while rolling, dizzy 1.2 s after hitting a wall | pins 80%, pebble 30% |\n1115\t| frayedKnight | Frayed Knight | Humanoid `build:'heroic'` size 1.1, a muslin \"dress-form\" mannequin (`#e8dcc0`) with frayed hems, `eyeGlow:'#b070ff'`, `weapon:'sword'` recoloured as a long needle-lance | 40 | 12 | 8 | 40 | 9 | `stance:'ready'`; `thrust` (.3 s wind, lunge); `spin` when surrounded | steelThread 70%, frayedScrap 50% |\n1116\t| knotbrute | Knotbrute | Humanoid `build:'bulky'` size 1.4, navy yarn `#2a2a48`, `hunch:.3`, `eyeGlow` red, knot bumps on the shoulders | 60 | 14 | 6 | 26 | 10 | `haymaker` (.45 s); block smash 25; shoulder charge (.5 s wind) | blackYarn 100% |\n1117\t| buttonGolem | Sir Buttonsworth | §7.8 | 220 | 14 | 8 | 30 | arena | Slam, Button Volley, Stomp Charge, summon at 50% (§6.12) | goldenNeedle, steelThread ×3 |\n1118\t| gnarlgrim | Gnarlgrim | §7.8 | 600 | 18 | 25 (0 Tangled) | 34 (charge 140) | town | §6.12 | goldenThread (story) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"b3be0ef3-a2e7-400c-9719-6333c7cd0397","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:08.857Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### 6.24 About/Credits screen and exit interview\n- `tools/build.mjs` reads `./exit-interview.json`, if present, and embeds its `sourceInformation`, `testingFeedback`, `engineFeedback` and `promptFeedback` as `DQ.ABOUT`. The About pages render them.\n  - If the file is missing during development, a dev-only notice says so. A release build fails without it.\n  - Order matters: write `exit-interview.json` before the final build.\n- **Credits page:**\n  - \"Dragon Quilt Builders: an original game inspired by Dragon Quest Builders (Square Enix). Not affiliated with or endorsed by Square Enix. No assets from the original.\"\n  - Design, code, art, music and writing: the AI model (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5) under direction.\n  - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT) by michaelcrosato, with the list of our engine changes.\n  - AI Hub Session client 1.4.0.\n  - Plan: PLAN.md.\n- **Source Information** fields (TASK.md), with \"unknown\" where something cannot be confirmed:\n  - Date `2026-11-03 17:47:40`\n  - Source `Dragon Quest Builders`\n  - Plan `PLAN.md`\n  - Genre and perspective: \"Sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building); isometric 2.5D third person, rotatable\"\n  - Tech, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment (`Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown`), model (`Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max`), usage\n- **Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback** answer TASK.md's questions in order. The same text goes in the final chat reply.\n- **`exit-interview.json`** (the exact shape in TASK.md). Validate it with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Suggested `aiHub` values:\n\n  | Field | Value |\n  |---|---|\n  | name | \"Dragon Quilt Builders\" |\n  | tagline | \"Stitch a frayed world back together\" |\n  | description | \"Gather, craft and build block by block to mend a patchwork kingdom unravelled by a dragon. Raise rooms for quirky residents, defend your town and unpick a knotted boss, or raise a barn together in co-op Quilting Bee rounds.\" |\n  | type | \"Game\" |\n  | genre | \"RPG\" |\n  | source | \"Dragon Quest Builders\" |\n  | series | \"Dragon Quest\" |\n  | players | \"1–4\" |\n  | controls | \"Stick/WASD move · ✕/Space jump · □/Click break · △/Right-click place · L1 R1/wheel items · ○/F talk\" |\n  | tags | [\"building\", \"crafting\", \"co-op\", \"fantasy\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\"] |\n\n---\n## 7. Content\n\n### 7.1 The world: the Patchwork Realm around Thimbleton (144 × 144 columns, 24 levels, seed 20261103)\n\n```\n x→ 0                 48                 96                 143\ny 0 +-------------------+------------------+------------------+\n  | CORDUROY CRAGS      |                  |   TWEEDWOOD      |\n  |  Button Quarry(22,18)                  |   Lint Camp      |\n  |  ledge button(48,8) |                  |   (116,30)       |\n  |   Lint Hollow(38,40)>exit(50,42)      |   hollow-tree    |\n48|...................  GINGHAM GLEN  .....|...button(134,52)|\n  |  stream ~           (meadow)           |                  |\n  |      ~       THIMBLETON  banner(72,76)  Rift(96,80)        |\n  |        ~     border r=10..20       east road → (143,76)   |\n96|   ~                                     |FRAYED VERGE| THE FRAYING\n  | CALICO COAST         (glen south)       |x92-99 |KnotWall x99-100\n  |  shipwreck+button(22,126)               |       | Knotted Spire(124,124)\n  |  sea x<14, y>132                        |       | gate y112-114\n143+-------------------+------------------+------------------+\n```\nSurface levels are approximate (generated with `E.noise2` plus per-region shaping). The outer 2-column ring is void with frayed fringe.\n\n| Region | Area | Surface | Top / under | Features | Spawns (day / night) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Lint Hollow** (start) | centre (38,40), floor 12×10 | floor L7, rim L13–14 | earth, stone walls | Dead bushes (branches), 6 loose earth blocks, one Lintling. A dark 6-block tunnel (2-high, roofed: tests the cutaway) with stairs up to the exit at (50,42). A \"darkness zone\" (ambient .15 until a torch is placed at the marked spot) | 1 scripted Lintling |\n| **Gingham Glen** | x 44–100, y 44–104 (minus the town) | L9 ± 2, gentle hills | grass / 3 earth / stone | Tufts (1 per 12 cells), cotton puffs, thimbleberry bushes near the town, buttercups, a shallow stream (1-deep water) from (30,58) winding to the coast at (18,132), trees in small groves | Lintling 70%, Dyed Lintling 30% / Lintling 40%, Mothlet 60% |\n| **Thimbleton** | banner spot (72,76) on a cobble plaza 5×5 | L9 flattened in radius 12 | grass, cobble ruins | Ruined foundations: three 1-high cobble outlines of old houses (hints for room shapes), a broken well, a pond 3×4 (decor water), the east road (planks path) to (143,76), the Thimbleton Bobbin Portal at (70,80) | none inside the border |\n| **Corduroy Crags** | x 4–60, y 4–56 | L11–20 ridges | stone, gravel on slopes, grass in hollows | Exposed copper (levels 7–12) and coal (8–14) veins as blobs, 4–7 blocks each, Poisson-spaced. The Button Quarry. A Bobbin Portal at the Hollow exit (52,44) and at the Quarry rim (34,20). The Ancient Button on a stone pillar ledge at (48,8), L19 (a stairs puzzle) | Lintling, Pinhog / Lintling, Pinhog |\n| **Button Quarry** | open pit (22,18), 16×14, floor L6 | rim L15 | stone terraces | Ramp from the east, terraces with coal and copper, 4 cobble pillars, boss arena floor 12×10. Sir Buttonsworth sleeps here (wakes on entry after M10) | Pinhog (before the boss) |\n| **Tweedwood** | x 92–140, y 6–60 | L10 ± 2 | grass / earth | Dense voxel trees: trunk 3–5 Plaid Logs, Pompom leaf blob radius 2, Poisson spacing ~4. Puffballs in shade, bluebells at the edges. The Lint Camp at (116,30): Lintwick in a Knot Cage (a 1×1 object, HP 30, tier 2), 3 Dyed Lintlings, knot-fence decor. A hollow tree with the Ancient Button at (134,52). A Bobbin Portal at (110,36) | Dyed Lintling / Mothlet, Dyed Lintling |\n| **Calico Coast** | x 4–60, y 100–140 | sand L7–8; sea L5–6 water where height < 7 | sand / sand / stone | Beach, dunes, cotton puffs, a shipwreck stamp (plank hull) holding the Ancient Button at (22,126), a Bobbin Portal at (30,116) | Pinhog / Pinhog, Mothlet |\n| **Frayed Verge** | x 92–99, y 92–140 | L9 | frayed cloth patches | The approach to the Knot Wall; a Bobbin Portal at (94,110) | Frayed Knight (night only, plus 2 fixed guards by day near the gate) |\n| **The Knot Wall** | x 99–100, y 92–141, up to L17 | — | knot (tier 3) | The **Knot Gate** at y 112–114 (3 wide × 5 high) is the only way through (Seam Ripper) | — |\n| **The Fraying** | x 101–140, y 94–140 | L9 ± 3 with void holes | frayed / earth / stone | Void holes (columns emptied entirely, Backing Cloth included: falling in = unravel respawn), dead trees, ash weather, purple ambient. The **Knotted Spire** at (124,124): a 9×9 base of knot and frayed blocks up to L22, with an outer spiral ramp 2 wide (stairs blocks), and a pedestal with the Golden Thread fragment on top | Frayed Knight, Knotbrute (rare) / the same, ×1.5 |\n| **The Rift** | (96,80), radius 3 | void | — | A frayed hole east of town that is the siege's spawn point. Re-stitched at the chapter's end (a wave turns it into meadow) | Frayed Knight at night |\n\nStamps (`DQ.WORLD.stamps`, ASCII layers bottom to top with a legend; `' '` means keep the existing block, `.` air):\n- `lintHollow`, `thimbletonRuins`, `buttonQuarry`, `lintCamp`, `shipwreck`, `knotGate`, `knottedSpire`, `rift`\n- `portalPad` (×6), `demoTown` (the attract/title diorama: Lv4 Thimbleton), `beeMeadow` (48×48 Bee world)\n- `beat_*` stamps for dev story beats (the rooms a player would have built by then)\n\nWorldgen order:\n1. heightmap\n2. layers\n3. ores\n4. water fill\n5. trees\n6. plants (objects)\n7. stamps\n8. portals\n9. `escape` sweep\n10. nav build\n11. `world.base` snapshot\n\nMust be deterministic: test it by `world.hash()` equality across two runs.\n\n### 7.2 Blocks (`DQ.BLOCKS`)\nTexture names refer to the patterns in §8.1. \"tier\" is the minimum tool tier to break it (∞ = never). Every face has stitched seams.\n\n| id | key | Name | hp | tier | Drops | Placeable | Texture (top / side) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | backing | Backing Cloth | ∞ | ∞ | — | no | navy felt with a square stitch grid | level 0 |\n| 2 | earth | Corduroy Earth | 6 | 1 | earth | yes | brown cord crosshatch / vertical cord ribs | |\n| 3 | grass | Gingham Turf | 6 | 1 | earth | no (gives earth) | green gingham checks / earth with a 3-texel felt fringe | |\n| 4 | sand | Calico Sand | 4 | 1 | sand | yes | pale yellow calico, tiny orange florets | |\n| 5 | gravel | Button Gravel | 8 | 1 | pebble ×2 | no | grey with little round bumps | |\n| 6 | stone | Tweed Stone | 20 | 2 | stone | yes | grey herringbone tweed | |\n| 7 | copperOre | Copper Sequin Seam | 30 | 2 | copperOre | no | tweed with copper sequins (glint frame) | |\n| 8 | coal | Charcloth Seam | 24 | 2 | coal | no | tweed with black felt lumps | |\n| 9 | log | Plaid Log | 12 | 1 | log | yes | stitched rings / brown bark with tartan stripes | |\n| 10 | leaves | Pompom Leaves | 2 | 1 | branch 35% | no | green bobbles with lit tops | |\n| 11 | frayed | Frayed Cloth | 24 | 2 | frayedScrap | no | dark plum, torn weave, loose threads | |\n| 12 | knot | Black Knot | 60 | 3 | blackYarn | no | tangled black-violet yarn loops | |\n| 13 | water | Satin Water | — | — | — | no | blue satin shimmer (translucent) | static; 2+ deep blocks walkers |\n| 20 | cobble | Cobble Patch | 22 | 2 | cobble | yes | grey quilted rounded stones | |\n| 21 | planks | Plank Patch | 10 | 1 | planks | yes | tan boards with stitched seams | |\n| 22 | thatch | Straw Thatch | 4 | 1 | thatch | yes | golden straw courses | |\n| 23 | feltRed | Red Felt Patch | 6 | 1 | feltRed | yes | felt with a diamond stitch | also Blue (24) and Yellow (25) |\n| 26 | glow | Glow Patch | 6 | 1 | glow | yes | pale gold felt with a stitched star (emissive) | light 48 |\n| 27 | stairsPlank | Plank Stairs | 10 | 1 | stairsPlank | yes | planks (wedge) | `rot` from facing |\n| 28 | stairsCobble | Cobble Stairs | 22 | 2 | stairsCobble | yes | cobble (wedge) | |\n| 29 | tangle | Tangle | 12 | 1 | — | no | black yarn ball | Gnarlgrim residue, vanishes after 20 s |\n| 30 | gildedFelt | Gilded Felt | 6 | 1 | gildedFelt | yes | gold felt with sparkle | S3 reward |\n\n### 7.3 Items and materials (`DQ.ITEMS`)\nEvery item has an `icon`: a block cube rendered from the atlas, `E.shapeSprite` for objects, or a 16×16 `E.sprite` string (marked ✎) to author. Descriptions are in Dragon Quest style; examples are given for a few.\n\n| id | Name | Kind | From | Use / notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| earth, sand, stone, log, cobble, planks, thatch, feltRed/Blue/Yellow, glow, stairsPlank, stairsCobble, gildedFelt | (blocks) | block | breaking or crafting | place |\n| pebble ✎ | Pebble | material | gravel | Cobble Club, Weapon Rack. \"A little stone with big dreams.\" |\n| copperOre ✎ | Copper Ore | material | copper seams | Copper Ingot |\n| coal ✎ | Charcloth | material | coal seams | ingots, Hearth Pot, Forge |\n| branch ✎ | Branch | material | dead bushes, leaves | torches, doors, club |\n| straw ✎ | Straw | material | tufts (1–2) | beds, thatch |\n| grain ✎ | Wild Grain | ingredient | tufts 30% | buns, stew |\n| cotton ✎ | Cotton Puff | material | cotton puffs (2) | thread, beds, felt, vest |\n| thread ✎ | Thread | material | crafted | doors, lanterns, vest |\n| lint ✎ | Lint | material | Lintlings, Lintwick | torches. \"Fluffy, flammable, faintly judgemental.\" |\n| mothDust ✎ | Moth Dust | material | Mothlets | Glow Patch, Moth Lantern |\n| pins ✎ | Pins | material | Pinhogs | Pin Trap |\n| steelThread ✎ | Steel Thread | material | Frayed Knights 70%, Sir Buttonsworth ×3 | Ballista, Seam Ripper |\n| blackYarn ✎ | Black Yarn | material | Knotbrutes, Black Knots | Gilded Felt alternate recipe (2 feltYellow + 1 blackYarn → 4, after S3). \"Tangled beyond all reason.\" |\n| frayedScrap ✎ | Frayed Scrap | material | Frayed Cloth | fuel: replaces the 1 coal in the Hearth Pot's own recipe |\n| copperIngot ✎ | Copper Ingot | material | Forge | gear, ballista, lantern |\n| dyeRed/Blue/Yellow ✎ | Rose / Bluebell / Buttercup Dye | material | crafted from berries / bluebells / buttercups | felt |\n| thimbleberry ✎ | Thimbleberry | food | berry bushes (2) | eat raw: Belly +5. Bun, stew, red dye |\n| bluebell ✎, buttercup ✎ | flowers | material | flowers | dyes |\n| puffball ✎ | Puffball | ingredient | Tweedwood | roast, stew |\n| roastPuffball ✎ | Roast Puffball | food | Hearth Pot | Belly +20, HP +5 |\n| bun ✎ | Thimbleberry Bun | food | Hearth Pot | Belly +35, HP +10 |\n| stew ✎ | Glen Stew | food | Hearth Pot | Belly +60, HP +20 |\n| pie ✎ | Marigold's Hearty Pie | food | Marigold only | Belly +100, HP full |\n| darningStick ✎ | Darning Stick | weapon | start | atk 3, blockDmg 6, tier 1 |\n| cobbleClub ✎ | Cobble Club | weapon | Bench | atk 7, blockDmg 10, tier 2 |\n| copperBodkin ✎ | Copper Bodkin | weapon | Forge | atk 12, blockDmg 12, tier 2, swing ×0.9 time |\n| seamRipper ✎ | Seam Ripper | weapon | Forge | atk 9, blockDmg 20, tier 3; ×4 against Black Knots and the Heart Knot |\n| quiltedVest ✎ | Quilted Vest | body | Bench | def +3 |\n| copperBuckler ✎ | Copper Buckler | shield | Forge | def +4 |\n| heartpatch ✎ | Heartpatch | use | quests M5, M8, M10 | max HP +10 (consumed on use, with a sparkle and jingle) |\n| banner ✎ | Banner of Mending | key | M1 reward | plant at Thimbleton |\n| hallPattern ✎ | Pattern: Quilters' Hall | key | Professor (M10) | place the Pattern |\n| goldenNeedle ✎ | Golden Needle | key | Sir Buttonsworth | Seam Ripper |\n| goldenThread ✎ | Golden Thread (fragment) | key | Spire top | story |\n| ancientButton ✎ | Ancient Button | key | 3 hidden | S3 |\n| goldenThimble ✎ | Golden Thimble | key | S3 reward | unlocks Gilded Felt |\n\nItem counts and sources above are the balance defaults. The Dev → Tuning sliders scale drops, damage and drains on top of them; balance changes to the tables themselves go in the data files.\n\n### 7.4 Recipes (`DQ.RECIPES`: station, inputs → output, notion trigger)\n\n| Recipe | Station | Inputs → Output | Notion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wick Torch | Pocket | 1 branch + 1 lint → 1 torch | pickup lint (Hollow) |\n| Mending Bench | Pocket | 3 branch + 4 earth → 1 bench | banner planted (Granny teaches) |\n| Straw Bed | Bench | 4 straw + 1 cotton → 1 strawBed | pickup straw |\n| Lattice Door | Bench | 3 branch → 1 latticeDoor | banner planted |\n| Storage Chest | Bench | 2 log + 2 branch → 1 chest | M3 reward |\n| Planks | Bench | 1 log → 3 planks | pickup log |\n| Thread | Bench | 2 cotton → 2 thread | pickup cotton |\n| Straw Thatch | Bench | 2 straw → 3 thatch | pickup straw |\n| Rose / Bluebell / Buttercup Dye | Bench | 2 thimbleberry / bluebell / buttercup → 1 dye | pickup the flower or berry, at Lv3 |\n| Cobble Club | Bench | 2 branch + 3 pebble → 1 | pickup pebble |\n| Cobble Patch | Bench | 1 stone + 1 earth → 2 cobble | Lv2 |\n| Stool | Bench | 2 planks → 1 | Lv2 |\n| Plank Table | Bench | 4 planks → 1 | Lv2 |\n| Plank Door | Bench | 2 planks + 1 thread → 1 | Lv2 |\n| Weapon Rack | Bench | 3 planks + 2 pebble → 1 | M6 start |\n| Plank Stairs | Bench | 2 planks → 2 | Lv2 |\n| Cobble Stairs | Bench | 2 cobble → 2 | Lv3 |\n| Quilted Vest | Bench | 4 cotton + 2 thread → 1 | Lv3 |\n| Felt Patch (colour) | Bench | 2 cotton + 1 dye → 4 felt | Lv3 |\n| Hearth Pot | Bench | 4 stone + 1 coal (or frayedScrap) → 1 | M8 start |\n| Thimble Forge | Bench | 6 stone + 2 coal + 2 cobble → 1 | M9 start |\n| Pin Trap | Bench | 3 pins + 1 planks → 2 | Lv4 |\n| Glow Patch | Bench | 1 mothDust + 1 feltYellow → 2 glow | pickup mothDust, at Lv3 |\n| Moth Lantern | Bench | 1 copperIngot + 1 mothDust + 1 thread → 1 | Lv4 |\n| Gilded Felt | Bench | 2 feltYellow + 1 copperIngot (or 1 blackYarn) → 4 | S3 reward |\n| Roast Puffball | Hearth | 1 puffball → 1 | pickup puffball |\n| Thimbleberry Bun | Hearth | 2 thimbleberry + 1 grain → 1 | Hearth placed |\n| Glen Stew | Hearth | 2 puffball + 1 thimbleberry + 1 grain → 1 | M8 reward |\n| Copper Ingot | Forge | 1 copperOre + 1 coal → 1 | Forge placed |\n| Copper Bodkin | Forge | 2 copperIngot + 1 log → 1 | Forge placed |\n| Copper Buckler | Forge | 2 copperIngot + 2 planks → 1 | Forge placed |\n| Bobbin Ballista | Forge | 2 log + 2 copperIngot + 2 steelThread → 1 | M10 (Professor) |\n| Seam Ripper | Forge | 1 goldenNeedle + 2 copperIngot + 2 steelThread → 1 | Golden Needle picked up |\n\n### 7.5 Objects (`DQ.OBJECTS`; each has an `E.SHAPES` entry, sized for the 26-unit hero)\n| id | Name | Cells | Solid | Light | Behaviour | Shape notes (materials) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| bench | Mending Bench | 1 | yes | — | crafting station | plank table, a pincushion, 2 spools, scissors (oak, wool, iron) |\n| torch | Wick Torch | 1 | no | 64, `#ffb060` | room light | stick + lint wick + `flames` |\n| lantern | Moth Lantern | 1 | no | 96, `#ffe7a0` | room light | copper cage, glow material |\n| latticeDoor | Lattice Door | 1×2 high | passable | — | door, HP 30 | crossed branches, two leaves that swing |\n| plankDoor | Plank Door | 1×2 high | passable | — | door, HP 50 | planks with a stitched heart |\n| strawBed | Straw Bed | 1 | low (z 6) | — | sleep slot | frame + straw + a patchwork quilt blanket (feltRed/Blue checks) |\n| table | Plank Table | 1 | yes | — | mess hall | core `table` with planks |\n| stool | Stool | 1 | low | — | seat | core `stool` |\n| chest | Storage Chest | 1 | yes | — | 20 slots, Town Chest flag | core `chest` |\n| hearthPot | Hearth Pot | 1 | yes | 48, `#ff8040` | cooking station | stone ring, iron pot, `flames` |\n| forge | Thimble Forge | 1 | yes | 56, `#ff7030` | smithing station | a giant thimble-shaped furnace with a glowing mouth |\n| weaponRack | Weapon Rack | 1 | yes | — | guard post | planks with 2 clubs |\n| pinTrap | Pin Trap | 1 | no | — | trap | a board with coloured pin heads |\n| ballista | Bobbin Ballista | 1 | yes | — | turret, HP 150 | wooden frame, steel-thread bowstring, a spool bolt |\n| banner | Banner of Mending | 1 | yes | 80, `#ffd870` | town core, HP 300 | pole plus a cloth banner, drawn in code (sine flutter) with a stripe per level |\n| portal | Bobbin Portal | 1×2 high | no | 40, `#c8a0ff` | travel | a bobbin-shaped arch with swirling thread (animated in code) |\n| cage | Knot Cage | 1 | yes | — | Lintwick, HP 30, tier 2 | knot bars |\n| tuft, cottonPuff, berryBush, bluebell, buttercup, puffball, deadBush | plants | 1 | no | — | harvest, regrow 1 day | core `grass`/`bush`/`flowers` recoloured; cotton balls and berries added as parts |\n| ancientButton | Ancient Button | 1 | no | glint | collectible | a big gold 4-hole button on a stand |\n| lostBundle | Lost Bundle | 1 | no | — | KO stash | a patch-sack |\n\n### 7.6 Rooms (`DQ.ROOMS`, checked in this priority order)\n| Type | Requirements (in addition to the room rule) | Cheer | maxAwards | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Quilters' Hall | Built from the Hall Pattern (complete), interior 50–64 cells | 100 | 1 | Landmark, plus Professor's comfort |\n| Guard Post | Weapon Rack + 2 lights | 30 | 1 | Mortimer's comfort; he stands watch |\n| Smithy | Thimble Forge + Chest | 30 | 1 | Forge works faster ×1.5 inside |\n| Kitchen | Hearth Pot + Chest | 25 | 1 | Marigold cooks here |\n| Mess Hall | Plank Table + 2 Stools | 25 | 1 | Supper spot; residents eat |\n| Workshop | Mending Bench + Chest | 25 | 1 | Professor's comfort |\n| Bedroom | ≥ 1 Straw Bed | 20 | 3 | Sleep slots = beds; Wren's and Lintwick's comfort |\n| Snug | (the room rule only) | 5 | 3 | — |\n\n### 7.7 Town levels (`DQ.LEVELS`)\n| Lv | Cheer | Border r (side) | Unlocks | Arrives |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0 | 10 (21×21) | base recipes | Wren, at the planting |\n| 2 | 40 | 13 (27×27) | cobble, stool, table, plank door, plank stairs, Town Chest designation | Mortimer |\n| 3 | 130 | 16 (33×33) | dyes, felt, quilted vest, cobble stairs, glow patch | Marigold |\n| 4 | 250 | 18 (37×37) | pin trap, moth lantern | Professor Selvage (brings the Hall Pattern) |\n| 5 | 450 | 20 (41×41) | Chapter clear; Hearty Pie served to everyone | — (Lintwick joins through S1 at any level ≥ 2) |\n\nExpected pacing (keep it when balancing):\n- Bedroom (20) + Workshop (25) → Lv2.\n- + Guard Post (30) + Mess Hall (25) + M5/M6 rewards (25) + bubbles (about 15) → Lv3.\n- + Kitchen (25) + Smithy (30) + M8/M9 rewards (35) + S1 (20) + bubbles (about 30) → Lv4.\n- + Hall (100) + boss victory (+150) → Lv5.\n\n### 7.8 Characters\nAll humans are `E.Humanoid` with `build: 'chibi'` unless noted. Faces use `face: { eyes: 'big' }`. Portraits come from `rig.drawPortrait`.\n\n| Who | Role | Look (Humanoid / Blob options) | Voice (Animalese profile) | Personality, tics, sample lines |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **The Builder** (player, default \"Patch\") | Silent hero | Size 1.0. A: `hair:'spiky'`, `hat:{style:'band',color:'#c8443a'}`, `outfit:'tunic'` denim `#3a5f9a` with patch trim `#e8c870`. B: `hair:'ponytail'`, `outfit:'robe'` (apron dress) `#4a8a5a`. Skin `#f2c39a`, a tool-belt colour | silent | Choices only |\n| **Granny Gossamer** | The Great Quilter; voice from the sky | No body. Portrait: a glowing golden spool with kind half-moon eyes and a needle \"hairpin\" (custom portrait function) | 165 Hz, range ±25%, triangle, formant 0.9, slow, vibrato 5 Hz 3% | Warm, scatterbrained, fond of \"dearie\" and \"my little stitch\". \"Wakey wakey, dearie! Oh good, you're not a pincushion. I'd hate to have stitched you together for nothing.\" / \"Frayvern pulled the Golden Thread right out of the world, and everything came apart at the seams. Worse, he swallowed everyone's Knack! Not a soul can make so much as a potholder.\" / \"But you still have the Knack. You're a Builder, dearie!\" |\n| **Wren Tuck** | First resident; eager kid | Size 0.85, `hair:'ponytail'` orange `#e07a2a`, `outfit:'shirt'` green `#5aa04a`, freckles drawn on the portrait | 330 Hz ±35%, pulse 25%, formant 1.25, fast | Breathless, curious, invents words (\"bildering\"). \"Whoa! Are you a monster? You don't LOOK like a monster. Monsters don't usually wave.\" / \"You MADE that? With your hands? On PURPOSE?!\" / \"Granny says people used to sleep on things called 'beds'. Do they bite?\" |\n| **Mortimer Bodkin** | Old guard, grump | `build:'bulky'` size 1.05, `hair:'bald'`, a white beard drawn on the portrait, `hat:'helmet'` dented, `outfit:'coat'` grey `#6a6a78`, `armor:true`, weapon `'club'` | 110 Hz ±15%, saw with 0.2 noise, formant 0.8, slow | \"Hmph.\" Everything was harder in his day. \"In my day we slept on rocks, and we were GRATEFUL for the rocks.\" / \"A club is just a stick with ambition.\" / (later) \"...Not bad, Builder. Not bad at all. Don't let it go to your head.\" |\n| **Marigold Purl** | Cook without a kitchen | Size 1.0, `hair:'long'` blonde, `hat:{style:'cap',color:'#ffffff'}` (chef), `outfit:'robe'` `#e8a0a0` with apron trim | 240 Hz ±30%, triangle, formant 1.1, bouncy alternation | Food puns, big feelings. \"I've got Glen Stew in my head and not a single pot to stew it in! It's a crock, I tell you. A CROCK!\" / \"Supper's on! Wash your paws, Lintwick.\" |\n| **Professor Hemsley Selvage** | Scholar of the Knack | `build:'heroic'` size 1.05 (tall, thin), `hair:'short'` grey, `hat:'pointed'` dark green, `outfit:'robe'` `#3a6a5a`, glasses drawn on the portrait and the rig head | 200 Hz ±20%, pulse12 (nasal), formant 1.15, fast | Long words, \"Fascinating!\" \"A functioning door! Do you realise nobody has hinged anything in forty years?\" / \"This Pattern is a schematic of considerable grandeur. And considerable lumber.\" |\n| **Lintwick** | Reformed Lintling | `E.Blob({ R: 7, colors: {base:'#cfcad6', dk:'#9a94a8', lt:'#f0eef4'}, feet: true, mouth: true, face: 'front' })` plus a fuzz outline (dithered edge) and button eyes drawn over the eyes | 520 Hz ±40%, sine with an upward chirp, formant 1.4 | Third person, sweet. \"Lintwick not bad monster! Lintwick just fuzzy!\" / \"Lintwick want bed. Soft bed. Lintwick will not shed on it. ...Much.\" |\n| **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** | Frayvern's general | `build:'bulky'` size 2.6, colours black and violet yarn, `eyeGlow` magenta, `cape` (tattered threads), `hat:'crown'` recoloured as knotted spikes, a glowing Heart Knot drawn on the chest | 70 Hz ±10%, saw plus a waveshaper drive, formant 0.7 | Boastful, knot puns. \"YOU! The needle in my side! I'll tie you in knots, little Builder!\" / \"I'm... unravelling...!\" |\n| **Sir Buttonsworth** | Button Golem mini-boss | `build:'bulky'` size 2.0, tan felt `#c8a878`, big button eyes and a belly button drawn on, `weapon: null` | 90 Hz, square, formant 0.75 | Pompous. \"HALT! None shall pass without a proper fastening!\" |\n| **Frayvern** | The dragon (seen only as a silhouette) | A huge moth-winged dragon silhouette drawn with `px.poly` in the sky during 2 cutscenes | 55 Hz saw with an echo (delay node) | \"Mend all the patches you like, Builder. I hold the Golden Thread, and the whole quilt is mine to pull.\" |\n\n### 7.9 Monsters (`DQ.MONSTERS`; speeds in units/s, aggro in blocks)\n| id | Name | Body | HP | Atk | Def | Speed | Aggro | Moves (wind-up telegraphs) | Drops |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| lintling | Lintling | Blob R6 `#b8b4c0`, fuzz edge, button eyes, `mouth:true` | 8 | 4 | 1 | 34 | 7 | Hop chase; lunge (squash wind .35 s, leap 60) | lint 100%, cotton 15% |\n| dyedLintling | Dyed Lintling | Blob R6 `#e88ab8` | 16 | 7 | 2 | 38 | 8 | Double-hop lunge (.3 s) | lint 100%, dyeRed 25% |\n| mothlet | Mothlet | Blob R5 `wings:true`, `mouth:'fangs'`, dusty violet; flies at z + 18..28 | 10 | 6 | 1 | 48 | 10 | Circles; swoop dive (rises .4 s, dives at 140); night only | mothDust 100% |\n| pinhog | Pinhog | Blob R7 `feet:true` with 10 coloured pins drawn radially | 22 | 9 | 5 | 30 (roll 110) | 8 | Curl (.6 s wind, shake), roll charge for 1.2 s, immune from the front while rolling, dizzy 1.2 s after hitting a wall | pins 80%, pebble 30% |\n| frayedKnight | Frayed Knight | Humanoid `build:'heroic'` size 1.1, a muslin \"dress-form\" mannequin (`#e8dcc0`) with frayed hems, `eyeGlow:'#b070ff'`, `weapon:'sword'` recoloured as a long needle-lance | 40 | 12 | 8 | 40 | 9 | `stance:'ready'`; `thrust` (.3 s wind, lunge); `spin` when surrounded | steelThread 70%, frayedScrap 50% |\n| knotbrute | Knotbrute | Humanoid `build:'bulky'` size 1.4, navy yarn `#2a2a48`, `hunch:.3`, `eyeGlow` red, knot bumps on the shoulders | 60 | 14 | 6 | 26 | 10 | `haymaker` (.45 s); block smash 25; shoulder charge (.5 s wind) | blackYarn 100% |\n| buttonGolem | Sir Buttonsworth | §7.8 | 220 | 14 | 8 | 30 | arena | Slam, Button Volley, Stomp Charge, summon at 50% (§6.12) | goldenNeedle, steelThread ×3 |\n| gnarlgrim | Gnarlgrim | §7.8 | 600 | 18 | 25 (0 Tangled) | 34 (charge 140) | town | §6.12 | goldenThread (story) |","numLines":280,"startLine":839,"totalLines":1613}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jjn7E9TQVZvJFeyPoJtcvy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
