{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3ZAi1wBAswAG91Bvb6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PHchnXSbNjJQysuy8FZB6J","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":1118,"limit":260},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14642,"cache_read_input_tokens":466218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14642},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"57416f15-4311-4db5-8baa-cc80b894b066","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:24.915Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3ZANBtZjgJH1KFkzxb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PHchnXSbNjJQysuy8FZB6J":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":1118,"limit":260}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHchnXSbNjJQysuy8FZB6J","type":"tool_result","content":"1118\t| gnarlgrim | Gnarlgrim | §7.8 | 600 | 18 | 25 (0 Tangled) | 34 (charge 140) | town | §6.12 | goldenThread (story) |\n1119\t\n1120\t**Siege waves** (sizes × `tuning.siegeSize`):\n1121\t- **W1:** 8 Lintlings + 3 Dyed Lintlings (east road)\n1122\t- **W2:** 6 Lintlings + 4 Pinhogs + 3 Mothlets (east plus north)\n1123\t- **W3:** 4 Lintlings + 4 Frayed Knights + 3 Knotbrutes (east plus the Rift)\n1124\t- **Boss:** Gnarlgrim, with summons at phases 2 and 3\n1125\t\n1126\t**Bee raid:** 3 waves × (4 + 2 per player) Lintlings, then Pinhogs, then 1 Knotbrute per 2 players.\n1127\t\n1128\t### 7.10 Story and quests: \"Chapter One: A Stitch in Time\"\n1129\tEach quest lists the giver, steps (conditions from §6.15), the reward, and its cutscenes. Main quests are M1–M14; side quests S1–S3 are optional but count toward Cheer.\n1130\t\n1131\t**Prologue (intro crawl, 4 pages).**\n1132\t1. \"Long ago, Granny Gossamer stitched the Patchwork Realm from a thousand scraps of light.\"\n1133\t2. \"Its people had the Knack: whatever they dreamed, their hands could make.\"\n1134\t3. \"Then came Frayvern, the Unraveller. He pulled the Golden Thread from the heart of the world, and swallowed every last bit of Knack.\"\n1135\t4. \"Now the realm frays at its edges... and nobody remembers how to make a bed.\"\n1136\t\n1137\t**M1 \"Come Undone\"** (Granny; Lint Hollow). The opening cutscene is darkness, then Granny's golden box: \"Wakey wakey, dearie!\"\n1138\t\n1139\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1140\t|---|---|---|\n1141\t| 1 | Look around (tutorial prompts for move, camera turn and jump) | `{ at: 'hollowLedge' }` |\n1142\t| 2 | Break 3 Corduroy Earth | `{ have: { earth: 3 } }` |\n1143\t| 3 | Defeat the Lintling (\"A Lintling bounces into view!\") | `{ killed: { lintling: 1 } }` |\n1144\t| 4 | Craft a Wick Torch from the Bag (Notion on picking up Lint) | `{ crafted: 'torch' }` |\n1145\t| 5 | Light the dark tunnel (place the torch at the marked spot; the darkness lifts) | `{ placed: 'torch', at: 'tunnelMark' }` |\n1146\t| 6 | Climb out of the Hollow | `{ at: 'hollowExit' }` |\n1147\t\n1148\tReward: the Banner of Mending (key). Cutscene: the frayed world revealed, a camera pan over the Glen to the ruins. Granny: \"Plant this where Thimbleton used to be, dearie. Folks will come. They always come for a light.\"\n1149\t\n1150\t**M2 \"Plant the Banner\"** (Granny).\n1151\t\n1152\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1153\t|---|---|---|\n1154\t| 1 | Reach the ruins of Thimbleton | `{ at: 'bannerSpot', radius: 3 }` |\n1155\t| 2 | Plant the Banner (use it) | `{ flag: 'bannerPlanted' }` |\n1156\t\n1157\tPlanting cutscene: the banner rises, a gold light ring spreads, the border stitch runs around, and \"Thimbleton has been founded!\" appears. Wren walks in from the road. Granny teaches the Mending Bench (a Pocket recipe) and Lattice Door notions.\n1158\t\n1159\t**M3 \"Wren's Bed\"** (Wren).\n1160\t\n1161\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1162\t|---|---|---|\n1163\t| 1 | Gather 4 Straw from tufts | `{ have: { straw: 4 } }` |\n1164\t| 2 | Gather 1 Cotton Puff | `{ have: { cotton: 1 } }` |\n1165\t| 3 | Make and place a Mending Bench | `{ placed: 'bench' }` |\n1166\t| 4 | Craft a Straw Bed and a Lattice Door | `{ crafted: ['strawBed', 'latticeDoor'] }` |\n1167\t| 5 | Build a Bedroom: walls 2 blocks high, a door, the bed and a light inside | `{ room: 'bedroom' }` |\n1168\t\n1169\tReward: Cheer +10 and the Storage Chest notion. Wren: \"It's... a BED. I'm going to sleep in it for a hundred years!\" Her bedtime that night is her first heart bubble.\n1170\t\n1171\t**M4 \"A Place to Make Things\"** (Wren).\n1172\t\n1173\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1174\t|---|---|---|\n1175\t| 1 | Craft a Storage Chest | `{ crafted: 'chest' }` |\n1176\t| 2 | Build a Workshop (bench + chest in a room) | `{ room: 'workshop' }` |\n1177\t\n1178\tReward: Cheer +10. This is likely Lv2, and Mortimer arrives at dawn (\"Hmph. Another dreamer.\").\n1179\t\n1180\t**M5 \"Club Med\"** (Mortimer).\n1181\t\n1182\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1183\t|---|---|---|\n1184\t| 1 | Gather 3 Pebbles in the Crags (marker on the nearest gravel) | `{ have: { pebble: 3 } }` |\n1185\t| 2 | Craft a Cobble Club | `{ crafted: 'cobbleClub' }` |\n1186\t| 3 | Show it to Mortimer | `{ talk: 'mortimer' }` |\n1187\t\n1188\tReward: Spin Stitch technique (cutscene: Mortimer demonstrates on a straw dummy), Heartpatch #1, Cheer +10.\n1189\t\n1190\t**M6 \"Guard Duty\"** (Mortimer). Step: build a Guard Post (a Weapon Rack, from the notion at the quest start, plus 2 lights) → `{ room: 'guardPost' }`. Reward: Cheer +15. From now on Mortimer patrols at night.\n1191\t\n1192\t**M7 \"Supper Time\"** (Wren and Mortimer, a joint talk). Step: build a Mess Hall (table + 2 stools) → `{ room: 'messHall' }`. Reward: Cheer +10. This is likely Lv3: Marigold arrives (\"Is that a TABLE? I could weep!\").\n1193\t\n1194\t**M8 \"Hearth and Home\"** (Marigold).\n1195\t\n1196\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1197\t|---|---|---|\n1198\t| 1 | Mine 4 Tweed Stone and 1 Charcloth (needs the Cobble Club; marker on the nearest coal) | `{ have: { stone: 4, coal: 1 } }` |\n1199\t| 2 | Craft a Hearth Pot | `{ crafted: 'hearthPot' }` |\n1200\t| 3 | Build a Kitchen (Hearth Pot + chest) | `{ room: 'kitchen' }` |\n1201\t| 4 | Bring Marigold 2 Puffballs from Tweedwood | `{ have: { puffball: 2 }, talk: 'marigold' }` |\n1202\t\n1203\tReward: Glen Stew notion, Heartpatch #2, Cheer +15. Marigold starts cooking.\n1204\t\n1205\t**M9 \"Copper Bottomed\"** (Mortimer, then Marigold).\n1206\t\n1207\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1208\t|---|---|---|\n1209\t| 1 | Craft a Thimble Forge | `{ crafted: 'forge' }` |\n1210\t| 2 | Build a Smithy (Forge + chest) | `{ room: 'smithy' }` |\n1211\t| 3 | Smelt 2 Copper Ingots | `{ crafted: { copperIngot: 2 } }` |\n1212\t| 4 | Forge a Copper Bodkin | `{ crafted: 'copperBodkin' }` |\n1213\t\n1214\tReward: Cheer +20. This is likely Lv4: the Professor arrives with the Hall Pattern (\"Fascinating! A functioning door!\").\n1215\t\n1216\t**M10 \"The Quilters' Hall\"** (Professor).\n1217\t\n1218\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1219\t|---|---|---|\n1220\t| 1 | Place the Hall Pattern inside the town (a suggested site is outlined NE of the banner, 11×9) | `{ flag: 'hallPlaced' }` |\n1221\t| 2 | Designate a Town Chest so residents can help | `{ flag: 'townChest' }` |\n1222\t| 3 | Complete the Pattern | `{ pattern: 'hall' }` |\n1223\t\n1224\tThe Pattern (outer 11×9, interior 9×7 = 63 cells) has 129 cells:\n1225\t- level 1: 35 Cobble (the perimeter minus the door)\n1226\t- level 2: 35 Planks\n1227\t- level 3: 36 Planks (a lintel over the door)\n1228\t- level 4: 18 Felt crenellations, 6 per colour, on every other perimeter cell\n1229\t- 1 Plank Door\n1230\t- 4 Moth Lanterns in the interior corners\n1231\t\n1232\t Reward: Cheer +100, Heartpatch #3, and the Bobbin Ballista notion. Revelation cutscene in the Hall: the Professor reads the old Pattern margins. \"The Golden Thread fragment lies atop the Knotted Spire, past the Knot Wall. Only a Seam Ripper can cut a Black Knot. And the only Golden Needle left is fastened to Sir Buttonsworth's chest.\"\n1233\t\n1234\t**M11 \"Needle in a Haystack\"** (Professor).\n1235\t\n1236\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1237\t|---|---|---|\n1238\t| 1 | Go to the Button Quarry | `{ at: 'quarryFloor' }` |\n1239\t| 2 | Defeat Sir Buttonsworth (intro cutscene) | `{ boss: 'buttonGolem' }` |\n1240\t| 3 | Forge the Seam Ripper (needs Steel Thread: the Golem drops 3, Frayed Knights more) | `{ crafted: 'seamRipper' }` |\n1241\t\n1242\tReward: Cheer +20.\n1243\t\n1244\t**M12 \"Rip It Up\"** (Professor).\n1245\t\n1246\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1247\t|---|---|---|\n1248\t| 1 | Cut through the Knot Gate (rip cutscene: the wall unpicks itself in a wave) | `{ flag: 'gateCut' }` |\n1249\t| 2 | Climb the Knotted Spire | `{ at: 'spireTop' }` |\n1250\t| 3 | Take the Golden Thread fragment | `{ have: { goldenThread: 1 } }` |\n1251\t\n1252\tCutscene: the thread glows, Frayvern's silhouette spreads across the sky (\"Mend all the patches you like...\"), and Gnarlgrim's roar echoes from the Rift. Granny: \"Hurry home, dearie, they're going after Thimbleton!\" Autosave.\n1253\t\n1254\t**M13 \"Hold the Line\"** (Mortimer).\n1255\t\n1256\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1257\t|---|---|---|\n1258\t| 1 | Return to Thimbleton (portal) | `{ at: 'bannerSpot', radius: 12 }` |\n1259\t| 2 | Talk to Mortimer, \"Ready?\" (Yes starts the siege prep; \"Not yet\" lets you prepare freely) | `{ flag: 'siegeStarted' }` |\n1260\t| 3 | Survive 3 waves | `{ siegeDone: true }` |\n1261\t\n1262\tMortimer suggests building at least 2 Ballistas and some Pin Traps (hint only).\n1263\t\n1264\t**M14 \"Gnarlgrim the Knotted\"**. Step: defeat Gnarlgrim → `{ boss: 'gnarlgrim' }`.\n1265\t\n1266\tFinale cutscene:\n1267\t1. Gnarlgrim unravels and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner.\n1268\t2. The Banner flares, and the Rift and the frayed patch east of town re-stitch: a wave of stitches turns void into meadow.\n1269\t3. Town Lv5.\n1270\t4. The party: residents dance and cheer, confetti scraps fly, fireworks particles burst, and Marigold serves Hearty Pies.\n1271\t5. Granny: \"You did it, my little stitch. One patch mended... and a great many to go.\"\n1272\t6. Results, then credits, then free play.\n1273\t\n1274\t**S1 \"Lintwick's Lament\"** (found at the Lint Camp, from Lv2).\n1275\t\n1276\t| # | Step | Condition |\n1277\t|---|---|---|\n1278\t| 1 | Break the Knot Cage (tier 2) | `{ flag: 'lintwickFreed' }` |\n1279\t| 2 | Lintwick follows you home (he walks or warps along) | `{ at: 'bannerSpot' }` |\n1280\t| 3 | Build him a Bedroom with at least one Felt block in its walls | `{ room: 'bedroom', felt: true }` |\n1281\t\n1282\tReward: Cheer +20 and daily Lint gifts.\n1283\t\n1284\t**S2 \"Bluebell Blues\"** (Wren, from Lv3). Steps: craft 4 Blue Felt → `{ crafted: { feltBlue: 4 } }`; place 8 Blue Felt blocks inside the border → `{ placedInTown: { feltBlue: 8 } }`. Reward: Cheer +15. Wren: \"It's like the sky came down to visit!\"\n1285\t\n1286\t**S3 \"Buttons of Old\"** (Professor, from Lv4). Step: find 3 Ancient Buttons (Coast shipwreck, Crags ledge, Tweedwood hollow tree; the map marks their regions with \"?\") → `{ have: { ancientButton: 3 } }`. Reward: Golden Thimble (Gilded Felt notion) and Cheer +30.\n1287\t\n1288\t**Talk variety.** Each resident has at least 6 idle lines that vary by time of day, mood, town level and quest state, plus reactions to the player's actions:\n1289\t- seeing a new room type: \"A KITCHEN!\"\n1290\t- Belly low: \"You look peckish, Builder.\"\n1291\t- the night: \"Lock the doors!\"\n1292\t\n1293\t### 7.11 Music (`DQ.SONGS`; original compositions, engine step format)\n1294\tThe leitmotif, **\"The Golden Thread\"**, is the seed every theme quotes. Melody in B♭ major, eighth notes (`steps: 2`):\n1295\t```\n1296\tF4 Bb4 C5 D5 | Eb5 - D5 C5 | Bb4 - G4 C5 | A4 - - - | F4 Bb4 C5 D5 | F5 - Eb5 D5 | C5 Bb4 A4 C5 | Bb4 - - -\n1297\tchords:  Bb | Eb | Gm | F | Bb | Bb7/D | Eb F | Bb\n1298\t```\n1299\t\n1300\t| Song | Use | Key / tempo / metre | Notes |\n1301\t|---|---|---|---|\n1302\t| \"Overture of Mending\" | Title | B♭, 116 bpm, 4/4 | Fanfare intro (square brass), the leitmotif in full, triangle bass, march drums |\n1303\t| \"Granny's Lullaby\" | Intro crawl, Granny moments | B♭, 72 bpm, 3/4 | Leitmotif slowed, sine and triangle |\n1304\t| \"Lint Hollow\" | Cave and tutorial | D dorian, 88 bpm | Plucky pulse arpeggios, sparse |\n1305\t| \"Thimbleton Days\" | Town (day) | F, 96 bpm, 3/4 waltz | 4 layers: base, `strings` (Lv2), `bells` (Lv3), `drums` (Lv4) |\n1306\t| \"Moonlit Hem\" | Night (anywhere) | A minor, 72 bpm | Soft triangle melody, the leitmotif in minor |\n1307\t| \"Gingham Glen\" | Glen and Coast | D, 112 bpm | Bright pulse melody, walking bass |\n1308\t| \"Corduroy Deep\" | Crags and Quarry | E minor, 92 bpm | Low saw drone, clinking noise percussion |\n1309\t| \"Tweedwood Rustle\" | Tweedwood | G, 100 bpm, 6/8 | Flute-like pulse12 |\n1310\t| \"The Fraying\" | Verge, Fraying, Spire | E phrygian, 66 bpm | Detuned pulses, dissonant intervals, slow noise swells |\n1311\t| \"Snip Snap Skirmish\" | Siege waves | C minor, 150 bpm | Driving bass, leitmotif fragments |\n1312\t| \"Sir Buttonsworth\" | Mini-boss | F minor, 140 bpm | Pompous march, comedic |\n1313\t| \"Gnarlgrim\" | Boss | G minor, 160 bpm | The leitmotif inverted. Layer `fury` from phase 3 |\n1314\t| \"Quilting Bee\" | Bee round | C, 128 bpm | Jaunty; layer `raid` comes in at the raid phase |\n1315\t| \"Patchwork Finale\" | Results and credits | B♭, 108 bpm | Medley: leitmotif, town waltz, triumphant ending |\n1316\t\n1317\tJingles (`loop: false`):\n1318\t\n1319\t| Jingle | Length | Character |\n1320\t|---|---|---|\n1321\t| Notion! | 1.2 s | harp gliss up |\n1322\t| Room Complete! | 2.5 s | fanfare |\n1323\t| Town Level Up! | 3.5 s | |\n1324\t| Quest Complete | 2 s | |\n1325\t| Item Get | 1 s | |\n1326\t| Resident Arrives | 2 s | |\n1327\t| Night Falls | 2 s | descending |\n1328\t| Morning | 1.5 s | rooster-ish pulse chirps |\n1329\t| Come Undone | 2.5 s | sad |\n1330\t| Wave Cleared | 1.5 s | |\n1331\t| Victory | 3 s | |\n1332\t| Zzz | 2 s | |\n1333\t\n1334\t### 7.12 Sound effects (`DQ.SFX`, engine voices; all from code)\n1335\t- **Blocks:**\n1336\t  - `hitSoft` (noise lowpass 900 Hz + triangle 180→120, 60 ms), `hitHard` (+ a 2 kHz click)\n1337\t  - `clink` (pulse 1800→2200, 50 ms, for under-tier)\n1338\t  - `rip` (noise bandpass 2.5 kHz → 700 Hz over 160 ms, then `pop`: sine 600→200, 40 ms)\n1339\t  - `stitch` (pulse12 880→1320, 40 ms + a soft click)\n1340\t  - `crumble` (Tangle and frayed breaks)\n1341\t- **Actions:**\n1342\t  - `swing` (noise whoosh), `spinCharge` (rising triangle), `spinRelease`, `jump`, `land`\n1343\t  - Footsteps by material: grass (soft noise), stone (click), wood (knock), sand (hiss), water (splash)\n1344\t- **Items and UI:**\n1345\t  - `pickup` (arpeggio 0-4-7, 90 ms), `notion`, `craft` (tok tok + a chime), `eat` (munch ×3)\n1346\t  - `zipper` (opening Satchel or Chest: a rising noise ratchet, 250 ms), `uiMove`, `uiConfirm`, `uiCancel`\n1347\t- **World:**\n1348\t  - `doorOpen` / `doorClose` (creaks with a pitch slide), `torchLight`, `portal` (swirl)\n1349\t  - `bubble` (two-note ding for Cheer), `levelUp`, `trap` (pins), `ballistaFire` (thwomp + whoosh), `ballistaReload` (click-clack)\n1350\t- **Combat:**\n1351\t  - `monsterHurt` (squeak per type: Lintling high, Knotbrute low), `monsterDie` (pop), `builderHurt`, `heartbeat`\n1352\t  - Boss: `slam` (boom + low rumble), `roar` (saw drive)\n1353\t  - Mothlet flaps, Pinhog roll rattle\n1354\t\n1355\t---\n1356\t## 8. Art direction and animation\n1357\t\n1358\tThe base is the engine's native look: low-res pixel buffer, shaded HD puppet rigs, stepped-alpha blends, canvas lighting, the 5×7 font and `E.font.title` logos. The new assets make it feel like a cosy patchwork-quilt reimagining of a block-building action RPG. Generic props may come from the engine library and the asset store (`node engine/tools/asset-find.mjs \"barrel\"`): barrels, crates, pots, signs, sacks, fences, rocks. Everything that defines the game's identity is made new: blocks, characters, monsters, furniture with a sewing twist, the banner, portals, UI, the logo.\n1359\t\n1360\t### 8.1 Block textures (16×16 texels per face, 1 texel ≈ 1 world unit)\n1361\tA texel's colour is one of the material's five tones from `E.tones(base)`: `deep`, `sh`, `base`, `lt`, `hi`. Some patterns add an accent colour, and seams use the thread colour. Common rules:\n1362\t- **Seam:** the outer ring (u or v = 0 or 15) is `deep`. A **running stitch** sits at ring 2 (u or v = 2 or 13): along positions 3–12, texels where `(along % 4) < 2` take the thread colour (default cream `#f1e6c8`; dark blocks use `#c8b890`). That gives each block its stitched-patch look.\n1363\t- **Faces:** top faces use the full tone set. Side faces shift one tone darker for faceA and two for faceB (§6.1.3). The pattern moves the tone by −1..+2 steps, as engine materials do.\n1364\t- **Variety:** 4 variants per material, made by offsetting each pattern's hash seed.\n1365\t\n1366\t| Pattern | Rule (u, v in 0..15) | Blocks (base colour) |\n1367\t|---|---|---|\n1368\t| `gingham` | Checks of 4×4: `((u>>2)+(v>>2))&1` → `base`/`lt`; where a light row crosses a light column → `hi` | grass top `#6cb84a` |\n1369\t| `fringe` | Earth side with the top 3 rows green felt and ragged yarn tufts (rows 3–4 at hashed u) | grass side |\n1370\t| `cord` | Sides: ribs, `u%3` → `sh`/`base`/`lt`. Tops: crosshatch | earth `#8a5a3a` |\n1371\t| `calico` | Base plus florets: hashed centres ~5 apart, centre texel accent `#e07a3a`, 4 petals `lt` | sand `#e8d08a` |\n1372\t| `bumps` | Discs of radius 1.5 on a jittered grid, lit top-left | gravel `#9a96a0` |\n1373\t| `tweed` | Herringbone: diagonal bands 2 wide that flip direction every 4 rows; speckles | stone `#8c8c9a` |\n1374\t| `sequins` | Tweed plus 3–4 discs (r 1.5) in `#d07a3a` with a `hi` glint. At draw time one sequin flashes white every ~2 s (overlay) | copper ore |\n1375\t| `lumps` | Tweed plus 3 black felt blobs `#2a2630` | coal |\n1376\t| `plaid` | Bark `#7a5032`, vertical stripes at u 4–5 and 11 in `#b0403a`, horizontal at v 7–8 in `#3a6a3a`; crossings darker | log side |\n1377\t| `rings` | Concentric rings every 2.5 texels, `sh`/`base`, a stitched outer ring, a centre dot | log top `#c89a62` |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"c4405de1-b7c3-4eed-ad21-4e5c32aab9b9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:24.922Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"| gnarlgrim | Gnarlgrim | §7.8 | 600 | 18 | 25 (0 Tangled) | 34 (charge 140) | town | §6.12 | goldenThread (story) |\n\n**Siege waves** (sizes × `tuning.siegeSize`):\n- **W1:** 8 Lintlings + 3 Dyed Lintlings (east road)\n- **W2:** 6 Lintlings + 4 Pinhogs + 3 Mothlets (east plus north)\n- **W3:** 4 Lintlings + 4 Frayed Knights + 3 Knotbrutes (east plus the Rift)\n- **Boss:** Gnarlgrim, with summons at phases 2 and 3\n\n**Bee raid:** 3 waves × (4 + 2 per player) Lintlings, then Pinhogs, then 1 Knotbrute per 2 players.\n\n### 7.10 Story and quests: \"Chapter One: A Stitch in Time\"\nEach quest lists the giver, steps (conditions from §6.15), the reward, and its cutscenes. Main quests are M1–M14; side quests S1–S3 are optional but count toward Cheer.\n\n**Prologue (intro crawl, 4 pages).**\n1. \"Long ago, Granny Gossamer stitched the Patchwork Realm from a thousand scraps of light.\"\n2. \"Its people had the Knack: whatever they dreamed, their hands could make.\"\n3. \"Then came Frayvern, the Unraveller. He pulled the Golden Thread from the heart of the world, and swallowed every last bit of Knack.\"\n4. \"Now the realm frays at its edges... and nobody remembers how to make a bed.\"\n\n**M1 \"Come Undone\"** (Granny; Lint Hollow). The opening cutscene is darkness, then Granny's golden box: \"Wakey wakey, dearie!\"\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Look around (tutorial prompts for move, camera turn and jump) | `{ at: 'hollowLedge' }` |\n| 2 | Break 3 Corduroy Earth | `{ have: { earth: 3 } }` |\n| 3 | Defeat the Lintling (\"A Lintling bounces into view!\") | `{ killed: { lintling: 1 } }` |\n| 4 | Craft a Wick Torch from the Bag (Notion on picking up Lint) | `{ crafted: 'torch' }` |\n| 5 | Light the dark tunnel (place the torch at the marked spot; the darkness lifts) | `{ placed: 'torch', at: 'tunnelMark' }` |\n| 6 | Climb out of the Hollow | `{ at: 'hollowExit' }` |\n\nReward: the Banner of Mending (key). Cutscene: the frayed world revealed, a camera pan over the Glen to the ruins. Granny: \"Plant this where Thimbleton used to be, dearie. Folks will come. They always come for a light.\"\n\n**M2 \"Plant the Banner\"** (Granny).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Reach the ruins of Thimbleton | `{ at: 'bannerSpot', radius: 3 }` |\n| 2 | Plant the Banner (use it) | `{ flag: 'bannerPlanted' }` |\n\nPlanting cutscene: the banner rises, a gold light ring spreads, the border stitch runs around, and \"Thimbleton has been founded!\" appears. Wren walks in from the road. Granny teaches the Mending Bench (a Pocket recipe) and Lattice Door notions.\n\n**M3 \"Wren's Bed\"** (Wren).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Gather 4 Straw from tufts | `{ have: { straw: 4 } }` |\n| 2 | Gather 1 Cotton Puff | `{ have: { cotton: 1 } }` |\n| 3 | Make and place a Mending Bench | `{ placed: 'bench' }` |\n| 4 | Craft a Straw Bed and a Lattice Door | `{ crafted: ['strawBed', 'latticeDoor'] }` |\n| 5 | Build a Bedroom: walls 2 blocks high, a door, the bed and a light inside | `{ room: 'bedroom' }` |\n\nReward: Cheer +10 and the Storage Chest notion. Wren: \"It's... a BED. I'm going to sleep in it for a hundred years!\" Her bedtime that night is her first heart bubble.\n\n**M4 \"A Place to Make Things\"** (Wren).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Craft a Storage Chest | `{ crafted: 'chest' }` |\n| 2 | Build a Workshop (bench + chest in a room) | `{ room: 'workshop' }` |\n\nReward: Cheer +10. This is likely Lv2, and Mortimer arrives at dawn (\"Hmph. Another dreamer.\").\n\n**M5 \"Club Med\"** (Mortimer).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Gather 3 Pebbles in the Crags (marker on the nearest gravel) | `{ have: { pebble: 3 } }` |\n| 2 | Craft a Cobble Club | `{ crafted: 'cobbleClub' }` |\n| 3 | Show it to Mortimer | `{ talk: 'mortimer' }` |\n\nReward: Spin Stitch technique (cutscene: Mortimer demonstrates on a straw dummy), Heartpatch #1, Cheer +10.\n\n**M6 \"Guard Duty\"** (Mortimer). Step: build a Guard Post (a Weapon Rack, from the notion at the quest start, plus 2 lights) → `{ room: 'guardPost' }`. Reward: Cheer +15. From now on Mortimer patrols at night.\n\n**M7 \"Supper Time\"** (Wren and Mortimer, a joint talk). Step: build a Mess Hall (table + 2 stools) → `{ room: 'messHall' }`. Reward: Cheer +10. This is likely Lv3: Marigold arrives (\"Is that a TABLE? I could weep!\").\n\n**M8 \"Hearth and Home\"** (Marigold).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Mine 4 Tweed Stone and 1 Charcloth (needs the Cobble Club; marker on the nearest coal) | `{ have: { stone: 4, coal: 1 } }` |\n| 2 | Craft a Hearth Pot | `{ crafted: 'hearthPot' }` |\n| 3 | Build a Kitchen (Hearth Pot + chest) | `{ room: 'kitchen' }` |\n| 4 | Bring Marigold 2 Puffballs from Tweedwood | `{ have: { puffball: 2 }, talk: 'marigold' }` |\n\nReward: Glen Stew notion, Heartpatch #2, Cheer +15. Marigold starts cooking.\n\n**M9 \"Copper Bottomed\"** (Mortimer, then Marigold).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Craft a Thimble Forge | `{ crafted: 'forge' }` |\n| 2 | Build a Smithy (Forge + chest) | `{ room: 'smithy' }` |\n| 3 | Smelt 2 Copper Ingots | `{ crafted: { copperIngot: 2 } }` |\n| 4 | Forge a Copper Bodkin | `{ crafted: 'copperBodkin' }` |\n\nReward: Cheer +20. This is likely Lv4: the Professor arrives with the Hall Pattern (\"Fascinating! A functioning door!\").\n\n**M10 \"The Quilters' Hall\"** (Professor).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Place the Hall Pattern inside the town (a suggested site is outlined NE of the banner, 11×9) | `{ flag: 'hallPlaced' }` |\n| 2 | Designate a Town Chest so residents can help | `{ flag: 'townChest' }` |\n| 3 | Complete the Pattern | `{ pattern: 'hall' }` |\n\nThe Pattern (outer 11×9, interior 9×7 = 63 cells) has 129 cells:\n- level 1: 35 Cobble (the perimeter minus the door)\n- level 2: 35 Planks\n- level 3: 36 Planks (a lintel over the door)\n- level 4: 18 Felt crenellations, 6 per colour, on every other perimeter cell\n- 1 Plank Door\n- 4 Moth Lanterns in the interior corners\n\n Reward: Cheer +100, Heartpatch #3, and the Bobbin Ballista notion. Revelation cutscene in the Hall: the Professor reads the old Pattern margins. \"The Golden Thread fragment lies atop the Knotted Spire, past the Knot Wall. Only a Seam Ripper can cut a Black Knot. And the only Golden Needle left is fastened to Sir Buttonsworth's chest.\"\n\n**M11 \"Needle in a Haystack\"** (Professor).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Go to the Button Quarry | `{ at: 'quarryFloor' }` |\n| 2 | Defeat Sir Buttonsworth (intro cutscene) | `{ boss: 'buttonGolem' }` |\n| 3 | Forge the Seam Ripper (needs Steel Thread: the Golem drops 3, Frayed Knights more) | `{ crafted: 'seamRipper' }` |\n\nReward: Cheer +20.\n\n**M12 \"Rip It Up\"** (Professor).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Cut through the Knot Gate (rip cutscene: the wall unpicks itself in a wave) | `{ flag: 'gateCut' }` |\n| 2 | Climb the Knotted Spire | `{ at: 'spireTop' }` |\n| 3 | Take the Golden Thread fragment | `{ have: { goldenThread: 1 } }` |\n\nCutscene: the thread glows, Frayvern's silhouette spreads across the sky (\"Mend all the patches you like...\"), and Gnarlgrim's roar echoes from the Rift. Granny: \"Hurry home, dearie, they're going after Thimbleton!\" Autosave.\n\n**M13 \"Hold the Line\"** (Mortimer).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Return to Thimbleton (portal) | `{ at: 'bannerSpot', radius: 12 }` |\n| 2 | Talk to Mortimer, \"Ready?\" (Yes starts the siege prep; \"Not yet\" lets you prepare freely) | `{ flag: 'siegeStarted' }` |\n| 3 | Survive 3 waves | `{ siegeDone: true }` |\n\nMortimer suggests building at least 2 Ballistas and some Pin Traps (hint only).\n\n**M14 \"Gnarlgrim the Knotted\"**. Step: defeat Gnarlgrim → `{ boss: 'gnarlgrim' }`.\n\nFinale cutscene:\n1. Gnarlgrim unravels and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner.\n2. The Banner flares, and the Rift and the frayed patch east of town re-stitch: a wave of stitches turns void into meadow.\n3. Town Lv5.\n4. The party: residents dance and cheer, confetti scraps fly, fireworks particles burst, and Marigold serves Hearty Pies.\n5. Granny: \"You did it, my little stitch. One patch mended... and a great many to go.\"\n6. Results, then credits, then free play.\n\n**S1 \"Lintwick's Lament\"** (found at the Lint Camp, from Lv2).\n\n| # | Step | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Break the Knot Cage (tier 2) | `{ flag: 'lintwickFreed' }` |\n| 2 | Lintwick follows you home (he walks or warps along) | `{ at: 'bannerSpot' }` |\n| 3 | Build him a Bedroom with at least one Felt block in its walls | `{ room: 'bedroom', felt: true }` |\n\nReward: Cheer +20 and daily Lint gifts.\n\n**S2 \"Bluebell Blues\"** (Wren, from Lv3). Steps: craft 4 Blue Felt → `{ crafted: { feltBlue: 4 } }`; place 8 Blue Felt blocks inside the border → `{ placedInTown: { feltBlue: 8 } }`. Reward: Cheer +15. Wren: \"It's like the sky came down to visit!\"\n\n**S3 \"Buttons of Old\"** (Professor, from Lv4). Step: find 3 Ancient Buttons (Coast shipwreck, Crags ledge, Tweedwood hollow tree; the map marks their regions with \"?\") → `{ have: { ancientButton: 3 } }`. Reward: Golden Thimble (Gilded Felt notion) and Cheer +30.\n\n**Talk variety.** Each resident has at least 6 idle lines that vary by time of day, mood, town level and quest state, plus reactions to the player's actions:\n- seeing a new room type: \"A KITCHEN!\"\n- Belly low: \"You look peckish, Builder.\"\n- the night: \"Lock the doors!\"\n\n### 7.11 Music (`DQ.SONGS`; original compositions, engine step format)\nThe leitmotif, **\"The Golden Thread\"**, is the seed every theme quotes. Melody in B♭ major, eighth notes (`steps: 2`):\n```\nF4 Bb4 C5 D5 | Eb5 - D5 C5 | Bb4 - G4 C5 | A4 - - - | F4 Bb4 C5 D5 | F5 - Eb5 D5 | C5 Bb4 A4 C5 | Bb4 - - -\nchords:  Bb | Eb | Gm | F | Bb | Bb7/D | Eb F | Bb\n```\n\n| Song | Use | Key / tempo / metre | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"Overture of Mending\" | Title | B♭, 116 bpm, 4/4 | Fanfare intro (square brass), the leitmotif in full, triangle bass, march drums |\n| \"Granny's Lullaby\" | Intro crawl, Granny moments | B♭, 72 bpm, 3/4 | Leitmotif slowed, sine and triangle |\n| \"Lint Hollow\" | Cave and tutorial | D dorian, 88 bpm | Plucky pulse arpeggios, sparse |\n| \"Thimbleton Days\" | Town (day) | F, 96 bpm, 3/4 waltz | 4 layers: base, `strings` (Lv2), `bells` (Lv3), `drums` (Lv4) |\n| \"Moonlit Hem\" | Night (anywhere) | A minor, 72 bpm | Soft triangle melody, the leitmotif in minor |\n| \"Gingham Glen\" | Glen and Coast | D, 112 bpm | Bright pulse melody, walking bass |\n| \"Corduroy Deep\" | Crags and Quarry | E minor, 92 bpm | Low saw drone, clinking noise percussion |\n| \"Tweedwood Rustle\" | Tweedwood | G, 100 bpm, 6/8 | Flute-like pulse12 |\n| \"The Fraying\" | Verge, Fraying, Spire | E phrygian, 66 bpm | Detuned pulses, dissonant intervals, slow noise swells |\n| \"Snip Snap Skirmish\" | Siege waves | C minor, 150 bpm | Driving bass, leitmotif fragments |\n| \"Sir Buttonsworth\" | Mini-boss | F minor, 140 bpm | Pompous march, comedic |\n| \"Gnarlgrim\" | Boss | G minor, 160 bpm | The leitmotif inverted. Layer `fury` from phase 3 |\n| \"Quilting Bee\" | Bee round | C, 128 bpm | Jaunty; layer `raid` comes in at the raid phase |\n| \"Patchwork Finale\" | Results and credits | B♭, 108 bpm | Medley: leitmotif, town waltz, triumphant ending |\n\nJingles (`loop: false`):\n\n| Jingle | Length | Character |\n|---|---|---|\n| Notion! | 1.2 s | harp gliss up |\n| Room Complete! | 2.5 s | fanfare |\n| Town Level Up! | 3.5 s | |\n| Quest Complete | 2 s | |\n| Item Get | 1 s | |\n| Resident Arrives | 2 s | |\n| Night Falls | 2 s | descending |\n| Morning | 1.5 s | rooster-ish pulse chirps |\n| Come Undone | 2.5 s | sad |\n| Wave Cleared | 1.5 s | |\n| Victory | 3 s | |\n| Zzz | 2 s | |\n\n### 7.12 Sound effects (`DQ.SFX`, engine voices; all from code)\n- **Blocks:**\n  - `hitSoft` (noise lowpass 900 Hz + triangle 180→120, 60 ms), `hitHard` (+ a 2 kHz click)\n  - `clink` (pulse 1800→2200, 50 ms, for under-tier)\n  - `rip` (noise bandpass 2.5 kHz → 700 Hz over 160 ms, then `pop`: sine 600→200, 40 ms)\n  - `stitch` (pulse12 880→1320, 40 ms + a soft click)\n  - `crumble` (Tangle and frayed breaks)\n- **Actions:**\n  - `swing` (noise whoosh), `spinCharge` (rising triangle), `spinRelease`, `jump`, `land`\n  - Footsteps by material: grass (soft noise), stone (click), wood (knock), sand (hiss), water (splash)\n- **Items and UI:**\n  - `pickup` (arpeggio 0-4-7, 90 ms), `notion`, `craft` (tok tok + a chime), `eat` (munch ×3)\n  - `zipper` (opening Satchel or Chest: a rising noise ratchet, 250 ms), `uiMove`, `uiConfirm`, `uiCancel`\n- **World:**\n  - `doorOpen` / `doorClose` (creaks with a pitch slide), `torchLight`, `portal` (swirl)\n  - `bubble` (two-note ding for Cheer), `levelUp`, `trap` (pins), `ballistaFire` (thwomp + whoosh), `ballistaReload` (click-clack)\n- **Combat:**\n  - `monsterHurt` (squeak per type: Lintling high, Knotbrute low), `monsterDie` (pop), `builderHurt`, `heartbeat`\n  - Boss: `slam` (boom + low rumble), `roar` (saw drive)\n  - Mothlet flaps, Pinhog roll rattle\n\n---\n## 8. Art direction and animation\n\nThe base is the engine's native look: low-res pixel buffer, shaded HD puppet rigs, stepped-alpha blends, canvas lighting, the 5×7 font and `E.font.title` logos. The new assets make it feel like a cosy patchwork-quilt reimagining of a block-building action RPG. Generic props may come from the engine library and the asset store (`node engine/tools/asset-find.mjs \"barrel\"`): barrels, crates, pots, signs, sacks, fences, rocks. Everything that defines the game's identity is made new: blocks, characters, monsters, furniture with a sewing twist, the banner, portals, UI, the logo.\n\n### 8.1 Block textures (16×16 texels per face, 1 texel ≈ 1 world unit)\nA texel's colour is one of the material's five tones from `E.tones(base)`: `deep`, `sh`, `base`, `lt`, `hi`. Some patterns add an accent colour, and seams use the thread colour. Common rules:\n- **Seam:** the outer ring (u or v = 0 or 15) is `deep`. A **running stitch** sits at ring 2 (u or v = 2 or 13): along positions 3–12, texels where `(along % 4) < 2` take the thread colour (default cream `#f1e6c8`; dark blocks use `#c8b890`). That gives each block its stitched-patch look.\n- **Faces:** top faces use the full tone set. Side faces shift one tone darker for faceA and two for faceB (§6.1.3). The pattern moves the tone by −1..+2 steps, as engine materials do.\n- **Variety:** 4 variants per material, made by offsetting each pattern's hash seed.\n\n| Pattern | Rule (u, v in 0..15) | Blocks (base colour) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `gingham` | Checks of 4×4: `((u>>2)+(v>>2))&1` → `base`/`lt`; where a light row crosses a light column → `hi` | grass top `#6cb84a` |\n| `fringe` | Earth side with the top 3 rows green felt and ragged yarn tufts (rows 3–4 at hashed u) | grass side |\n| `cord` | Sides: ribs, `u%3` → `sh`/`base`/`lt`. Tops: crosshatch | earth `#8a5a3a` |\n| `calico` | Base plus florets: hashed centres ~5 apart, centre texel accent `#e07a3a`, 4 petals `lt` | sand `#e8d08a` |\n| `bumps` | Discs of radius 1.5 on a jittered grid, lit top-left | gravel `#9a96a0` |\n| `tweed` | Herringbone: diagonal bands 2 wide that flip direction every 4 rows; speckles | stone `#8c8c9a` |\n| `sequins` | Tweed plus 3–4 discs (r 1.5) in `#d07a3a` with a `hi` glint. At draw time one sequin flashes white every ~2 s (overlay) | copper ore |\n| `lumps` | Tweed plus 3 black felt blobs `#2a2630` | coal |\n| `plaid` | Bark `#7a5032`, vertical stripes at u 4–5 and 11 in `#b0403a`, horizontal at v 7–8 in `#3a6a3a`; crossings darker | log side |\n| `rings` | Concentric rings every 2.5 texels, `sh`/`base`, a stitched outer ring, a centre dot | log top `#c89a62` |","numLines":260,"startLine":1118,"totalLines":1613}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PHchnXSbNjJQysuy8FZB6J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
