{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3aMKn142z97aNHmyFo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012LK4LbYkSDhUZtKR43NUM2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":1378,"limit":280},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9338,"cache_read_input_tokens":480860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9338},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"ab409b4f-8de2-4cfd-9a02-3a1ebe9bdbe9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:31.145Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3aM68Uo5L8erqhRPTp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012LK4LbYkSDhUZtKR43NUM2":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":1378,"limit":280}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012LK4LbYkSDhUZtKR43NUM2","type":"tool_result","content":"1378\t| `bobbles` | Pompoms of radius 2 on an offset grid, `lt` top-left and `sh` bottom-right, `deep` gaps; no seam | leaves `#4a9a4a` |\n1379\t| `torn` | A diagonal weave with gaps (`deep`), 2–3 loose `hi` threads crossing, broken stitches | frayed `#5a3a5a` |\n1380\t| `loops` | Overlapping yarn loops (ellipse outlines) in `sh`/`lt`; no seam | knot `#2a1a3a` |\n1381\t| `satin` | Blue with diagonal sheen bands that move by frame (4 frames) | water `#4a8ad0` |\n1382\t| `grid` | Navy with a large stitch grid every 8 texels | backing `#1a1840` |\n1383\t| `quiltstone` | Voronoi (5 seeds), `sh` borders, `lt` top-left rims | cobble `#9a9aa8` |\n1384\t| `boards` | Boards 4 texels tall, `sh` joints, staggered butt ends, stitched board lines | planks `#c8955a` |\n1385\t| `straw` | Horizontal straw courses `lt`/`base`/`sh` with a ragged lower edge | thatch `#e0b850` |\n1386\t| `felt` | Speckles 6% plus a diamond stitch `abs(u−7.5)+abs(v−7.5) ≈ 6` in thread colour | felts `#d04a4a`, `#4a6ad0`, `#e8c040` |\n1387\t| `star` | A stitched 5-point star; emissive (drawn again after lighting, as an `emissive` queue item) | glow `#fff0b0` |\n1388\t| `gild` | Gold with sparse `hi` sparkles | gildedFelt `#e8b830` |\n1389\t\n1390\tCheck every material with an atlas sheet written to `check-output/atlas.png` (§11.5). Each must read clearly at zoom 1 and 0.75 and be distinct from its neighbours: grass vs leaves, stone vs cobble, sand vs thatch.\n1391\t\n1392\t### 8.2 World dressing\n1393\t- **Void:** deep navy with lint motes, frayed fringe on edge columns, and a faint stitched grid in the far background.\n1394\t- **Thimbleton ruins:** the burned foundation outlines in a darker cobble.\n1395\t- **Props:** from the core library, recoloured to the palette: barrels, sacks, crates, a well, fences, signs. Place 3–8 per screen in town and at POIs.\n1396\t- **Plants:** they sway (a 0.5 Hz skew of 1 px).\n1397\t- **Lighting:** torches flicker (radius ±4 every 0.1 s) from the engine's flames. Dawn and dusk tint the scene warm; night is cool blue with warm pools of light.\n1398\t- **Weather:** ash in the Fraying, rain on some days in the Glen.\n1399\t\n1400\t### 8.3 Characters and monsters\n1401\tSee §7.8–7.9 for options. Style rules:\n1402\t- Chibi proportions, big eyes, distinct silhouettes, 4–6 colours each, the engine's outline.\n1403\t- Different body language per resident:\n1404\t\n1405\t  | Resident | Body language |\n1406\t  |---|---|\n1407\t  | Wren | bouncy, `run` faster |\n1408\t  | Mortimer | `stance:'ready'`, slow |\n1409\t  | Marigold | `hips` idle |\n1410\t  | Professor | `lean` forward, hands behind back |\n1411\t  | Lintwick | hop |\n1412\t\n1413\t- Monsters use `Blob` variety (fuzz, button eyes, pins, wings) and Humanoid builds (mannequin, yarn brute, button golem).\n1414\t- **Custom draw-over details**, drawn in the actor callback after `rig.draw` at joint positions from `rig.worldOffset`: button eyes, a felt fuzz edge (a dithered 1-px ring), Pinhog pins (radial lines with coloured heads), the Heart Knot glow, Mortimer's beard, the Professor's glasses. Keep each under 30 lines of code.\n1415\t\n1416\t### 8.4 UI look\n1417\t- Felt panels (dark indigo gradient) with cream running-stitch borders. Selected items get a gold stitch and a gentle 1-px bob.\n1418\t- Glyph icons are in §6.4.\n1419\t- Popups use `E.font.title` with patchwork gradient colours.\n1420\t- The **logo** is \"DRAGON QUILT\" at scale 4, each letter in a different fabric colour (gingham green, berry red, denim blue, calico yellow, plum, tan) with a stitched outline, and \"BUILDERS\" at scale 2 in gold thread. The emblem is a needle-and-thread drawn as a little dragon.\n1421\t- 10-foot check: at 1920×1080 every glyph and body text is at least 28 px tall. Verify on screenshots.\n1422\t\n1423\t### 8.5 Effects\n1424\t- **Block break:** `particles.bits(x,y,z, 10, tonesOfBlock)` plus `dust`, and a pop scale of the block's last frame.\n1425\t- **Place:** `glints` and the squash tween.\n1426\t- **Cheer bubble:** a pink heart sprite (8×8) bobbing, then flying in an arc to the HUD.\n1427\t- **Level up:** confetti in every felt colour, a light ring and a banner stripe stitch.\n1428\t- **KO and boss defeat:** an *unravel* effect. 40–80 thread particles: custom `particles.add({ kind:'spark' })` with long life, or our own line particles that peel off the rig's bounding area upward with sway.\n1429\t- **Notion bubble:** a thought cloud plus the item icon.\n1430\t- **Ballista:** a spool bolt with a thread trail, and a yarn burst on hit.\n1431\t- **Tangle:** a lobbed yarn ball with a shadow telegraph (`r.groundDisc` pulsing red).\n1432\t- **Finale:** fireworks (`particles.explosion` in felt colours, no shake) and the re-stitch wave (a sweep along the rift's edge, ring by ring, with a \"stitch\" sfx per ring).\n1433\t- Every hit gets hit-stop, shake, sparks and sound (engine `hitFx`). Flashes follow the comfort settings.\n1434\t\n1435\t### 8.6 Animation (engine-native rigs plus new moves)\n1436\tThe engine's procedural `Humanoid`/`Blob` rigs are the base: `E.MOVES`, poses, `E.Combo`, `rig.kick`, tweens and scripts. Add new moves as `E.MOVES` specs (`{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover, hand, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`) and new poses through state combinations.\n1437\t\n1438\t| Character | Animation | How |\n1439\t|---|---|---|\n1440\t| Builder | Combat combo | `E.Combo(['slash','backslash'])` |\n1441\t| Builder | Break block at feet or below | `overhead` (a hammer-like chop) |\n1442\t| Builder | Break at chest or head | `slash` |\n1443\t| Builder | Spin Stitch | charge (`crouch` plus a glow) → `spin` with `rig.drawSmear` |\n1444\t| Builder | **place** (new) | `{ hand:'both', a0:-.2, a1:.15, z0:20, z1:8, reach:9, wind:.05, active:.05, recover:.12, lunge:1.5 }` plus the block pop |\n1445\t| Builder | **eat** (new) | 3 quick `{ hand:'L', z0:14, z1:24, reach:3, wind:.08, active:.1, recover:.1 }` with `expr:'smile'` |\n1446\t| Builder | **craft** | a `bash` loop at the station, 0.5 s |\n1447\t| Builder | **plant banner** | `plunge` two-handed with a 0.3 s hold |\n1448\t| Builder | **notion** | `pose:'kneel'` blend 0.4 s → `pose:'cheer'` 0.6 s, plus a thought bubble |\n1449\t| Builder | Sleep | `down: 1` on the bed (z = bed top), Zzz particles |\n1450\t| Builder | Sit (stools, ballista) | `pose:'crouch'` with a z offset |\n1451\t| Builder | Hurt, die, unravel | `hurt`, `pose:'die'` → unravel |\n1452\t| Builder | Wave and cheer (rooms, levels) | `wave`, `cheer` with `rig.kick(.3)` |\n1453\t| Residents | Walking styles | per §8.3 |\n1454\t| Residents | Talk gesture | alternate `wave`/`hips` with `expr:'smile'` |\n1455\t| Residents | Jobs | **stir** (new: a small circular hand loop `{hand:'R', a0:-.4, a1:.4, z0:14, z1:14, reach:8}` repeated), **hammer** (`bash` loop), **read** (`kneel` with hands forward), slingshot (`throw`), Mortimer `overhead`, Marigold pie `throw` |\n1456\t| Residents | Daily life | `cheer` on rooms and level-ups, `pose:'down'` asleep, `crouch` cowering when hurt |\n1457\t| Lintwick | Hop, dance | Blob hop and squash (`kick`), a dance loop (squash oscillation + hop + a facing spin) |\n1458\t| Lintlings | Hop chase, lunge | squash-hop chase; lunge = squash wind then stretch |\n1459\t| Mothlets | Flight | `flap` 1 → swoop |\n1460\t| Pinhogs | Roll | curl (`squash .4`, pins shrink inward) → roll (rotating pin angles) → dizzy (stars over the head) |\n1461\t| Frayed Knight | Fighting | `stance:'ready'`, `thrust`, `spin` |\n1462\t| Knotbrute | Fighting | `haymaker`, `sweep`, a shoulder charge (`lean` forward) |\n1463\t| Sir Buttonsworth | Boss moves | `haymaker` (slam), `throw` (volley), a charge with `lean`, a `down` stagger |\n1464\t| Gnarlgrim | Boss moves | `haymaker` slam, `throw` toss, charge, `down:.6` (Tangled), `expr:'shout'` roar, unravel death |\n1465\t| Objects | Motion | door swing (tweened rotation of the door leaf), banner flutter (a sine wave across the cloth, 3 px), portal swirl (rotating thread arcs), ballista crank and bolt recoil, plant sway, bed blanket |\n1466\t| Camera | Cutscenes | eased pans and zooms (tweens), a 90° turn crossfade |\n1467\t\n1468\tCheck every attack and the new moves with `filmstrip.mjs` (wind-up, strike, settle; no backward sweeps). Enemies' wind-ups are longer than the hero's (.3–.6 s).\n1469\t\n1470\t---\n1471\t\n1472\t## 9. Build order and milestones\n1473\tEach milestone ends with: `node tests/run.mjs` green, `node tools/build.mjs` producing a playable HTML, and a short note in `DEVLOG.md` in the dev folder. Build the **core loop end to end early** (MS1–MS6 make Act 1 playable), then widen. Milestones are numbered MS0–MS12; quests keep their own IDs, M1–M14 and S1–S3.\n1474\t\n1475\t| # | Milestone | Deliverables | Acceptance |\n1476\t|---|---|---|---|\n1477\t| **MS0** | Setup | Folder layout, engine copy, `vendor/aihub`, `build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the loader (vm context with `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` stand-ins, as `engine/kits/test.mjs` does), an empty `DQ` booting to a placeholder title | Build works from `file://`; the test runner prints `N passed, 0 failed`; `check.mjs` reports no errors |\n1478\t| **MS1** | **Voxel core** (riskiest; §10) | `VoxelWorld`, `VoxelRenderer` (atlas, runs, AO, cutaway, x-ray, water, void), `VoxelBody`, picking, break/place in a dev \"sandbox\" scene (a 32×32 diorama stamp), 4 rotations, zoom steps, depth hooks | Unit tests: collision, ground, ceiling, stairs, raycast, pick, diff, hash. Diorama screenshots in 4 rotations × 2 zooms show no sorting errors. Sorting filmstrip; manual play feels solid. Fallbacks in §10 decided by the end of MS1 |\n1479\t| **MS2** | Builder and controls | Movement, auto-hop, sprint, jump, combo, Spin Stitch, break tiers, place, cursor modes (auto, mouse, Builder's Eye), hotbar, glyph icons and prompts by device, camera controls | Input-driven tests per action (taps and holds); prompt label tests for keyboard, mouse, PlayStation and Xbox |\n1480\t| **MS3** | Items, crafting, objects | Data tables §7.2–7.5, bag and hotbar, drops and pickups, chests, Pocket and Bench crafting UI, notions, doors, lights, beds, plants and regrowth, `E.SHAPES` for all objects | Craft-chain tests; UI navigation tests (MENU actions, mouse hover/click via `input.feed`); object sheets via `asset-sheet.mjs` |\n1481\t| **MS4** | World | `generateWorld` with every region, stamps and POI from §7.1, portals, day/night and lighting, weather | Determinism hash test; every POI reachable by nav from the banner (portals allowed); region screenshots |\n1482\t| **MS5** | Rooms and town | Room detection and classes, Banner planting, border, Cheer, levels, bubbles, Patterns (ghosts, progress, placement UI) | Room test matrix (§11.2); level-up and border-growth tests; Pattern completion test |\n1483\t| **MS6** | Residents and story (Act 1–2) | Nav/A\\*, resident schedule, needs, jobs and helpers; `E.Story` dialog with portraits; quest director; quests M1–M7 and S1; cutscenes with skip; Journal; objective marker | Playthrough test up to Lv3; residents sleep and eat; quests turn in |\n1484\t| **MS7** | Combat, monsters, bosses (Act 3–4) | All monsters, spawning, combat feel, KO and Lost Bundle, traps, ballistas, Sir Buttonsworth, siege director, Gnarlgrim; quests M8–M14, S2 and S3; the finale | Damage-formula tests, siege and boss state tests, filmstrips of every attack; playthrough to Chapter Clear |\n1485\t| **MS8** | Audio | Every song and jingle, sfx, Animalese synth with `onLetter`, Voices bus and setting, the music director with layers | Headless: every song id resolves, no audio errors. Browser: a listening pass (record notes), plus a `dev/voices.html` test page cycling through speakers |\n1486\t| **MS9** | UI polish | Title diorama and logo, New Game, intro, HUD final, Satchel (Bag, Map, Journal), Banner screen, results, credits, About, settings additions, touch-only notice | Screenshot review at 1920×1080 (legibility, 10 ft); keyboard-only, mouse-only and pad-only walkthroughs |\n1487\t| **MS10** | Save, dev mode, attract | `game.saves` integration, autosave, Continue; Dev Tools (all tabs, sliders with reset, stamp export, beats); Attract (9 vignettes, any input exits) | Save round-trip test (hash and state equal); slider live-effect and reset tests; attract runs 3 loops headless with no errors, and a keypress exits within 1 step |\n1488\t| **MS11** | Multiplayer | `DQ.Net` (codec, host, client, prediction), the Bee world and rules, `hubcard`, server mode, loopback, solo Bee from the title | Net loopback tests (§11.3); `--browser` harness passes all 4 scenarios |\n1489\t| **MS12** | Finish | Balance pass with dev sliders; full playthrough under 3 min headless; final screenshots; `exit-interview.json`; About filled from it; final build | §12 checklist all ticked |\n1490\t\n1491\tParallel work (for teams): after MS1's API is frozen (end of MS1), MS3 (data and crafting), MS4 (worldgen) and MS8 (audio) can proceed alongside MS2. MS11 can start with the loopback once the Builder and VoxelWorld APIs exist.\n1492\t\n1493\t---\n1494\t\n1495\t## 10. Risks and de-risking\n1496\t\n1497\t| Risk | Why | De-risk (do early) | Fallback |\n1498\t|---|---|---|---|\n1499\t| **Voxel rendering in a 2D engine** (sorting, overhangs, cutaway) | The engine sorts single points; overhangs can draw actors over roofs | MS1 first, against the diorama with every hard case (§11.2): lift and sink in `_liftOrder`, runs as occluders, x-ray, cutaway. Use filmstrips in 4 rotations | (a) Draw each block as its own queue item instead of runs; (b) if overhang sorting still glitches, always cut away blocks above `heroLevel+2` within the radius, and let NPCs under roofs be hidden by the roof (sink rule only); (c) as a last resort, limit placement so blocks need support below or a neighbour (no floating roofs). Decide by the end of MS1 and record it in DEVLOG |\n1500\t| **Render cost / hitches** | Thousands of blits; atlas rebuild on zoom | Face-sprite atlas (no per-run baking), zoom steps, visible-column culling. Perf readout in Debug | Fewer variants, top-only far columns, lower `H` |\n1501\t| **Body collision in voxels** (stuck, jitter, ceilings) | A new system with heights | Unit tests for every edge case: corners, 1-high step, 2-high gap, stairs, water, void; the `escape()` routine; no placement inside bodies | Make bodies smaller (r 4); disable auto-hop |\n1502\t| **Room detection** correctness | Many shapes; false positives and negatives frustrate players | A test matrix with 20+ layouts, a leak-hint HUD and a dev overlay | Relax the rule (count 1-high door-adjacent gaps as leaks only) |\n1503\t| **NPC navigation** in an editable world | Changing graph; residents stuck | Incremental invalidation, A\\* caps, the stuck rule (off-screen teleport), a dev path overlay | Residents hop over 1-block obstacles and teleport within the border when stuck for more than 8 s even on screen (a poof effect) |\n1504\t| **Shared-world netcode** | Latency, loss, message caps, host or server modes | Keep the Bee world small; voxel edits are reliable and idempotent; snapshots are unreliable with timestamps; a loopback suite with simulated latency, jitter and loss; run the harness early (a skeleton round in MS6) | Reduce the Bee round to the build phase plus a single raid wave; lower snapshot rates to 6 Hz |\n1505\t| **Scope** (17 quests, 8 monsters, 2 bosses) | A large content load | Data-driven tables; finish one vertical path (Act 1) before widening; the scripted playthrough guards regressions | Cut the side quests' extra steps (keep S1–S3 short); keep S3 even if minimal |\n1506\t| **Animalese quality / annoyance** | Synth voices can grate | Prototype the test page on the first day of MS8; soft envelopes, low volume (.18), a Voices volume setting, text speed | A one-blip-per-two-letters mode |\n1507\t| **10-foot legibility** | Pixel font at 240p | Text at scale 1 or more; a 1080p screenshot review in MS9 | Use `res: 'snes'` (taller pixels) for menus only, through the scene `res` |\n1508\t| **Headless testability of UI** | Menus are visual | UI logic as state machines; `game.debug` exposes the UI state; tests drive inputs | — |\n1509\t| **Determinism** | Attract, tests, replays | Seeded streams only; `game.stateHash` for replays | — |\n1510\t\n1511\t---\n1512\t\n1513\t## 11. Testing plan\n1514\t\n1515\tRules (from TASK.md):\n1516\t- One command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints **only failures and a one-line count**. Rerun it only after changing the code it covers; use `--only` with suite names.\n1517\t- Use the engine's `game.advance(seconds)` and `game.debug` for scripted play. Use screenshots only for what a script cannot check.\n1518\t- Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n1519\t\n1520\t### 11.1 Harness\n1521\t- `tests/lib/load.mjs` creates a vm context with stand-ins (`window = ctx`, `addEventListener(){}`, `location: {hash, search:''}`, `matchMedia: () => ({matches:false})`). It runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then each `src/*.js` in build order, and returns `{ E, game, DQ }`. Each suite gets a fresh context.\n1522\t- Helpers:\n1523\t  - `press(action, s)` (tap, then advance)\n1524\t  - `hold(action, s)`\n1525\t  - `run(s)` (advance)\n1526\t  - `snap()` (`game.debug.snapshot()`)\n1527\t  - `expect(cond, msg, detail)`\n1528\t  - `atBeat(id)` (dev beat)\n1529\t- `tests/run.mjs` imports every `*.test.mjs` it finds, collects `{name, ok, detail}`, prints failures only, and prints the final count. Exit 1 on any failure. `--only a,b` filters by file prefix. `--browser` adds `tests/browser/*`.\n1530\t\n1531\t### 11.2 Headless suites (what each checks)\n1532\t| Suite | Checks |\n1533\t|---|---|\n1534\t| `voxel.test` | get/set bounds; `topZ` upkeep; `standLevels`; `groundAt` on edges and stairs; `ceilingAt`; `collide` (corner, step, 2-high gap passes, 1-high gap blocks); water depth rules; void respawn; raycast and `pickScreen` in all 4 rotations and 2 views (pick a known block from its projected centre); `diff`/`applyDiff` round trip; hash stability |\n1535\t| `render-logic.test` | Run splitting; visible-column culling contains the camera's cell; `_liftOrder` lift and sink cases (a hero on a block sorts after it; a hero under a roof sorts before the roof run; a body under a bridge sorts before the bridge); cutaway trigger cases |\n1536\t| `builder.test` | Walk speed matches tuning; jump clears 1 block, not 2; auto-hop; Builder's Eye cursor moves and levels; break tiers (clink vs break), crack stages, drops; place validity (reach, occupied, inside a body); combo timing; Spin Stitch charge; KO → respawn and Lost Bundle content (50%) |\n1537\t| `input.test` | Prompt labels per device (keyboard, mouse, PlayStation, Xbox); the glyph setting switches; the Create+Options hub rule; wheel steps cycle the hotbar |\n1538\t| `items.test` | Stacks, overflow, hotbar refs, chest store-all, Town Chest designation |\n1539\t| `crafting.test` | Every recipe: inputs consumed, output added; station gating; notion triggers fire once; the quantity picker |\n1540\t| `objects.test` | Doors open for builders and residents and stay shut for monsters; beds sleep only at night and safely; trap damage; ballista auto and manned fire, reload, repair; portal discovery and travel; plant regrowth after a day |\n1541\t| `rooms.test` | Matrix: 2×1 snug; 3×3 bedroom; a 1-high wall leak; a corner gap leak; a missing door; a missing light; 65 cells too big; a roofed room; a door on a corner (invalid, since doors must be in straight walls); stairs inside; two rooms sharing a wall; a room outside the border (detected, no Cheer); a type change (bedroom → snug when the bed is removed); every room type in §7.6; the Hall Pattern recognised; awards counted once per slot and capped by maxAwards |\n1542\t| `town.test` | Planting creates the border; Cheer thresholds → levels; border growth; arrivals at dawn; bubbles spawn once per need per day and collect; Pattern placement validity and rotation; ghost counting; helper placement from the Town Chest; \"need\" balloon |\n1543\t| `nav.test` | Paths over steps and stairs and through doors (residents) but not doors (monsters); a breaker path through a wall; re-path after an edit; the stuck rule |\n1544\t| `npc.test` | Schedule transitions; sleep in an assigned bed; supper at the Mess Hall; Marigold cooks from the chest; Wren's and Lintwick's gifts; requests show \"!\" and \"?\" |\n1545\t| `monsters.test` | Spawn rules (not in the border, not near the builder, night tables); aggro, leash and despawn; each attack's wind-up precedes damage; the damage formula with def/tuning/difficulty; drop tables |\n1546\t| `siege.test` | Prep → W1–W3 → boss sequencing; monsters target the Banner and break walls; the fail and retry checkpoint; wave sizes scale with tuning |\n1547\t| `bosses.test` | Buttonsworth patterns and summon at 50%; Gnarlgrim def 25 → ~1 damage; 2 ballista hits in 8 s → Tangled; charge-hit → Tangled; Seam Ripper ×4 on the Heart Knot; phase transitions at 66% and 33%; the defeat cutscene's `apply()` state |\n1548\t| `time.test` | The day length tunable; ambient by hour; sleep skips to 06:00; Belly drain and starving |\n1549\t| `quests.test` | Each quest's steps complete from its conditions; rewards granted once; `applyBeat` for every beat yields a consistent snapshot (no errors; flags, residents, rooms present) |\n1550\t| `save.test` | Mid-game save → load in a fresh context: `world.hash`, bag, quests, town, residents, clock all equal; the autosave triggers |\n1551\t| `dev.test` | Every slider changes behaviour live (walk speed, monster HP, day length...); Reset restores the defaults; cheats toggle; warp lands on standable cells; spawn works; stamp export → import round trip |\n1552\t| `attract.test` | Start after 10.0 s idle on the title (not 9.9 s); 3 full loops (about 7 minutes simulated) with no errors and each vignette reaching its end condition; any input (key, mouse move, pad button) returns to the title within 1 step; the player's save is untouched |\n1553\t| `touch.test` | With `matchMedia` coarse-only stubs and no keys: the title shows the notice, no touch buttons, attract still runs |\n1554\t| `ui.test` | Satchel tabs, Bag actions, crafting navigation by MENU actions and by `input.feed` mouse hover and click; the name entry; settings additions persist |\n1555\t| `about.test` | The About pages contain every Source Information field and the three feedback lists from the embedded data |\n1556\t| **`playthrough.test`** | **Full scripted run, New Game → Chapter Clear → credits → free play.** `DQ.Autopilot` uses real systems: walk with nav, break and place through Builder actions, craft through Crafting, talk through Story choices, fight with combos. Cheats allowed: god mode, teleports to POIs (instead of long walks), extra materials for the Hall, time skips, and a boosted helper rate. **Every quest must complete through its own triggers.** It asserts at each beat: quest states, town level, residents present, room types formed, Notions known, Golden Needle and Seam Ripper obtained, gate cut, siege waves cleared, boss defeated, results scene, credits, back to play. Error count 0 throughout. Target under 3 minutes wall time (big `advance` chunks during travel, 1/120 steps during combat via `game.advance`) |\n1557\t| `bee.test` | Solo Bee from the title: the Pattern scales with players; the build and raid phases; scoring rules; win and lose |\n1558\t| `net.test` (loopback) | 2 and 4 game instances in separate vm contexts with a **fake AIHub** (connect, ready, card events, start, `time()`, send/on, leave, time-up, end, `rng`, server flag) over an in-process bus with seeded latency 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss on unreliable messages. Checks:<br>(1) `connect`/`ready` with no key press; the card answers Ready on Enter and More on Triangle.<br>(2) Bot builders place and break; after quiescence every copy's `world.hash()` is equal.<br>(3) Monsters move on clients from snapshots.<br>(4) Message rate ≤ 20/s per copy (bursts ≤ 40); every payload ≤ 16 KB; unreliable ≤ 1,200 bytes.<br>(5) A player leaving removes their builder.<br>(6) Time-up → the host `finish()` within grace, once, with valid standings (every id once).<br>(7) Server mode (a host with no player) runs the round and finishes.<br>(8) `end` stops input and sound.<br>(9) `AIHub.active` false → the normal title |\n1559\t\n1560\t### 11.3 Browser suites (`--browser`; Playwright, pinned in `engine/package.json`)\n1561\t- **`hub-check.mjs`**\n1562\t  - **Setup:** `tools/hub-serve.mjs` serves a temp copy folder holding the built HTML plus `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` on `127.0.0.1:<OS port>`. It confirms the game page title.\n1563\t  - **Runs** (open `harness.html?game=<file>&...`):\n1564\t    - `&players=2&auto=1`\n1565\t    - `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n1566\t    - the same as above with `&scenario=host-leave`\n1567\t    - `&players=2&scenario=server`\n1568\t  - **Pass:** wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. On failure, print the harness checklist's failing items.\n1569\t  - **Standalone:** open the game alone (outside a session) and require that it reaches the title.\n1570\t  - **Teardown:** kill only the server PID it started.\n1571\t- **`shots.mjs`** writes screenshots to `check-output/` at 1920×1080 (and 1280×720) for human review:\n1572\t  - title, New Game, intro\n1573\t  - Hollow dark/lit, Glen day, Thimbleton at Lv1/Lv3/Lv4 (dev beats), Crags, Quarry boss, Tweedwood, Coast, Fraying, Spire top\n1574\t  - night town, siege, Gnarlgrim Tangled\n1575\t  - Bag, Crafting, Map, Journal, Banner screen, Dev Tools, About\n1576\t  - Bee card, touch-only notice\n1577\t  - 4 camera rotations, three-quarter view\n1578\t  - the block atlas sheet\n1579\t- Also run `node engine/tools/check.mjs <html>#play` (fails on errors; acts on look notes) and `filmstrip.mjs` for every attack and new move.\n1580\t\n1581\t### 11.4 Manual passes (short, recorded in DEVLOG)\n1582\t- **Controller only** (DualSense, or the standard mapping): the whole of Act 1, menus, dev sliders.\n1583\t- **Keyboard only.** Mouse plus keyboard. The prompts switch instantly with the last input.\n1584\t- **Glyph setting:** Xbox.\n1585\t- **TV distance:** all text readable from 3 m on a 1080p screen, or approximate it by viewing a 1080p screenshot at 33% scale.\n1586\t- **Feel:** jump arc, swing hit-stop, break and place rhythm (one block per ~0.4 s feels snappy), camera turn.\n1587\t\n1588\t### 11.5 Asset checks\n1589\t- `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs src/03-data-objects.js#bench` (each object) shows every view and facing next to the hero. Fix the lint notes.\n1590\t- An atlas dump writes every block material and face to `check-output/atlas.png`.\n1591\t\n1592\t---\n1593\t\n1594\t## 12. Definition of done (check every line before handing off)\n1595\t- [ ] `./DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174740.html` is one file, works from `file://`, has no external requests, and its title shows **Dragon Quilt Builders**.\n1596\t- [ ] Everything in §6 and §7 is implemented; there are **no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features** (`grep -rn \"TODO\\|FIXME\\|placeholder\" src/` is empty).\n1597\t- [ ] Chapter One is playable start to finish (M1–M14), S1–S3 work, and free play continues after the credits.\n1598\t- [ ] All systems are present:\n1599\t  - voxel building with rotation and cutaway; tools and tiers; crafting and Notions; rooms; Banner, levels and Patterns with helpers\n1600\t  - residents with schedules, needs, jobs and requests; Cheer bubbles; day/night; Belly\n1601\t  - combat with 6 monster types plus 2 bosses; the siege; ballistas and traps; portals; Map and Journal; saves\n1602\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: cheats, warp, spawn, story beats, debug overlays, **live sliders with Reset to defaults**, stamp export.\n1603\t- [ ] Attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title or menus, loops, cheats freely, and any input exits.\n1604\t- [ ] AI Hub: tags, unmodified `session.js` first in `<head>`, shared-world Bee round, own card, ready without a key press, standings and finish, leave, time-up, end, server mode. **The harness passes all 4 scenarios.** Outside a session the game is unaffected.\n1605\t- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI. PlayStation glyphs by default with a Settings option for Xbox. Keyboard and mouse are native (WASD, Space, Shift, mouse targeting, wheel hotbar, Q/E camera, F talk, Tab bag). Prompts follow the last input device. Mouse hover moves the focus in every menu.\n1606\t- [ ] Touch-only devices: no touch controls, the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice, the settings button, and the attract mode runs.\n1607\t- [ ] Audio is all code: original music with the leitmotif, sfx, Animalese voices per character, and a Voices volume setting.\n1608\t- [ ] Tone is Dragon Quest-like throughout (punny, warm, earnest, silent hero). No names, characters, art, music, places or iconic lines from the source.\n1609\t- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` and `node tests/run.mjs --browser` pass (only failures are printed, then one count line).\n1610\t- [ ] `exit-interview.json` exists beside the HTML, parses as JSON, and has exactly the TASK.md shape with every value filled (\"unknown\" where unconfirmed; `plan`: \"PLAN.md\").\n1611\t- [ ] The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (from the same data as the exit interview), the engine changes and licences.\n1612\t- [ ] The final chat reply includes Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n1613\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d","uuid":"4c5b6426-e7e9-4e3b-ac2e-53e382f9e4d8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:31.282Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"| `bobbles` | Pompoms of radius 2 on an offset grid, `lt` top-left and `sh` bottom-right, `deep` gaps; no seam | leaves `#4a9a4a` |\n| `torn` | A diagonal weave with gaps (`deep`), 2–3 loose `hi` threads crossing, broken stitches | frayed `#5a3a5a` |\n| `loops` | Overlapping yarn loops (ellipse outlines) in `sh`/`lt`; no seam | knot `#2a1a3a` |\n| `satin` | Blue with diagonal sheen bands that move by frame (4 frames) | water `#4a8ad0` |\n| `grid` | Navy with a large stitch grid every 8 texels | backing `#1a1840` |\n| `quiltstone` | Voronoi (5 seeds), `sh` borders, `lt` top-left rims | cobble `#9a9aa8` |\n| `boards` | Boards 4 texels tall, `sh` joints, staggered butt ends, stitched board lines | planks `#c8955a` |\n| `straw` | Horizontal straw courses `lt`/`base`/`sh` with a ragged lower edge | thatch `#e0b850` |\n| `felt` | Speckles 6% plus a diamond stitch `abs(u−7.5)+abs(v−7.5) ≈ 6` in thread colour | felts `#d04a4a`, `#4a6ad0`, `#e8c040` |\n| `star` | A stitched 5-point star; emissive (drawn again after lighting, as an `emissive` queue item) | glow `#fff0b0` |\n| `gild` | Gold with sparse `hi` sparkles | gildedFelt `#e8b830` |\n\nCheck every material with an atlas sheet written to `check-output/atlas.png` (§11.5). Each must read clearly at zoom 1 and 0.75 and be distinct from its neighbours: grass vs leaves, stone vs cobble, sand vs thatch.\n\n### 8.2 World dressing\n- **Void:** deep navy with lint motes, frayed fringe on edge columns, and a faint stitched grid in the far background.\n- **Thimbleton ruins:** the burned foundation outlines in a darker cobble.\n- **Props:** from the core library, recoloured to the palette: barrels, sacks, crates, a well, fences, signs. Place 3–8 per screen in town and at POIs.\n- **Plants:** they sway (a 0.5 Hz skew of 1 px).\n- **Lighting:** torches flicker (radius ±4 every 0.1 s) from the engine's flames. Dawn and dusk tint the scene warm; night is cool blue with warm pools of light.\n- **Weather:** ash in the Fraying, rain on some days in the Glen.\n\n### 8.3 Characters and monsters\nSee §7.8–7.9 for options. Style rules:\n- Chibi proportions, big eyes, distinct silhouettes, 4–6 colours each, the engine's outline.\n- Different body language per resident:\n\n  | Resident | Body language |\n  |---|---|\n  | Wren | bouncy, `run` faster |\n  | Mortimer | `stance:'ready'`, slow |\n  | Marigold | `hips` idle |\n  | Professor | `lean` forward, hands behind back |\n  | Lintwick | hop |\n\n- Monsters use `Blob` variety (fuzz, button eyes, pins, wings) and Humanoid builds (mannequin, yarn brute, button golem).\n- **Custom draw-over details**, drawn in the actor callback after `rig.draw` at joint positions from `rig.worldOffset`: button eyes, a felt fuzz edge (a dithered 1-px ring), Pinhog pins (radial lines with coloured heads), the Heart Knot glow, Mortimer's beard, the Professor's glasses. Keep each under 30 lines of code.\n\n### 8.4 UI look\n- Felt panels (dark indigo gradient) with cream running-stitch borders. Selected items get a gold stitch and a gentle 1-px bob.\n- Glyph icons are in §6.4.\n- Popups use `E.font.title` with patchwork gradient colours.\n- The **logo** is \"DRAGON QUILT\" at scale 4, each letter in a different fabric colour (gingham green, berry red, denim blue, calico yellow, plum, tan) with a stitched outline, and \"BUILDERS\" at scale 2 in gold thread. The emblem is a needle-and-thread drawn as a little dragon.\n- 10-foot check: at 1920×1080 every glyph and body text is at least 28 px tall. Verify on screenshots.\n\n### 8.5 Effects\n- **Block break:** `particles.bits(x,y,z, 10, tonesOfBlock)` plus `dust`, and a pop scale of the block's last frame.\n- **Place:** `glints` and the squash tween.\n- **Cheer bubble:** a pink heart sprite (8×8) bobbing, then flying in an arc to the HUD.\n- **Level up:** confetti in every felt colour, a light ring and a banner stripe stitch.\n- **KO and boss defeat:** an *unravel* effect. 40–80 thread particles: custom `particles.add({ kind:'spark' })` with long life, or our own line particles that peel off the rig's bounding area upward with sway.\n- **Notion bubble:** a thought cloud plus the item icon.\n- **Ballista:** a spool bolt with a thread trail, and a yarn burst on hit.\n- **Tangle:** a lobbed yarn ball with a shadow telegraph (`r.groundDisc` pulsing red).\n- **Finale:** fireworks (`particles.explosion` in felt colours, no shake) and the re-stitch wave (a sweep along the rift's edge, ring by ring, with a \"stitch\" sfx per ring).\n- Every hit gets hit-stop, shake, sparks and sound (engine `hitFx`). Flashes follow the comfort settings.\n\n### 8.6 Animation (engine-native rigs plus new moves)\nThe engine's procedural `Humanoid`/`Blob` rigs are the base: `E.MOVES`, poses, `E.Combo`, `rig.kick`, tweens and scripts. Add new moves as `E.MOVES` specs (`{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover, hand, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`) and new poses through state combinations.\n\n| Character | Animation | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| Builder | Combat combo | `E.Combo(['slash','backslash'])` |\n| Builder | Break block at feet or below | `overhead` (a hammer-like chop) |\n| Builder | Break at chest or head | `slash` |\n| Builder | Spin Stitch | charge (`crouch` plus a glow) → `spin` with `rig.drawSmear` |\n| Builder | **place** (new) | `{ hand:'both', a0:-.2, a1:.15, z0:20, z1:8, reach:9, wind:.05, active:.05, recover:.12, lunge:1.5 }` plus the block pop |\n| Builder | **eat** (new) | 3 quick `{ hand:'L', z0:14, z1:24, reach:3, wind:.08, active:.1, recover:.1 }` with `expr:'smile'` |\n| Builder | **craft** | a `bash` loop at the station, 0.5 s |\n| Builder | **plant banner** | `plunge` two-handed with a 0.3 s hold |\n| Builder | **notion** | `pose:'kneel'` blend 0.4 s → `pose:'cheer'` 0.6 s, plus a thought bubble |\n| Builder | Sleep | `down: 1` on the bed (z = bed top), Zzz particles |\n| Builder | Sit (stools, ballista) | `pose:'crouch'` with a z offset |\n| Builder | Hurt, die, unravel | `hurt`, `pose:'die'` → unravel |\n| Builder | Wave and cheer (rooms, levels) | `wave`, `cheer` with `rig.kick(.3)` |\n| Residents | Walking styles | per §8.3 |\n| Residents | Talk gesture | alternate `wave`/`hips` with `expr:'smile'` |\n| Residents | Jobs | **stir** (new: a small circular hand loop `{hand:'R', a0:-.4, a1:.4, z0:14, z1:14, reach:8}` repeated), **hammer** (`bash` loop), **read** (`kneel` with hands forward), slingshot (`throw`), Mortimer `overhead`, Marigold pie `throw` |\n| Residents | Daily life | `cheer` on rooms and level-ups, `pose:'down'` asleep, `crouch` cowering when hurt |\n| Lintwick | Hop, dance | Blob hop and squash (`kick`), a dance loop (squash oscillation + hop + a facing spin) |\n| Lintlings | Hop chase, lunge | squash-hop chase; lunge = squash wind then stretch |\n| Mothlets | Flight | `flap` 1 → swoop |\n| Pinhogs | Roll | curl (`squash .4`, pins shrink inward) → roll (rotating pin angles) → dizzy (stars over the head) |\n| Frayed Knight | Fighting | `stance:'ready'`, `thrust`, `spin` |\n| Knotbrute | Fighting | `haymaker`, `sweep`, a shoulder charge (`lean` forward) |\n| Sir Buttonsworth | Boss moves | `haymaker` (slam), `throw` (volley), a charge with `lean`, a `down` stagger |\n| Gnarlgrim | Boss moves | `haymaker` slam, `throw` toss, charge, `down:.6` (Tangled), `expr:'shout'` roar, unravel death |\n| Objects | Motion | door swing (tweened rotation of the door leaf), banner flutter (a sine wave across the cloth, 3 px), portal swirl (rotating thread arcs), ballista crank and bolt recoil, plant sway, bed blanket |\n| Camera | Cutscenes | eased pans and zooms (tweens), a 90° turn crossfade |\n\nCheck every attack and the new moves with `filmstrip.mjs` (wind-up, strike, settle; no backward sweeps). Enemies' wind-ups are longer than the hero's (.3–.6 s).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Build order and milestones\nEach milestone ends with: `node tests/run.mjs` green, `node tools/build.mjs` producing a playable HTML, and a short note in `DEVLOG.md` in the dev folder. Build the **core loop end to end early** (MS1–MS6 make Act 1 playable), then widen. Milestones are numbered MS0–MS12; quests keep their own IDs, M1–M14 and S1–S3.\n\n| # | Milestone | Deliverables | Acceptance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **MS0** | Setup | Folder layout, engine copy, `vendor/aihub`, `build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the loader (vm context with `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` stand-ins, as `engine/kits/test.mjs` does), an empty `DQ` booting to a placeholder title | Build works from `file://`; the test runner prints `N passed, 0 failed`; `check.mjs` reports no errors |\n| **MS1** | **Voxel core** (riskiest; §10) | `VoxelWorld`, `VoxelRenderer` (atlas, runs, AO, cutaway, x-ray, water, void), `VoxelBody`, picking, break/place in a dev \"sandbox\" scene (a 32×32 diorama stamp), 4 rotations, zoom steps, depth hooks | Unit tests: collision, ground, ceiling, stairs, raycast, pick, diff, hash. Diorama screenshots in 4 rotations × 2 zooms show no sorting errors. Sorting filmstrip; manual play feels solid. Fallbacks in §10 decided by the end of MS1 |\n| **MS2** | Builder and controls | Movement, auto-hop, sprint, jump, combo, Spin Stitch, break tiers, place, cursor modes (auto, mouse, Builder's Eye), hotbar, glyph icons and prompts by device, camera controls | Input-driven tests per action (taps and holds); prompt label tests for keyboard, mouse, PlayStation and Xbox |\n| **MS3** | Items, crafting, objects | Data tables §7.2–7.5, bag and hotbar, drops and pickups, chests, Pocket and Bench crafting UI, notions, doors, lights, beds, plants and regrowth, `E.SHAPES` for all objects | Craft-chain tests; UI navigation tests (MENU actions, mouse hover/click via `input.feed`); object sheets via `asset-sheet.mjs` |\n| **MS4** | World | `generateWorld` with every region, stamps and POI from §7.1, portals, day/night and lighting, weather | Determinism hash test; every POI reachable by nav from the banner (portals allowed); region screenshots |\n| **MS5** | Rooms and town | Room detection and classes, Banner planting, border, Cheer, levels, bubbles, Patterns (ghosts, progress, placement UI) | Room test matrix (§11.2); level-up and border-growth tests; Pattern completion test |\n| **MS6** | Residents and story (Act 1–2) | Nav/A\\*, resident schedule, needs, jobs and helpers; `E.Story` dialog with portraits; quest director; quests M1–M7 and S1; cutscenes with skip; Journal; objective marker | Playthrough test up to Lv3; residents sleep and eat; quests turn in |\n| **MS7** | Combat, monsters, bosses (Act 3–4) | All monsters, spawning, combat feel, KO and Lost Bundle, traps, ballistas, Sir Buttonsworth, siege director, Gnarlgrim; quests M8–M14, S2 and S3; the finale | Damage-formula tests, siege and boss state tests, filmstrips of every attack; playthrough to Chapter Clear |\n| **MS8** | Audio | Every song and jingle, sfx, Animalese synth with `onLetter`, Voices bus and setting, the music director with layers | Headless: every song id resolves, no audio errors. Browser: a listening pass (record notes), plus a `dev/voices.html` test page cycling through speakers |\n| **MS9** | UI polish | Title diorama and logo, New Game, intro, HUD final, Satchel (Bag, Map, Journal), Banner screen, results, credits, About, settings additions, touch-only notice | Screenshot review at 1920×1080 (legibility, 10 ft); keyboard-only, mouse-only and pad-only walkthroughs |\n| **MS10** | Save, dev mode, attract | `game.saves` integration, autosave, Continue; Dev Tools (all tabs, sliders with reset, stamp export, beats); Attract (9 vignettes, any input exits) | Save round-trip test (hash and state equal); slider live-effect and reset tests; attract runs 3 loops headless with no errors, and a keypress exits within 1 step |\n| **MS11** | Multiplayer | `DQ.Net` (codec, host, client, prediction), the Bee world and rules, `hubcard`, server mode, loopback, solo Bee from the title | Net loopback tests (§11.3); `--browser` harness passes all 4 scenarios |\n| **MS12** | Finish | Balance pass with dev sliders; full playthrough under 3 min headless; final screenshots; `exit-interview.json`; About filled from it; final build | §12 checklist all ticked |\n\nParallel work (for teams): after MS1's API is frozen (end of MS1), MS3 (data and crafting), MS4 (worldgen) and MS8 (audio) can proceed alongside MS2. MS11 can start with the loopback once the Builder and VoxelWorld APIs exist.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Risks and de-risking\n\n| Risk | Why | De-risk (do early) | Fallback |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Voxel rendering in a 2D engine** (sorting, overhangs, cutaway) | The engine sorts single points; overhangs can draw actors over roofs | MS1 first, against the diorama with every hard case (§11.2): lift and sink in `_liftOrder`, runs as occluders, x-ray, cutaway. Use filmstrips in 4 rotations | (a) Draw each block as its own queue item instead of runs; (b) if overhang sorting still glitches, always cut away blocks above `heroLevel+2` within the radius, and let NPCs under roofs be hidden by the roof (sink rule only); (c) as a last resort, limit placement so blocks need support below or a neighbour (no floating roofs). Decide by the end of MS1 and record it in DEVLOG |\n| **Render cost / hitches** | Thousands of blits; atlas rebuild on zoom | Face-sprite atlas (no per-run baking), zoom steps, visible-column culling. Perf readout in Debug | Fewer variants, top-only far columns, lower `H` |\n| **Body collision in voxels** (stuck, jitter, ceilings) | A new system with heights | Unit tests for every edge case: corners, 1-high step, 2-high gap, stairs, water, void; the `escape()` routine; no placement inside bodies | Make bodies smaller (r 4); disable auto-hop |\n| **Room detection** correctness | Many shapes; false positives and negatives frustrate players | A test matrix with 20+ layouts, a leak-hint HUD and a dev overlay | Relax the rule (count 1-high door-adjacent gaps as leaks only) |\n| **NPC navigation** in an editable world | Changing graph; residents stuck | Incremental invalidation, A\\* caps, the stuck rule (off-screen teleport), a dev path overlay | Residents hop over 1-block obstacles and teleport within the border when stuck for more than 8 s even on screen (a poof effect) |\n| **Shared-world netcode** | Latency, loss, message caps, host or server modes | Keep the Bee world small; voxel edits are reliable and idempotent; snapshots are unreliable with timestamps; a loopback suite with simulated latency, jitter and loss; run the harness early (a skeleton round in MS6) | Reduce the Bee round to the build phase plus a single raid wave; lower snapshot rates to 6 Hz |\n| **Scope** (17 quests, 8 monsters, 2 bosses) | A large content load | Data-driven tables; finish one vertical path (Act 1) before widening; the scripted playthrough guards regressions | Cut the side quests' extra steps (keep S1–S3 short); keep S3 even if minimal |\n| **Animalese quality / annoyance** | Synth voices can grate | Prototype the test page on the first day of MS8; soft envelopes, low volume (.18), a Voices volume setting, text speed | A one-blip-per-two-letters mode |\n| **10-foot legibility** | Pixel font at 240p | Text at scale 1 or more; a 1080p screenshot review in MS9 | Use `res: 'snes'` (taller pixels) for menus only, through the scene `res` |\n| **Headless testability of UI** | Menus are visual | UI logic as state machines; `game.debug` exposes the UI state; tests drive inputs | — |\n| **Determinism** | Attract, tests, replays | Seeded streams only; `game.stateHash` for replays | — |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Testing plan\n\nRules (from TASK.md):\n- One command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints **only failures and a one-line count**. Rerun it only after changing the code it covers; use `--only` with suite names.\n- Use the engine's `game.advance(seconds)` and `game.debug` for scripted play. Use screenshots only for what a script cannot check.\n- Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n### 11.1 Harness\n- `tests/lib/load.mjs` creates a vm context with stand-ins (`window = ctx`, `addEventListener(){}`, `location: {hash, search:''}`, `matchMedia: () => ({matches:false})`). It runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then each `src/*.js` in build order, and returns `{ E, game, DQ }`. Each suite gets a fresh context.\n- Helpers:\n  - `press(action, s)` (tap, then advance)\n  - `hold(action, s)`\n  - `run(s)` (advance)\n  - `snap()` (`game.debug.snapshot()`)\n  - `expect(cond, msg, detail)`\n  - `atBeat(id)` (dev beat)\n- `tests/run.mjs` imports every `*.test.mjs` it finds, collects `{name, ok, detail}`, prints failures only, and prints the final count. Exit 1 on any failure. `--only a,b` filters by file prefix. `--browser` adds `tests/browser/*`.\n\n### 11.2 Headless suites (what each checks)\n| Suite | Checks |\n|---|---|\n| `voxel.test` | get/set bounds; `topZ` upkeep; `standLevels`; `groundAt` on edges and stairs; `ceilingAt`; `collide` (corner, step, 2-high gap passes, 1-high gap blocks); water depth rules; void respawn; raycast and `pickScreen` in all 4 rotations and 2 views (pick a known block from its projected centre); `diff`/`applyDiff` round trip; hash stability |\n| `render-logic.test` | Run splitting; visible-column culling contains the camera's cell; `_liftOrder` lift and sink cases (a hero on a block sorts after it; a hero under a roof sorts before the roof run; a body under a bridge sorts before the bridge); cutaway trigger cases |\n| `builder.test` | Walk speed matches tuning; jump clears 1 block, not 2; auto-hop; Builder's Eye cursor moves and levels; break tiers (clink vs break), crack stages, drops; place validity (reach, occupied, inside a body); combo timing; Spin Stitch charge; KO → respawn and Lost Bundle content (50%) |\n| `input.test` | Prompt labels per device (keyboard, mouse, PlayStation, Xbox); the glyph setting switches; the Create+Options hub rule; wheel steps cycle the hotbar |\n| `items.test` | Stacks, overflow, hotbar refs, chest store-all, Town Chest designation |\n| `crafting.test` | Every recipe: inputs consumed, output added; station gating; notion triggers fire once; the quantity picker |\n| `objects.test` | Doors open for builders and residents and stay shut for monsters; beds sleep only at night and safely; trap damage; ballista auto and manned fire, reload, repair; portal discovery and travel; plant regrowth after a day |\n| `rooms.test` | Matrix: 2×1 snug; 3×3 bedroom; a 1-high wall leak; a corner gap leak; a missing door; a missing light; 65 cells too big; a roofed room; a door on a corner (invalid, since doors must be in straight walls); stairs inside; two rooms sharing a wall; a room outside the border (detected, no Cheer); a type change (bedroom → snug when the bed is removed); every room type in §7.6; the Hall Pattern recognised; awards counted once per slot and capped by maxAwards |\n| `town.test` | Planting creates the border; Cheer thresholds → levels; border growth; arrivals at dawn; bubbles spawn once per need per day and collect; Pattern placement validity and rotation; ghost counting; helper placement from the Town Chest; \"need\" balloon |\n| `nav.test` | Paths over steps and stairs and through doors (residents) but not doors (monsters); a breaker path through a wall; re-path after an edit; the stuck rule |\n| `npc.test` | Schedule transitions; sleep in an assigned bed; supper at the Mess Hall; Marigold cooks from the chest; Wren's and Lintwick's gifts; requests show \"!\" and \"?\" |\n| `monsters.test` | Spawn rules (not in the border, not near the builder, night tables); aggro, leash and despawn; each attack's wind-up precedes damage; the damage formula with def/tuning/difficulty; drop tables |\n| `siege.test` | Prep → W1–W3 → boss sequencing; monsters target the Banner and break walls; the fail and retry checkpoint; wave sizes scale with tuning |\n| `bosses.test` | Buttonsworth patterns and summon at 50%; Gnarlgrim def 25 → ~1 damage; 2 ballista hits in 8 s → Tangled; charge-hit → Tangled; Seam Ripper ×4 on the Heart Knot; phase transitions at 66% and 33%; the defeat cutscene's `apply()` state |\n| `time.test` | The day length tunable; ambient by hour; sleep skips to 06:00; Belly drain and starving |\n| `quests.test` | Each quest's steps complete from its conditions; rewards granted once; `applyBeat` for every beat yields a consistent snapshot (no errors; flags, residents, rooms present) |\n| `save.test` | Mid-game save → load in a fresh context: `world.hash`, bag, quests, town, residents, clock all equal; the autosave triggers |\n| `dev.test` | Every slider changes behaviour live (walk speed, monster HP, day length...); Reset restores the defaults; cheats toggle; warp lands on standable cells; spawn works; stamp export → import round trip |\n| `attract.test` | Start after 10.0 s idle on the title (not 9.9 s); 3 full loops (about 7 minutes simulated) with no errors and each vignette reaching its end condition; any input (key, mouse move, pad button) returns to the title within 1 step; the player's save is untouched |\n| `touch.test` | With `matchMedia` coarse-only stubs and no keys: the title shows the notice, no touch buttons, attract still runs |\n| `ui.test` | Satchel tabs, Bag actions, crafting navigation by MENU actions and by `input.feed` mouse hover and click; the name entry; settings additions persist |\n| `about.test` | The About pages contain every Source Information field and the three feedback lists from the embedded data |\n| **`playthrough.test`** | **Full scripted run, New Game → Chapter Clear → credits → free play.** `DQ.Autopilot` uses real systems: walk with nav, break and place through Builder actions, craft through Crafting, talk through Story choices, fight with combos. Cheats allowed: god mode, teleports to POIs (instead of long walks), extra materials for the Hall, time skips, and a boosted helper rate. **Every quest must complete through its own triggers.** It asserts at each beat: quest states, town level, residents present, room types formed, Notions known, Golden Needle and Seam Ripper obtained, gate cut, siege waves cleared, boss defeated, results scene, credits, back to play. Error count 0 throughout. Target under 3 minutes wall time (big `advance` chunks during travel, 1/120 steps during combat via `game.advance`) |\n| `bee.test` | Solo Bee from the title: the Pattern scales with players; the build and raid phases; scoring rules; win and lose |\n| `net.test` (loopback) | 2 and 4 game instances in separate vm contexts with a **fake AIHub** (connect, ready, card events, start, `time()`, send/on, leave, time-up, end, `rng`, server flag) over an in-process bus with seeded latency 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss on unreliable messages. Checks:<br>(1) `connect`/`ready` with no key press; the card answers Ready on Enter and More on Triangle.<br>(2) Bot builders place and break; after quiescence every copy's `world.hash()` is equal.<br>(3) Monsters move on clients from snapshots.<br>(4) Message rate ≤ 20/s per copy (bursts ≤ 40); every payload ≤ 16 KB; unreliable ≤ 1,200 bytes.<br>(5) A player leaving removes their builder.<br>(6) Time-up → the host `finish()` within grace, once, with valid standings (every id once).<br>(7) Server mode (a host with no player) runs the round and finishes.<br>(8) `end` stops input and sound.<br>(9) `AIHub.active` false → the normal title |\n\n### 11.3 Browser suites (`--browser`; Playwright, pinned in `engine/package.json`)\n- **`hub-check.mjs`**\n  - **Setup:** `tools/hub-serve.mjs` serves a temp copy folder holding the built HTML plus `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` on `127.0.0.1:<OS port>`. It confirms the game page title.\n  - **Runs** (open `harness.html?game=<file>&...`):\n    - `&players=2&auto=1`\n    - `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n    - the same as above with `&scenario=host-leave`\n    - `&players=2&scenario=server`\n  - **Pass:** wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. On failure, print the harness checklist's failing items.\n  - **Standalone:** open the game alone (outside a session) and require that it reaches the title.\n  - **Teardown:** kill only the server PID it started.\n- **`shots.mjs`** writes screenshots to `check-output/` at 1920×1080 (and 1280×720) for human review:\n  - title, New Game, intro\n  - Hollow dark/lit, Glen day, Thimbleton at Lv1/Lv3/Lv4 (dev beats), Crags, Quarry boss, Tweedwood, Coast, Fraying, Spire top\n  - night town, siege, Gnarlgrim Tangled\n  - Bag, Crafting, Map, Journal, Banner screen, Dev Tools, About\n  - Bee card, touch-only notice\n  - 4 camera rotations, three-quarter view\n  - the block atlas sheet\n- Also run `node engine/tools/check.mjs <html>#play` (fails on errors; acts on look notes) and `filmstrip.mjs` for every attack and new move.\n\n### 11.4 Manual passes (short, recorded in DEVLOG)\n- **Controller only** (DualSense, or the standard mapping): the whole of Act 1, menus, dev sliders.\n- **Keyboard only.** Mouse plus keyboard. The prompts switch instantly with the last input.\n- **Glyph setting:** Xbox.\n- **TV distance:** all text readable from 3 m on a 1080p screen, or approximate it by viewing a 1080p screenshot at 33% scale.\n- **Feel:** jump arc, swing hit-stop, break and place rhythm (one block per ~0.4 s feels snappy), camera turn.\n\n### 11.5 Asset checks\n- `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs src/03-data-objects.js#bench` (each object) shows every view and facing next to the hero. Fix the lint notes.\n- An atlas dump writes every block material and face to `check-output/atlas.png`.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Definition of done (check every line before handing off)\n- [ ] `./DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174740.html` is one file, works from `file://`, has no external requests, and its title shows **Dragon Quilt Builders**.\n- [ ] Everything in §6 and §7 is implemented; there are **no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features** (`grep -rn \"TODO\\|FIXME\\|placeholder\" src/` is empty).\n- [ ] Chapter One is playable start to finish (M1–M14), S1–S3 work, and free play continues after the credits.\n- [ ] All systems are present:\n  - voxel building with rotation and cutaway; tools and tiers; crafting and Notions; rooms; Banner, levels and Patterns with helpers\n  - residents with schedules, needs, jobs and requests; Cheer bubbles; day/night; Belly\n  - combat with 6 monster types plus 2 bosses; the siege; ballistas and traps; portals; Map and Journal; saves\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: cheats, warp, spawn, story beats, debug overlays, **live sliders with Reset to defaults**, stamp export.\n- [ ] Attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title or menus, loops, cheats freely, and any input exits.\n- [ ] AI Hub: tags, unmodified `session.js` first in `<head>`, shared-world Bee round, own card, ready without a key press, standings and finish, leave, time-up, end, server mode. **The harness passes all 4 scenarios.** Outside a session the game is unaffected.\n- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI. PlayStation glyphs by default with a Settings option for Xbox. Keyboard and mouse are native (WASD, Space, Shift, mouse targeting, wheel hotbar, Q/E camera, F talk, Tab bag). Prompts follow the last input device. Mouse hover moves the focus in every menu.\n- [ ] Touch-only devices: no touch controls, the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice, the settings button, and the attract mode runs.\n- [ ] Audio is all code: original music with the leitmotif, sfx, Animalese voices per character, and a Voices volume setting.\n- [ ] Tone is Dragon Quest-like throughout (punny, warm, earnest, silent hero). No names, characters, art, music, places or iconic lines from the source.\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` and `node tests/run.mjs --browser` pass (only failures are printed, then one count line).\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json` exists beside the HTML, parses as JSON, and has exactly the TASK.md shape with every value filled (\"unknown\" where unconfirmed; `plan`: \"PLAN.md\").\n- [ ] The About/Credits screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (from the same data as the exit interview), the engine changes and licences.\n- [ ] The final chat reply includes Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n","numLines":236,"startLine":1378,"totalLines":1613}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012LK4LbYkSDhUZtKR43NUM2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
